        "373": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $0175: DISK_IDENTIFY.","comment":"DISK_IDENTIFY: the format of the disk in unit C"},
        "376": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $0178: FORMAT_SELECT.","comment":"FORMAT_SELECT"},
        "379": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $017B: UNIT1_PRESENT.","comment":"UNIT1_PRESENT"},
        "382": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $017E: DRIVE_STATUS.","comment":"DRIVE_STATUS"},
        "385": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $0181: DRIVE_KIND_GET.","comment":"DRIVE_KIND_GET"},
        "388": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $0184: SECTOR_HOOK_SET.","comment":"SECTOR_HOOK_SET"},
        "391": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $0187: FORMAT_FROM_SPEC.","comment":"FORMAT_FROM_SPEC"},
        "394": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $018A: PARAMS_FROM_SPEC.","comment":"PARAMS_FROM_SPEC"},
        "397": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $018D: SEEK_TRACK.","comment":"SEEK_TRACK"},
        "400": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $0190: L3EF5, which runs a command block with a read execution phase\n(CMD_SEND_HEAD, EXEC_READ, then the results at $20EF).","comment":"L3EF5: a command block with a read phase"},
        "403": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $0193: CMD_WRITE.","comment":"CMD_WRITE: a command block with a write phase"},
        "406": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $0196: MOTOR_ON.","comment":"MOTOR_ON"},
        "409": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $0199: MOTOR_TIMER_SET.","comment":"MOTOR_TIMER_SET"},
        "412": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $019C: L3EE6, which turns the disk motor off at once (the count at $E600\ncleared, bit 3 of $5B67 cleared through PORT_1FFD_SET).","comment":"L3EE6: the motor off at once"},
        "415": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $019F: L39BD, which returns A = $3A with carry clear.","comment":"L39BD: A = $3A, carry clear"},
        "418": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $01A2: L24C8.","comment":"L24C8"},
        "421": {"synopsis":"DOS_JUMPS entry $01A5: L29D3.","comment":"L29D3"},
        "424": {"synopsis":"Sets this ROM's state up from nothing (DOS_JUMPS $0100), keeping the byte at $DF9D:\n1. $DB00-$E4FF, the work area in RAM bank 7 (which must be paged in at $C000), is cleared.\n2. When a disk controller answers (FDC_PRESENT), it is set up (DISK_INIT) with the tables of\ndrives A and B (DRIVES_AB_INIT).\n3. With a controller or without, the RAM disk (drive M, DRIVE_M_INIT) takes blocks $08-$7F\nand the cache (CACHE_BUILD) blocks 0-7 (SETUP_DEFAULTS). A block is 512 bytes of RAM\nbanks 1, 3, 4 and 6 (BLOCK_ADDRESS).\n4. The default drive becomes the first letter that has a drive (FIRST_DRIVE).\n5. $DF9D gets its old value back and the work goes on at HD_STARTUP ($2831), the target of\n$00A6 in JUMPS_00A0.","comment":"$DF9D kept over the clearing"},
        "428": {"synopsis":"Step 1 of SETUP_ALL, $DF9D on the stack: the work area cleared, then the disk controller\nand drives A and B set up when there is a controller.","comment":"Bank 7's work area, $DB00-$E4FF"},
        "434": {"comment":"2,560 bytes"},
        "437": {"comment":"First byte 0, LDIR spreads it"},
        "441": {"comment":"Disk controller present?"},
        "444": {"comment":"No controller: keep these"},
        "446": {"comment":"Yes: the controller set up"},
        "449": {"comment":"Tables of drives A and B"},
        "452": {"comment":"RAM disk blocks $08-$7F","synopsis":"The layout, the same with a controller or without: the RAM disk in blocks $08-$7F, the cache\nin blocks 0-7."},
        "455": {"comment":"Cache blocks 0-7"},
        "458": {"synopsis":"The RAM disk from HL (H = first block, L = number of blocks), the cache from DE (D = first\nblock, E = number), the default drive (FIRST_DRIVE), then $DF9D back and on to HD_STARTUP\n($2831, SETUP_ALL).","comment":"Cache layout kept"},
        "459": {"comment":"RAM disk (drive M) from HL"},
        "462": {"comment":"DE = the cache layout"},
        "463": {"comment":"Cache from DE"},
        "466": {"comment":"Default drive (FIRST_DRIVE)"},
        "469": {"comment":"$DF9D back"},
        "473": {"comment":"On at HD_STARTUP"},
        "476": {"synopsis":"Returns fixed values (DOS_JUMPS $0103); nothing is read.\nExit: A = 0, BC = 0, DE = $0101, HL = $0069, carry set, NZ (from the SUB).","comment":"A = $FF: NZ"},
        "480": {"comment":"A = 0, BC = 0"},
        "484": {"comment":"DE = $0101"},
        "487": {"comment":"HL = $0069"},
        "490": {"comment":"Success"},
        "492": {"synopsis":"Gives the layout of the RAM disk and the cache (DOS_JUMPS $013C).\nExit: H = the RAM disk's first block and L its number of blocks (from $E3F4 and its end at\n$E3F1); D = the cache's first block and E its number of blocks ($E291, $E290). Carry is not\nset here.","comment":"H = first RAM disk block, L = their count"},
        "495": {"comment":"D, E = the cache's first block and count"},
        "498": {"synopsis":"Sets the layout of the cache and the RAM disk (DOS_JUMPS $013F). When the RAM disk's layout\ndiffers from the current one, drive M is made again (RAMDISK_RESET: error $24 while files\nare open on it; its blocks are filled with $E5; fewer than 4 blocks give no RAM disk). When\nthe cache's differs, the cache is written out (CACHE_FLUSH_ALL) and set up again\n(CACHE_BUILD).\nEntry: D = the cache's first block, E = its number of blocks; H = the RAM disk's first\nblock, L = its number of blocks.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"Cache layout kept"},
        "499": {"comment":"DE = the new RAM disk layout"},
        "500": {"comment":"HL = the current one"},
        "503": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "506": {"comment":"HL = the new layout"},
        "507": {"comment":"Differs: RAM disk made again"},
        "511": {"comment":"DE = the new cache layout"},
        "512": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "513": {"comment":"HL = the new cache layout"},
        "514": {"comment":"DE = the current one"},
        "517": {"comment":"DE = the new layout, HL the current"},
        "518": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "522": {"comment":"Differs: cache written out and set up"},
        "527": {"synopsis":"Copies BC bytes from HL to DE with RAM bank A paged in at $C000, then pages back the bank\nthat was there. Nothing happens when BC is 0.\nEntry: A = the bank, HL, DE, BC.\nExit: HL and DE past the bytes, BC = 0.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"C = 0?"},
        "529": {"comment":"No: copy"},
        "531": {"comment":"B = 0 too?"},
        "533": {"comment":"Yes: nothing to copy"},
        "534": {"synopsis":"Bank A in, the copy, and the old bank back through SWAP_BANK, into which this falls.","comment":"Bank A in, A = the old one"},
        "537": {"comment":"The copy"},
        "539": {"synopsis":"Pages RAM bank A (0-7) in at $C000 through port $7FFD and its copy at $5B5C, with interrupts\noff while the two are written and on again only if they were on. Calling it again with the A\nit returned puts the old bank back.\nEntry: A = the bank.\nExit: A = the bank that was in before.\nChanges: F.","comment":"HL and BC kept"},
        "541": {"comment":"B = the bank wanted"},
        "542": {"comment":"The paging byte"},
        "545": {"comment":"A = the bank in now"},
        "546": {"comment":"Bits 0-2: the bank"},
        "548": {"comment":"Kept as the result"},
        "559": {"synopsis":"A = the bank that was in; registers back.","comment":"A = the old bank"},
        "563": {"synopsis":"Finds a 512-byte block of the RAM disk and cache area: blocks 0-31 are in RAM bank 1, 32-63\nin bank 3, 64-95 in bank 4 and 96-127 in bank 6, each at $C000 + 512 x (block AND 31).\nEntry: A = the block (0-127).\nExit: A = the bank, HL = the block's address; carry set for banks 1 and 3, clear for 4 and\n6.","comment":"L = twice the block"},
        "565": {"comment":"H = $C0 + 2 x (block AND 31)"},
        "568": {"comment":"Bits 5-6 of the block"},
        "569": {"comment":"L = 0: a 512-byte boundary"},
        "571": {"comment":"Bits 5-6 to bits 1-2"},
        "574": {"comment":"A = 0, 2, 4 or 6"},
        "576": {"comment":"Bank 4 or 6?"},
        "578": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "579": {"comment":"Banks 1 and 3, carry"},
        "581": {"synopsis":"Copies IX bytes from HL in RAM bank C to DE in RAM bank B; an address below $C000 is the\nsame memory whatever the bank. With C = B it is one COPY_IN_BANK. Otherwise:\n1. the bytes before the destination reaches $C000 are copied with bank C in; 2. the bytes\n   before the source reaches $C000 with bank B in; 3. the rest, both ends at $C000 or above,\n   goes through $BFE0-$BFFF 32 bytes at a time (COPY_VIA_BOUNCE), with those 32 bytes kept\n   at $DB00 meanwhile and interrupts off (on again if they were).\nEntry: HL = the source, DE = the destination, IX = the count, C = the source bank, B = the\ndestination bank.\nExit: HL and DE past the bytes, IX = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"The same bank?"},
        "585": {"comment":"Yes: BC = the count"},
        "587": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "588": {"comment":"One copy"},
        "591": {"synopsis":"Different banks: the parts below $C000 first, then the rest through $BFE0.","comment":"Banks kept"},
        "592": {"comment":"BC = bytes before DE reaches $C000"},
        "595": {"comment":"Those, bank C in"},
        "598": {"comment":"Banks back"},
        "600": {"comment":"A = the destination bank"},
        "601": {"comment":"Now the source's low part"},
        "602": {"comment":"BC = bytes before HL reaches $C000"},
        "605": {"comment":"HL, DE back as they were"},
        "606": {"comment":"Those, bank B in"},
        "609": {"comment":"Anything left?"},
        "612": {"comment":"Count 0?"},
        "614": {"comment":"Banks back"},
        "615": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "616": {"comment":"P/V = the interrupt state"},
        "618": {"comment":"No interrupt while $BFE0 is borrowed"},
        "619": {"comment":"State kept"},
        "620": {"comment":"No carry: save"},
        "621": {"comment":"$BFE0-$BFFF kept at $DB00"},
        "624": {"comment":"The rest through $BFE0"},
        "627": {"comment":"Carry: restore"},
        "628": {"comment":"$BFE0-$BFFF back"},
        "631": {"comment":"Interrupts were off?"},
        "632": {"comment":"Interrupts were off: leave them"},
        "633": {"comment":"No: on again"},
        "635": {"synopsis":"Copies the 32 bytes at $BFE0 to $DB00 (carry clear) or back from $DB00 to $BFE0 (carry set).\nRegisters kept but F.","comment":"HL, DE, BC kept"},
        "638": {"comment":"32 bytes"},
        "641": {"comment":"From $BFE0 to $DB00"},
        "644": {"comment":"From $BFE0"},
        "647": {"comment":"Carry clear: that way"},
        "649": {"comment":"Carry: the other way"},
        "650": {"synopsis":"The copy.","comment":"The 32 bytes"},
        "656": {"synopsis":"Copies IX bytes from HL in bank C to DE in bank B, both at $C000 or above, through the 32\nbytes at $BFE0: up to 32 at a time from the source to $BFE0 with bank C in, then from $BFE0\nto the destination with bank B in, until IX is 0.\nExit: HL and DE past the bytes, IX = 0.","comment":"HL = the count left, source kept"},
        "659": {"comment":"256 or more left?"},
        "663": {"comment":"Low byte of the count"},
        "664": {"comment":"Fewer than 32?"},
        "666": {"comment":"Yes: all of them"},
        "668": {"synopsis":"32 bytes this time.","comment":"No: 32"},
        "670": {"synopsis":"A piece of A bytes: IX less A, then the two copies.","comment":"Count left less this piece"},
        "671": {"comment":"BC = the piece"},
        "675": {"comment":"Taken off the count"},
        "678": {"comment":"HL = source, the count left kept"},
        "679": {"comment":"IX = the count left"},
        "681": {"comment":"Piece of 0: done"},
        "683": {"comment":"DE, BC, piece kept"},
        "686": {"comment":"C = the piece, A = the source bank"},
        "687": {"comment":"A = the source bank"},
        "691": {"comment":"Into $BFE0"},
        "694": {"comment":"Source bank in"},
        "697": {"comment":"Piece, BC, DE back"},
        "700": {"comment":"HL past the piece kept"},
        "702": {"comment":"C = the piece, A = the destination bank"},
        "703": {"comment":"A = the destination bank"},
        "706": {"comment":"From $BFE0"},
        "709": {"comment":"Destination bank in, DE past it"},
        "714": {"comment":"Next piece"},
        "716": {"synopsis":"Counts the bytes of a copy before the address in DE reaches $C000: BC = $C000 - DE, but no\nmore than IX, and 0 when DE is $C000 or above; IX is reduced by BC.\nEntry: DE = the address, IX = the count.\nExit: BC = the part, IX = the rest. HL kept.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "717": {"comment":"None so far"},
        "720": {"comment":"HL = $C000 - DE"},
        "723": {"comment":"Compare with DE"},
        "726": {"comment":"DE above $C000?"},
        "728": {"comment":"Or at it?"},
        "730": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "733": {"comment":"More than the room below $C000?"},
        "734": {"comment":"Count less the room"},
        "737": {"comment":"No: the whole count"},
        "739": {"comment":"Yes: the room"},
        "741": {"synopsis":"IX less BC.","comment":"IX less the part"},
        "745": {"comment":"IX - BC"},
        "750": {"synopsis":"HL back.","comment":"HL back"},
        "752": {"synopsis":"Sets the routine that is asked about disk errors (DOS_JUMPS $014E); its address is kept at\n$DB20. ASK_RETRY calls it with HL = the message ($FF-ended) and takes the code it returns\nin A: 1 to retry, 0 to cancel, 2 or more to ignore.\nEntry: A = 0 to remove the routine (errors are then not asked about), otherwise HL = the\nroutine.\nExit: HL = the previous routine's address (0 for none), carry clear.","comment":"Remove the routine?"},
        "755": {"comment":"Yes: address 0"},
        "758": {"synopsis":"The address swapped.","comment":"DE = the old one"},
        "762": {"comment":"The new one"},
        "765": {"comment":"HL = the old one"},
        "767": {"synopsis":"Asks what to do about disk error A, through the routine at $DB20 (SET_ERR_HOOK): $DB22 is\nset to DOS_MESSAGES, the error's message is built at $DB29 (BUILD_MESSAGE) and the routine\nis called with HL = the message (CALL_ERR_HOOK). The code it returns in A is the answer.\nCalled from $1AA8.\nEntry: A = the error (0-9), C = the drive letter, D = the track and E = the sector the\nmessage prints.\nExit: A = the error; carry set and Z for code 1 (retry); carry set and NZ for 2 or more\n(ignore); carry clear for code 0 (cancel) or when there is no routine.","comment":"B = the error"},
        "768": {"comment":"A routine set?"},
        "771": {"comment":"Is it 0?"},
        "773": {"comment":"A = the error"},
        "774": {"comment":"Yes: ask it"},
        "776": {"comment":"No: NZ, carry clear (cancel)"},
        "778": {"synopsis":"A routine is set: the message table and the message made, the routine called, its code\nturned into the flags.","comment":"Error kept"},
        "779": {"comment":"The table: DOS_MESSAGES"},
        "785": {"comment":"Message A at $DB29, HL on it"},
        "788": {"comment":"Error kept"},
        "790": {"comment":"The routine; A = its code"},
        "794": {"comment":"1: Z; 0: a borrow"},
        "796": {"comment":"Carry: retry or ignore"},
        "797": {"comment":"A = the error"},
        "799": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the routine at $DB20 with HL kept; its RET goes back to the caller of\nCALL_ERR_HOOK.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "800": {"comment":"The routine's address"},
        "803": {"comment":"On the stack, HL back"},
        "804": {"comment":"Off to it"},
        "805": {"synopsis":"Builds message 10 of DOS_MESSAGES, the request to put in the disk for drive C, at $DB29:\n$DB22 = DOS_MESSAGES, then BUILD_MESSAGE. Called from $192B.\nEntry: C = the drive letter.\nExit: HL = $DB29.","comment":"Message 10"},
        "807": {"comment":"The table: DOS_MESSAGES"},
        "813": {"synopsis":"Builds message A (bit 7 ignored) of the message table at ($DB22), DOS_MESSAGES or\nCOLOUR_MESSAGES, at $DB29 and ends it with $FF.\nEntry: A = the message, $DB22 = the table; C = the drive letter, D and E the numbers for the\ncodes $FE, $FD and $FC.\nExit: HL = $DB29.\nChanges: AF, B, IX.","comment":"IX = where it goes"},
        "817": {"comment":"Kept as the result"},
        "819": {"comment":"The text"},
        "822": {"comment":"Its end"},
        "826": {"comment":"HL = the start"},
        "828": {"synopsis":"Puts message A AND $7F of the table at ($DB22) into the buffer at IX. A byte below $80 is a\ncharacter; $FE puts in the drive letter in C, $FD the number in D and $FC the number in E,\nin decimal; $FB puts in INK control $10 and colour 2 when the border colour in BORDCR is\n4-7,\ncolour 5 when it is 0-3; $FA puts in INK control $10 and BORDCR's bits 0-2; any other byte\nfrom $80 puts in message (byte AND $7F) through MESSAGE_TEXT again.\nEntry: A, IX; C, D, E; $DB22 = the table.\nExit: IX past the text.","comment":"The message number"},
        "830": {"comment":"HL = the table"},
        "833": {"comment":"B = number + 1"},
        "835": {"comment":"Into the count"},
        "837": {"synopsis":"Steps over one message, up to its $FF.","comment":"Up to the $FF"},
        "839": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "842": {"synopsis":"Next message, until B reaches the one wanted.","comment":"Skip another?"},
        "844": {"synopsis":"One byte of the message.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "846": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "849": {"comment":"Pointer kept"},
        "850": {"comment":"It goes in"},
        "854": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "856": {"synopsis":"Puts one byte of a message into the buffer: a character, the drive letter, a number, an ink\ncolour or another message.","comment":"A character?"},
        "860": {"comment":"$FE: the drive letter?"},
        "864": {"comment":"$FD: the number in D?"},
        "868": {"comment":"$FC: the number in E?"},
        "872": {"comment":"$FB: the warning ink?"},
        "876": {"comment":"$FA: the ink back?"},
        "878": {"comment":"No: another message"},
        "880": {"synopsis":"$FA: INK control and the lower screen's ink, BORDCR bits 0-2.","comment":"INK control"},
        "886": {"comment":"BORDCR's bits 0-2"},
        "891": {"comment":"The colour goes in"},
        "893": {"synopsis":"$FB: INK control and a colour that stands out from the border (BORDCR bits 3-5): red (2) on\nborder 4-7, cyan (5) on border 0-3.","comment":"INK control"},
        "899": {"comment":"BORDCR's bits 3-5: the border"},
        "904": {"comment":"Border 4 or above?"},
        "908": {"comment":"No: cyan"},
        "912": {"synopsis":"Red for a border of 4-7.","comment":"Red"},
        "914": {"synopsis":"The colour into the buffer.","comment":"The colour goes in"},
        "916": {"comment":"A = the number in E","synopsis":"A = the number in E."},
        "919": {"synopsis":"A = the number in D.","comment":"A = the number in D"},
        "920": {"synopsis":"A (0-255) into the buffer in decimal, without leading zeros. BC and DE kept.","comment":"DE, BC kept"},
        "922": {"comment":"HL = the number"},
        "923": {"comment":"Number in L, H = 0"},
        "925": {"comment":"D = 0: no digit yet"},
        "926": {"comment":"Hundreds"},
        "932": {"comment":"Tens"},
        "938": {"comment":"Units, always put in"},
        "939": {"comment":"As a digit"},
        "941": {"comment":"BC, DE back"},
        "943": {"comment":"It goes in"},
        "945": {"synopsis":"Counts how many times -BC goes into HL and leaves the rest in HL; the count goes into the\nbuffer as a digit unless it is a leading 0 (D = 0 while no digit has been put in).\nExit: D = $30 once a digit has gone in.","comment":"Count -1"},
        "947": {"synopsis":"One more subtraction.","comment":"Value kept"},
        "948": {"comment":"One more"},
        "949": {"comment":"Take one 100 or 10"},
        "950": {"comment":"Below 0: count done"},
        "952": {"comment":"Keep the new value"},
        "954": {"comment":"Again"},
        "956": {"synopsis":"The count is the digit.","comment":"HL = what was left"},
        "957": {"comment":"Count 0?"},
        "958": {"comment":"Not a digit yet?"},
        "960": {"comment":"No: digits from now on"},
        "962": {"synopsis":"The digit, or nothing for a leading 0.","comment":"A = the digit, or 0 when leading"},
        "963": {"comment":"Leading 0: nothing"},
        "964": {"comment":"Put it in"},
        "966": {"synopsis":"A = the drive letter in C.","comment":"A = the drive letter"},
        "967": {"synopsis":"A goes into the buffer at IX.","comment":"Into the buffer"},
        "970": {"comment":"Next place"},
        "973": {"synopsis":"The disk-error messages ASK_RETRY and MSG_INSERT_DISK use, sixteen of them, each ended by\n$FF and read by MESSAGE_TEXT through $DB22. Inside one, $FE stands for the drive letter, $FD\nfor the track and $FC for the sector, and a byte $80 + n for message n.\nMessages 0-9 are those of errors 0-9: (11) not ready, (12) write protected, (13) seek fail,\n(14) data error, (14) no data, (14) missing address mark, (11) bad format, (14) unknown\nerror, (12) changed, please replace, (12) unsuitable, each followed by (15).\n10 asks for the disk for drive $FE to be put in and a key pressed. 11-15 are pieces:\n11 \"Drive X: \", 12 (11) \"disk \", 13 (11) \"track N, \", 14 (13) \"sector N, \", 15 \" - Retry,\nIgnore or Cancel? \"."},
        "1259": {"synopsis":"Shifts DE right A times (A = 0 leaves it).\nEntry: A = the count, DE.\nExit: DE shifted, A = 0.\nChanges: F.","comment":"No shift?"},
        "1261": {"synopsis":"One place.","comment":"DE halved"},
        "1265": {"comment":"Again?"},
        "1269": {"synopsis":"Shifts DE left A times (A = 0 leaves it).\nEntry: A = the count, DE.\nExit: DE shifted, A = 0. HL kept.\nChanges: F.","comment":"No shift?"},
        "1271": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "1272": {"synopsis":"One place.","comment":"Doubled"},
        "1273": {"comment":"Again?"},
        "1276": {"comment":"DE = the result"},
        "1278": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL: a CALL to here calls the routine at HL. Called from $1336.","comment":"To HL"},
        "1279": {"synopsis":"Turns a lower-case letter in A (a-z) into its capital; any other value stays.\nChanges: F.","comment":"Below a?"},
        "1282": {"comment":"Above z?"},
        "1285": {"comment":"Less $20: the capital"},
        "1288": {"synopsis":"Makes the first letter from A to P that has a drive (DRIVE_FIND_UC) the default drive,\nstored\nat $DF94, $5B79 and $5B7A; with none, all three are 'A'. Called from $01D2.\nExit: carry set, A = C = the letter and IX = its drive table when one was found; otherwise\ncarry clear and A = $41.","comment":"B = 16 letters, C = 'A'"},
        "1291": {"synopsis":"One letter.","comment":"This letter"},
        "1292": {"comment":"A drive for it?"},
        "1295": {"comment":"A = the letter"},
        "1296": {"comment":"Yes: the default"},
        "1298": {"comment":"Next letter"},
        "1299": {"comment":"Next of the 16"},
        "1301": {"comment":"None: 'A'"},
        "1303": {"synopsis":"The default drive: $DF94 and the copies at $5B79 and $5B7A.","comment":"The default drive"},
        "1306": {"comment":"Its copies"},
        "1309": {"comment":"...at $5B79 and $5B7A"},
        "1313": {"synopsis":"Checks that file number B is open with bit 0 (reading) of its mode byte set. Called from\n$1129, $19C7 and $3573.\nEntry: B = the file number.\nExit: BC = its record; carry set when so, carry clear otherwise; A = $1D in either case,\nexcept $15 for a number of 16 or more.","comment":"Open?"},
        "1316": {"comment":"No"},
        "1317": {"comment":"Bit 0 (reading) to carry"},
        "1318": {"comment":"Error $1D if not"},
        "1321": {"synopsis":"Checks that file number B is open with bit 1 (writing) of its mode byte set. Called from\n$1186 and $121A.\nEntry: B = the file number.\nExit: BC = its record; carry set when so, carry clear otherwise; A = $1D in either case,\nexcept $15 for a number of 16 or more.","comment":"Open?"},
        "1324": {"comment":"No"},
        "1325": {"comment":"Bit 1 (writing) to carry"},
        "1327": {"comment":"Error $1D if not"},
        "1330": {"synopsis":"Finds file number B's record and checks that it is open (bit 7 of its mode byte, record +\n$20).\nEntry: B = the file number.\nExit: carry set, BC = the record, A = its mode byte; carry clear and A = $15 for a number of\n16 or more, $1D for one not open.","comment":"BC = the record, A = its mode"},
        "1333": {"comment":"Bad number"},
        "1334": {"comment":"Bit 7 to carry, A kept"},
        "1336": {"comment":"Open"},
        "1337": {"comment":"Not open: error $1D"},
        "1340": {"synopsis":"Finds file number B's record, checks that it is not open and clears it.\nEntry: B = the file number.\nExit: carry set and BC = the record, all 0; carry clear and A = $15 for a number of 16 or\nmore, $1D for one already open.","comment":"BC = the record, A = its mode"},
        "1343": {"comment":"Bad number"},
        "1344": {"comment":"Bit 7: open"},
        "1345": {"comment":"Carry when not"},
        "1346": {"comment":"Open: error $1D"},
        "1348": {"comment":"Error"},
        "1349": {"comment":"Registers kept"},
        "1352": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "1354": {"comment":"First byte 0"},
        "1356": {"comment":"DE = the next"},
        "1359": {"comment":"56 more bytes, one past the record"},
        "1364": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "1368": {"synopsis":"Finds the record of file number B. Each record is $38 bytes, from $DBA0, one for each number\n0-15; the scans over all of them (ACCESS_CONFLICT, FLUSH_DRV_FILES, FLUSH_SECTOR_BUF) take\n18, the two more at $DF20 and $DF58 being the records ERASE_BAK and the routines from $092E\nuse for names of their own. In a record: bytes 0-31 the directory entry (byte 0 $22 for a\nwhole drive), +$20 the mode byte (bit 0 reading, bit 1 writing, bits 2-3 the access other\nrecords may have, bit 7 open), +$21 the drive letter, +$22 flags, +$23-$25 the length,\n+$26-$28 the file pointer, +$2D-$2F the buffer's address and bank, +$30-$37 the 8 header\nbytes.\nEntry: B = the file number.\nExit: carry set, BC = the record, A = its mode byte; carry clear and A = $15 for B of 16 or\nmore. HL, DE kept.","comment":"HL, DE kept"},
        "1370": {"comment":"Number 16 or more?"},
        "1373": {"comment":"Error $15 if so"},
        "1377": {"comment":"One record before the first"},
        "1380": {"comment":"$38 bytes each"},
        "1383": {"comment":"B + 1 steps"},
        "1384": {"synopsis":"One record on.","comment":"One record on"},
        "1387": {"comment":"BC = the record"},
        "1389": {"comment":"Its mode byte"},
        "1392": {"comment":"The mode byte's address"},
        "1394": {"comment":"Success"},
        "1395": {"synopsis":"Registers back.","comment":"Registers back"},
        "1398": {"synopsis":"ACCESS_CONFLICT for the record at BC with its own mode byte held at 0 meanwhile, so that it\ndoes not clash with itself. Called from $0938, $099F and $09B2.\nEntry: BC = the record.\nExit: as ACCESS_CONFLICT.","comment":"HL = its mode byte"},
        "1402": {"comment":"Kept in E"},
        "1403": {"comment":"0 meanwhile"},
        "1407": {"comment":"The check"},
        "1412": {"comment":"Mode byte back"},
        "1414": {"synopsis":"Checks the record at BC against the open records of the 18 from $DBA0. Another open record\non the same drive (+$21) clashes when either is a whole-drive record (first byte $22) or the\ntwo have the same name (MATCH_EXACT_USER: byte 0 and the 11 name bytes, with ? in this\nrecord's name\nmatching anything), and its access bits (0-1 of its mode byte) include one that this\nrecord's bits 2-3 do not allow.\nEntry: BC = the record.\nExit: carry set when nothing clashes; carry clear and A = $1E otherwise.","comment":"The first record"},
        "1417": {"comment":"18 records"},
        "1419": {"synopsis":"One record.","comment":"Record and count kept"},
        "1421": {"comment":"HL = its mode byte"},
        "1425": {"comment":"D = its mode"},
        "1427": {"comment":"A = its drive"},
        "1430": {"comment":"Open?"},
        "1432": {"comment":"No: next"},
        "1434": {"comment":"The same drive as ours?"},
        "1435": {"comment":"Our drive's address"},
        "1441": {"comment":"No: next"},
        "1443": {"comment":"Ours a whole drive?"},
        "1444": {"comment":"$22: whole drive?"},
        "1446": {"comment":"Yes: check the access"},
        "1448": {"comment":"Its a whole drive?"},
        "1449": {"comment":"$22: whole drive?"},
        "1451": {"comment":"If not: the same name?"},
        "1454": {"comment":"No: next"},
        "1456": {"synopsis":"The other record's access against what this one lets others do.","comment":"Record kept"},
        "1457": {"comment":"Our mode byte"},
        "1462": {"comment":"Bits 2-3: what we let others do"},
        "1466": {"comment":"H = them"},
        "1467": {"comment":"Its bits 0-1: its access"},
        "1470": {"comment":"Any access we do not allow?"},
        "1472": {"comment":"Error $1E if so"},
        "1475": {"comment":"Clash"},
        "1476": {"synopsis":"Next record.","comment":"$38 bytes on"},
        "1482": {"comment":"Another?"},
        "1483": {"comment":"Another?"},
        "1485": {"comment":"No clash"},
        "1487": {"synopsis":"Writes back every open file on drive A (DOS_JUMPS $0142). The letter is made a capital and\nthe drive checked (DRIVE_LOGIN, which also scans its directory if that is not yet done);\nthen\nWRITE_BACK runs for each open record of the 18 whose drive is the drive's letter (IX+$1C).\nEntry: A = the drive letter.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error. BC kept.","comment":"A capital"},
        "1490": {"comment":"IX = the drive"},
        "1493": {"comment":"No such drive"},
        "1494": {"synopsis":"The same for the drive at IX; reached from $0A39.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "1495": {"comment":"The first record"},
        "1498": {"comment":"18 records"},
        "1500": {"synopsis":"One record.","comment":"Its mode byte"},
        "1504": {"comment":"Open?"},
        "1506": {"comment":"No: next"},
        "1508": {"comment":"Its drive"},
        "1510": {"comment":"This drive?"},
        "1513": {"comment":"Carry for the other case"},
        "1515": {"comment":"Yes: written back"},
        "1519": {"comment":"Error"},
        "1521": {"synopsis":"Next record.","comment":"$38 bytes on"},
        "1525": {"comment":"BC = the next record"},
        "1527": {"comment":"Another?"},
        "1530": {"comment":"All done"},
        "1531": {"synopsis":"BC back.","comment":"BC back"},
        "1533": {"synopsis":"Writes back the buffer of every open file on drive D that is marked in use (bit 3 of record\n+ $22) for the word HL (record + $2B): the record's drive is checked (FCB_DRIVE_LOGIN) and\nREC_RELEASE\nwrites the buffer out if it was changed. Called from $1557 with D and HL taken from a cache\nentry.\nEntry: D = the drive letter, HL = the word.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The first record"},
        "1536": {"comment":"18 records"},
        "1538": {"synopsis":"One record.","comment":"HL and the count kept"},
        "1540": {"comment":"A = the drive letter"},
        "1541": {"comment":"DE = the word wanted"},
        "1542": {"comment":"Its mode byte"},
        "1546": {"comment":"This drive?"},
        "1547": {"comment":"Not this drive"},
        "1549": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "1550": {"comment":"Buffer in use?"},
        "1552": {"comment":"Buffer not in use"},
        "1554": {"comment":"Its word at +$2B"},
        "1558": {"comment":"Low byte the same?"},
        "1563": {"comment":"High byte?"},
        "1567": {"comment":"The record's drive checked"},
        "1570": {"comment":"Buffer written back"},
        "1573": {"comment":"Error"},
        "1575": {"synopsis":"Next record.","comment":"$38 bytes on"},
        "1579": {"comment":"BC = the next record"},
        "1581": {"comment":"No error"},
        "1582": {"synopsis":"Count and HL back; stop on an error.","comment":"Count and HL back"},
        "1584": {"comment":"Error"},
        "1585": {"comment":"Another?"},
        "1586": {"comment":"Another?"},
        "1589": {"synopsis":"Opens or creates the file named at HL as file number B (DOS_JUMPS $0106).\n1. The record of B must not be open (FILE_FREE_REC); it is cleared, the name goes into it\n   (PARSE_NAME_EXACT: error $14 for a ? in it) and its drive is checked (FCB_DRIVE_LOGIN).\n2. Its mode byte becomes C and ACCESS_CONFLICT checks it against the open files (error $1E).\n3. The directory is searched for the name (DIR_SCAN with MATCH_EXACT_USER).\n4. Found: E says what happens: 0 error $18; 1 opened (READ_ENTRY) and its header read\n   (HEADER_READ); 2 opened with no header (LENGTH_FROM_DIR); 3 renamed to .BAK (ERASE_BAK,\n   then RENAME_FCB) and step 5; 4 erased (DELETE_FCB) and step 5; any other E error $15.\n5. Not found, or after E = 3 or 4: D says: 0 error $17; 1 created (CREATE_ENTRY) with a new\n   header (HEADER_BLANK); 2 created with none; any other D error $15.\n6. MARK_OPEN.\nEntry: B = the file number (0-15), C = the mode (bit 0 reading, bit 1 writing, bits 2-3 the\naccess other records may have), D and E as above, HL = the name.\nExit: carry set and A = $FF for a file that was there, 0 for a new one; carry clear and A =\nthe error.\nObserved: LOAD \"nope\" on a blank disk gave the report \"File not found, 0:1\".","comment":"D, E kept"},
        "1590": {"comment":"Mode and number kept"},
        "1591": {"comment":"Record free and cleared?"},
        "1594": {"comment":"The name into it"},
        "1597": {"comment":"Its drive"},
        "1600": {"comment":"L = the mode"},
        "1601": {"comment":"D, E back"},
        "1602": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "1604": {"comment":"The mode"},
        "1605": {"comment":"Into the mode byte"},
        "1610": {"comment":"Clash with an open file?"},
        "1613": {"comment":"HL = the name test (MATCH_EXACT_USER)"},
        "1616": {"comment":"The directory searched"},
        "1619": {"comment":"D, E back"},
        "1620": {"comment":"Error"},
        "1621": {"comment":"Not there: as D says"},
        "1623": {"comment":"There: as E says"},
        "1624": {"comment":"E = 0?"},
        "1625": {"comment":"E = 0: error $18"},
        "1628": {"comment":"E = 1?"},
        "1631": {"comment":"Opened"},
        "1634": {"comment":"Header read"},
        "1637": {"comment":"Done"},
        "1639": {"synopsis":"E = 2: opened without a header.","comment":"E = 2?"},
        "1642": {"comment":"Opened"},
        "1645": {"comment":"Length from the directory"},
        "1648": {"comment":"Done"},
        "1650": {"synopsis":"E = 3: the file renamed to .BAK, then created as D says.","comment":"D kept"},
        "1651": {"comment":"E = 3?"},
        "1654": {"comment":"Any .BAK erased"},
        "1657": {"comment":"This one renamed .BAK"},
        "1660": {"comment":"Then as D says"},
        "1662": {"synopsis":"E = 4: the file erased, then created as D says; any other E is error $15.","comment":"Error $15 for E over 4"},
        "1665": {"comment":"E = 4?"},
        "1666": {"comment":"Yes: erased"},
        "1669": {"synopsis":"D back; stop on an error.","comment":"D back"},
        "1670": {"comment":"Error"},
        "1671": {"synopsis":"The file is not there: D says what happens.","comment":"D = 0?"},
        "1672": {"comment":"D = 0?"},
        "1673": {"comment":"Error $17"},
        "1676": {"comment":"D = 1?"},
        "1679": {"comment":"Created"},
        "1682": {"comment":"With a blank header"},
        "1685": {"comment":"Done"},
        "1687": {"synopsis":"D = 2: created without a header; any other D is error $15.","comment":"Error $15 for D over 2"},
        "1690": {"comment":"D = 2?"},
        "1691": {"comment":"Yes: created"},
        "1694": {"synopsis":"A new file: A = 0.","comment":"Error"},
        "1695": {"comment":"A = 0, carry"},
        "1699": {"synopsis":"A file that was there: A = $FF.","comment":"Error"},
        "1700": {"comment":"A = $FF, carry kept"},
        "1701": {"synopsis":"Marks the record at BC open (bit 7 of its mode byte) and counts one more open file on its\ndrive (IX+$21). AF kept.","comment":"Result kept"},
        "1702": {"comment":"The mode byte"},
        "1706": {"comment":"Open"},
        "1708": {"comment":"One more open file on the drive"},
        "1711": {"comment":"Result back"},
        "1713": {"synopsis":"Creates the file's directory entry: without bit 1 (writing) of the mode byte it is error\n$1E; otherwise the disk is checked for writing (DRIVE_WRITE_OK), the entry made\n(EXTENT_WR_LOAD, HL = 0) and\nbit 0 of record + $22 set.\nEntry: BC = the record, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The mode byte"},
        "1718": {"comment":"Bit 1 (writing) to carry"},
        "1720": {"comment":"Error $1E without it"},
        "1722": {"comment":"The disk can be written?"},
        "1725": {"comment":"The entry made"},
        "1728": {"comment":"The entry made"},
        "1731": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "1732": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "1736": {"comment":"Bit 0: entry made by this open"},
        "1738": {"comment":"Success"},
        "1740": {"synopsis":"Copies the file's directory entry into the first 32 bytes of the record (EXTENT_FIND). With\nbit 1\n(writing) of the mode byte it also checks bit 7 of the byte at record + $29 (ENTRY_RO_TEST,\nerror\n$1C) and the disk for writing (DRIVE_WRITE_OK).\nEntry: BC = the record.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error, $17 when the entry is not found.","comment":"Entry found and copied?"},
        "1743": {"comment":"No"},
        "1745": {"comment":"The mode byte"},
        "1749": {"comment":"Writing?"},
        "1751": {"comment":"Carry: success"},
        "1752": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "1753": {"comment":"Bit 7 at HL + 9 (record + $29)?"},
        "1756": {"comment":"The disk can be written?"},
        "1760": {"synopsis":"Error $19 (not found) becomes $17; others stay.","comment":"Not found?"},
        "1762": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "1764": {"comment":"Other errors as they are"},
        "1765": {"comment":"Error $17"},
        "1768": {"synopsis":"Copies the record to $DF20 with the extension BAK (name bytes 9-11) and erases any file of\nthat name (DELETE_FCB).\nEntry: BC = the record.\nExit: carry set when it was erased or there was none (error $17); carry clear and A = any\nother error.","comment":"Record kept"},
        "1769": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "1771": {"comment":"Copied to $DF20"},
        "1774": {"comment":"One record, $38 bytes"},
        "1780": {"comment":"Extension B"},
        "1782": {"comment":"$DF29: extension first byte"},
        "1785": {"comment":"A, K"},
        "1788": {"comment":"$DF2A-$DF2B: the other two"},
        "1791": {"comment":"Record kept"},
        "1792": {"comment":"The .BAK record"},
        "1795": {"comment":"Erased"},
        "1799": {"comment":"Done"},
        "1800": {"comment":"None there?"},
        "1802": {"comment":"That is fine"},
        "1804": {"comment":"Other errors: carry clear"},
        "1806": {"synopsis":"Opens a whole drive as file number B (DOS_JUMPS $014B). The record's first byte becomes $22,\nits mode byte C and its drive A; ACCESS_CONFLICT checks it. Its length (record + $23-$25)\nis the word at IX+5 plus 1 (the drive's blocks), shifted left IX+2 - 2 times (to sectors),\nplus the sectors of the reserved tracks (REC_TO_SECTOR), times 512. Then MARK_OPEN.\nEntry: A = the drive letter, B = the file number, C = the mode.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error ($15 or $16 from DRIVE_FIND_UC,\n$1D already open, $1E a clash).","comment":"A capital"},
        "1809": {"comment":"D = the letter"},
        "1810": {"comment":"E = the mode"},
        "1811": {"comment":"Record free and cleared?"},
        "1814": {"comment":"No"},
        "1815": {"comment":"First byte $22: a whole drive"},
        "1817": {"comment":"The record's first byte"},
        "1818": {"comment":"The mode byte"},
        "1823": {"comment":"Its drive"},
        "1825": {"comment":"IX = the drive"},
        "1826": {"comment":"IX = the drive's table"},
        "1829": {"comment":"Clash with an open file?"},
        "1832": {"comment":"Error"},
        "1833": {"comment":"DE = the word at IX+5, plus 1"},
        "1839": {"comment":"One more"},
        "1840": {"comment":"Shifted left IX+2 times"},
        "1843": {"comment":"Less 2: blocks to sectors"},
        "1848": {"comment":"Plus the reserved tracks (REC_TO_SECTOR)"},
        "1851": {"comment":"Doubled: x 512 with +$23 = 0"},
        "1855": {"comment":"Length bytes 2 and 3"},
        "1858": {"comment":"+$24, +$25"},
        "1862": {"comment":"Success"},
        "1863": {"comment":"Marked open"},
        "1866": {"synopsis":"Closes file number B (DOS_JUMPS $0109): it must be open; its drive is checked\n(FCB_DRIVE_LOGIN), what\nis pending is written out (WRITE_BACK) and CLOSE_RECORD clears the mode byte.\nEntry: B = the file number.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error, the file still open.","comment":"Open?"},
        "1869": {"comment":"Its drive"},
        "1872": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "1875": {"comment":"Error: still open"},
        "1876": {"comment":"Closed"},
        "1878": {"synopsis":"Writes out what a file open for writing has pending; without bit 1 of the mode byte there is\nnothing. Otherwise HEADER_UPDATE puts the length and header bytes into its header,\nREC_RELEASE\nwrites its buffer, FLUSH_DRIVE the cache and EXTENT_STORE its directory entry.\nEntry: BC = the record, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The mode byte"},
        "1882": {"comment":"Writing?"},
        "1884": {"comment":"Carry: success"},
        "1885": {"comment":"No: nothing to do"},
        "1886": {"comment":"Header brought up to date"},
        "1889": {"comment":"The record's buffer"},
        "1892": {"comment":"The cache"},
        "1895": {"comment":"The directory entry"},
        "1899": {"synopsis":"Closes file number B without writing anything out (DOS_JUMPS $010C). For a file open for\nwriting, DIR_SLOT_RETURN and FCB_BLOCKS_FREE run when bit 1 of record + $22 is set, and\nCACHE_DROP_FILE runs; CLOSE_RECORD\nthen clears the mode byte.\nEntry: B = the file number.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error when the number is not open or\nthe drive fails.","comment":"Open?"},
        "1902": {"comment":"Its drive"},
        "1905": {"comment":"Error"},
        "1906": {"comment":"The mode byte"},
        "1910": {"comment":"Writing?"},
        "1912": {"comment":"No: just closed"},
        "1914": {"comment":"The flags at +$22"},
        "1916": {"comment":"Bit 1?"},
        "1918": {"comment":"No"},
        "1920": {"comment":"Yes: DIR_SLOT_RETURN, then FCB_BLOCKS_FREE"},
        "1923": {"comment":"Then FCB_BLOCKS_FREE"},
        "1926": {"synopsis":"CACHE_DROP_FILE for the file.","comment":"CACHE_DROP_FILE"},
        "1929": {"synopsis":"Clears the mode byte of the record at BC (no longer open) and counts one open file less on\nits drive (IX+$21); at none, DRIVE_LOG_OUT runs for the drive (bit 0 of IX+$1B cleared, then\nCACHE_DROP_DRIVE).\nExit: carry set.","comment":"The mode byte"},
        "1933": {"comment":"0: closed"},
        "1935": {"comment":"One open file less on the drive"},
        "1938": {"comment":"None left: DRIVE_LOG_OUT"},
        "1941": {"comment":"Success"},
        "1943": {"synopsis":"The first 10 bytes of a file header: the text PLUS3DOS, then $1A and $01. HEADER_BLANK\nwrites them, HEADER_READ compares them."},
        "1953": {"synopsis":"When the file has a header (bit 6 of record + $22), writes its length and 8 header bytes\ninto it (HEADER_FIELDS), the file pointer kept. Called from $075E.\nEntry: BC = the record.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The flags"},
        "1957": {"comment":"A header?"},
        "1959": {"comment":"Carry: success"},
        "1960": {"comment":"No: nothing"},
        "1961": {"comment":"E, HL = the file pointer"},
        "1964": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "1966": {"comment":"The fields written"},
        "1971": {"comment":"Result kept"},
        "1972": {"comment":"The pointer back"},
        "1977": {"synopsis":"Writes the header's fields: the pointer goes to byte 11; the 3 length bytes from record +\n$23 and a 0 go there, then the 8 bytes from record + $30 (bytes 15-22); HDR_SUM_STORE puts\nthe sum\nof bytes 0-126 at byte 127.\nEntry: BC = the record.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"Pointer to byte 11"},
        "1980": {"comment":"E = 0"},
        "1984": {"comment":"The length bytes"},
        "1988": {"comment":"Three"},
        "1990": {"comment":"Write them"},
        "1993": {"comment":"Error"},
        "1994": {"comment":"Byte 14: 0"},
        "1995": {"comment":"Write a 0"},
        "1998": {"comment":"Error"},
        "1999": {"comment":"The 8 header bytes"},
        "2003": {"comment":"Eight"},
        "2005": {"comment":"Write them"},
        "2008": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2009": {"comment":"The checksum at byte 127"},
        "2012": {"synopsis":"Writes E bytes from HL to the file, each through PUT_FILE_BYTE.\nEntry: BC = the record, HL, E.\nExit: carry set and HL past the bytes; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "2014": {"comment":"Written to the file"},
        "2017": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2018": {"comment":"Another?"},
        "2022": {"synopsis":"Writes a new header at the file pointer (0 for a new file): the 10 bytes of HEADER_SIG, 117\nbytes of 0 and the sum at byte 127 (HDR_SUM_STORE); HEADER_FLAG then marks it.\nEntry: BC = the record.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"Ten bytes"},
        "2024": {"comment":"The signature"},
        "2027": {"comment":"Write them"},
        "2030": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2031": {"comment":"Byte 10: 0"},
        "2033": {"comment":"Write it"},
        "2036": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2037": {"comment":"116 more bytes"},
        "2039": {"synopsis":"One byte of 0.","comment":"A 0"},
        "2040": {"comment":"Write it"},
        "2043": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2044": {"comment":"Another?"},
        "2047": {"comment":"The checksum at byte 127"},
        "2050": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2051": {"synopsis":"Marks the file as having a header (bit 6 of record + $22).\nExit: carry set.","comment":"The flags"},
        "2055": {"comment":"Bit 6: a header"},
        "2057": {"comment":"Success"},
        "2059": {"synopsis":"Reads the file's header. HDR_SUM_CHECK checks the sum of its first 127 bytes against byte\n127; the\nfirst 10 bytes must be those of HEADER_SIG and byte 10 must be 0. Then record + $23-$25 get\nthe 3 length bytes (byte 14 is skipped) and record + $30-$37 bytes 15-22, the pointer goes\nto 128 and HEADER_FLAG marks the header. A file without one (wrong sum or signature, or\nerror $19, too short) goes to HEADER_NONE.\nEntry: BC = the record.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"Checksum of the first 128 bytes"},
        "2062": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2064": {"comment":"Wrong: no header"},
        "2066": {"comment":"Ten bytes"},
        "2068": {"comment":"The signature"},
        "2071": {"synopsis":"One byte of the signature.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "2074": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2076": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "2078": {"comment":"No: no header"},
        "2080": {"comment":"Another?"},
        "2083": {"comment":"Byte 10"},
        "2086": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2088": {"comment":"Not 0?"},
        "2090": {"comment":"Yes: no header"},
        "2092": {"comment":"The length bytes"},
        "2096": {"comment":"Three"},
        "2098": {"synopsis":"One length byte.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "2101": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2102": {"comment":"Into the record"},
        "2104": {"comment":"Another?"},
        "2107": {"comment":"Byte 14, not kept"},
        "2110": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2111": {"comment":"The 8 header bytes"},
        "2115": {"comment":"Eight"},
        "2117": {"synopsis":"One header byte.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "2120": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2121": {"comment":"Into the record"},
        "2123": {"comment":"Another?"},
        "2126": {"comment":"Pointer to 128, past the header"},
        "2129": {"comment":"E = 0: pointer 128"},
        "2133": {"comment":"Header marked"},
        "2135": {"synopsis":"Error $19 means no header; other errors stay.","comment":"Too short?"},
        "2137": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "2139": {"comment":"Other errors as they are"},
        "2140": {"synopsis":"No header: the pointer back to 0, then LENGTH_FROM_DIR.","comment":"Pointer back to 0"},
        "2147": {"synopsis":"Finds a file's length from its directory entries: the walk with LENGTH_ENTRY keeps at\n$DF90-$DF92 the largest count ENTRY_REC_COUNT gives for an entry of its name, and the length\n(record +\n$23-$25) is that count times 128; error $22 when that does not fit in 3 bytes.\nEntry: BC = the record.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The largest so far: 0"},
        "2150": {"comment":"$DF91, $DF92 = 0"},
        "2153": {"comment":"Its top byte"},
        "2157": {"comment":"Each entry of the name"},
        "2160": {"comment":"The directory walked"},
        "2163": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2164": {"comment":"D, E = $DF92, $DF91"},
        "2168": {"comment":"H = $DF90"},
        "2171": {"comment":"L = 0"},
        "2173": {"comment":"Count x 256 halved: x 128"},
        "2175": {"comment":"32 bits shifted right one place"},
        "2181": {"comment":"Too big for 3 bytes?"},
        "2183": {"comment":"Error $22"},
        "2186": {"comment":"H, L kept"},
        "2187": {"comment":"Length byte 3"},
        "2192": {"comment":"D, E = H, L"},
        "2193": {"comment":"Byte 2"},
        "2196": {"comment":"Byte 1"},
        "2197": {"comment":"Success"},
        "2199": {"synopsis":"The directory walk's routine for LENGTH_FROM_DIR: for an entry with the record's name\n(MATCH_EXACT_USER), ENTRY_REC_COUNT gives a 24-bit count in A, H, L, and a larger one than\nthe 3 bytes at\n$DF90-$DF92 goes there. Returns carry set and NZ so that the walk goes on.\nEntry: HL = the entry, BC = the record.","comment":"This file's entry?"},
        "2202": {"comment":"No: go on"},
        "2203": {"comment":"Record kept"},
        "2204": {"comment":"BC = the entry"},
        "2206": {"comment":"A, H, L = its count"},
        "2209": {"comment":"B, D, E = it"},
        "2211": {"comment":"The largest so far"},
        "2214": {"comment":"Less than this one?"},
        "2215": {"comment":"Stored - new"},
        "2220": {"comment":"Top byte too"},
        "2221": {"comment":"No: kept"},
        "2223": {"comment":"Yes: this one"},
        "2227": {"comment":"Top byte"},
        "2231": {"synopsis":"Carry and NZ: the walk goes on.","comment":"Record back"},
        "2232": {"comment":"A = $FF, NZ, carry"},
        "2233": {"comment":"A = $FF, NZ"},
        "2235": {"synopsis":"Gives the address of file number B's 8 header bytes (DOS_JUMPS $010F).\nEntry: B = the file number.\nExit: carry set, IX = record + $30, Z when the file has no header (bit 6 of record + $22\nclear), NZ when it has one; carry clear and A = $15 or $1D for a bad number or one not open.","comment":"Open?"},
        "2238": {"comment":"No"},
        "2239": {"comment":"IX = the 8 bytes"},
        "2243": {"comment":"+ the record"},
        "2245": {"comment":"The flags"},
        "2249": {"comment":"Z: no header"},
        "2251": {"comment":"Success"},
        "2253": {"synopsis":"Gives open file number B the mode C (DOS_JUMPS $0145). The file is written back first\n(WRITE_BACK); then the new mode is checked against the other open files (ACCESS_CONFLICT,\nerror $1E) and, with bit 1 (writing), bit 7 at record + $29 (ENTRY_RO_TEST, error $1C) and\nthe disk\n(DRIVE_WRITE_OK). On a failure the old mode comes back.\nEntry: B = the file number, C = the new mode (bits 0-3).\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"E = the new mode"},
        "2254": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "2255": {"comment":"Open?"},
        "2258": {"comment":"Its drive"},
        "2261": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "2264": {"comment":"E back"},
        "2265": {"comment":"Error"},
        "2266": {"comment":"The mode byte"},
        "2270": {"comment":"D = the old mode"},
        "2271": {"comment":"The new one"},
        "2272": {"comment":"HL, D kept"},
        "2274": {"comment":"Clash with an open file?"},
        "2279": {"comment":"Yes: the old mode back"},
        "2281": {"comment":"Writing?"},
        "2283": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "2285": {"comment":"Bit 7 at HL + 9 (record + $29)?"},
        "2288": {"comment":"The disk can be written?"},
        "2291": {"comment":"No: the old mode back"},
        "2293": {"synopsis":"Marked open again; success.","comment":"Open"},
        "2295": {"comment":"Success"},
        "2297": {"synopsis":"The old mode back, carry clear.","comment":"The old mode"},
        "2298": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "2300": {"synopsis":"Counts the unused space of drive A (DOS_JUMPS $0121): the letter is made a capital and the\ndrive checked (DRIVE_LOGIN, which also scans its directory if that is not yet done), then\nFREE_KB_COUNT\ncounts the clear bits of the drive's block map (at IX+$28).\nEntry: A = the drive letter.\nExit: as FREE_KB_COUNT; carry clear and A = the error when there is no such drive.","comment":"A capital"},
        "2303": {"comment":"IX = the drive"},
        "2306": {"comment":"No such drive"},
        "2307": {"comment":"Count the unused blocks"},
        "2310": {"synopsis":"Reads or sets the byte at $DF93 (DOS_JUMPS $0130), which PARSE_FCB puts in byte 0 of a new\nname,\nthe byte compared with byte 0 of the directory entries.\nEntry: A = $FF to read it, otherwise the new value (0-15).\nExit: carry set and A = the value; carry clear and A = $15 for a value of 16 or more.","comment":"Only read it?"},
        "2312": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "2314": {"comment":"User number 0-15?"},
        "2316": {"comment":"B = the new user number"},
        "2317": {"comment":"Error $15 for 16 or more"},
        "2319": {"comment":"Carry clear: error"},
        "2320": {"comment":"Make it the default user number"},
        "2324": {"synopsis":"Returns the default user number ($DF93) in A, with carry set.","comment":"A = the default user number"},
        "2327": {"comment":"Success"},
        "2328": {"comment":"Return it"},
        "2329": {"synopsis":"Sets or reads the default drive (DOS_JUMPS $012D). A drive letter in A, in either case,\nbecomes the default drive at $DF94 when the drive has a table (DRIVE_FIND_UC); $FF only\nreads it.\nEntry: A = the drive letter, or $FF.\nExit: carry set and A = the default drive letter; carry clear and A = $15 (not A-P) or $16\n(no table for the drive).\nChanges: AF, B, IX (the drive's table, when a letter is given).","comment":"Drive letter to upper case"},
        "2332": {"comment":"$FF only reads the default?"},
        "2334": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "2336": {"comment":"B = the drive letter"},
        "2337": {"comment":"IX = its drive table; is the drive there?"},
        "2340": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2341": {"comment":"Make it the default drive"},
        "2345": {"synopsis":"Returns the default drive letter ($DF94) in A, with carry set.","comment":"A = the default drive"},
        "2348": {"comment":"Success"},
        "2350": {"synopsis":"Deletes the files whose name matches the text at HL (DOS_JUMPS $0124).\n1. Parses the name into the scratch file record at $DF20 (PARSE_NAME: wildcards allowed, an\n   optional user number and drive letter before a colon).\n2. Logs in its drive (FCB_DRIVE_LOGIN), refuses a name that a file record has open\n   (CONFLICT_OTHERS,\n   error $1E) and checks the drive (DRIVE_WRITE_OK).\n3. Runs DELETE_ONE on every directory entry through DIR_EACH_MATCH, which writes the changed\n   sectors when any entry matched.\nEntry: HL = the name, ended by $FF.\nExit: carry set on success; otherwise carry clear and A = the error: $14 bad name, $17\nnothing matched, $1C an entry with bit 7 of byte 9 set (the scan stops there), $1E open, or\nan error from the drive.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"Scratch file record at $DF20"},
        "2353": {"comment":"Parse HL's name into it, wildcards allowed"},
        "2356": {"comment":"Log in its drive"},
        "2359": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2360": {"synopsis":"Deletes the files matching the name in file record BC, whose drive is logged in (step 2 of\nFILE_DELETE). The file-opening code also comes here: from $0682, and from $0703 with a copy\nof the file's record at $DF20 whose type is BAK.\nEntry: BC = the file record, IX = the drive's table.\nExit: as FILE_DELETE.","comment":"Error $1E if a file record has the name open"},
        "2363": {"comment":"Can the drive be changed?"},
        "2366": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2367": {"comment":"Callback for each entry"},
        "2370": {"comment":"Run it over the directory"},
        "2373": {"synopsis":"DIR_SCAN callback for FILE_DELETE. When the entry matches record BC's name (MATCH_WILD):\nrefuses bit 7 of its byte 9 (ENTRY_RO_TEST), releases its blocks in the bitmap\n(ENTRY_BLOCKS_SET with A = 0), puts $E5 in its byte 0, writes it to its sector buffer\n(DIR_ENTRY_WRITE), counts one more free entry (DIR_FREE_INC) and sets $DF95 to $FF.\nEntry: HL = the entry's copy at $DFA2, DE = its number, BC = the file record.\nExit: carry set and NZ to go on; carry clear and A = the error to stop.","comment":"Entry matches the name?"},
        "2376": {"comment":"No: next entry"},
        "2377": {"comment":"Byte 9 bit 7 set? Error $1C"},
        "2380": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2381": {"comment":"Keep the entry and its number"},
        "2383": {"comment":"A = 0: release the entry's blocks"},
        "2384": {"comment":"Release them in the bitmap"},
        "2389": {"comment":"Mark the entry free"},
        "2391": {"comment":"Write it back to its sector buffer"},
        "2394": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2395": {"comment":"One more free entry"},
        "2398": {"comment":"$DF95 = $FF: a match was found"},
        "2402": {"comment":"Carry set, NZ: next entry"},
        "2403": {"synopsis":"Changes the attribute bits of the files whose name matches the text at HL (DOS_JUMPS $0148).\nThe attributes are bit 7 of name letters 1-4 and of the three type letters; bits 6-0 of D\nand E stand for name letters 1, 2, 3, 4 and type letters 1, 2, 3 in that order. Each set bit\nof D sets that attribute, then each set bit of E clears it (ATTRIB_ONE), so a bit set in\nboth ends clear.\nEntry: HL = the name, ended by $FF (wildcards allowed); D = the attributes to set; E = the\nattributes to clear.\nExit: carry set on success; otherwise carry clear and A = the error: $14 bad name, $17\nnothing matched, $1E open, or an error from the drive.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX; $DF96, $DF97.","comment":"$DF96 = bits to clear (E), $DF97 = bits to set (D)"},
        "2407": {"comment":"Scratch file record at $DF20"},
        "2410": {"comment":"Parse HL's name into it, wildcards allowed"},
        "2413": {"comment":"Log in its drive"},
        "2416": {"comment":"Can the drive be changed?"},
        "2419": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2420": {"comment":"Callback for each entry"},
        "2423": {"comment":"Refuse an open name, then run it"},
        "2425": {"synopsis":"Renames the file named by the text at HL to the name at DE (DOS_JUMPS $0127). Neither name\nmay have wildcards. The old name is parsed into the record at $DF58, the new one into $DF20,\nand the old name's drive is logged in.\n1. RENAME_FCB: both names must be on the same drive, the drive is checked (DRIVE_WRITE_OK),\n   the new\n   name must not be open nor in the directory.\n2. Every entry of the old name gets the new user number, name and type (RENAME_ONE), through\n   DIR_EACH_MATCH.\nEntry: HL = the old name, DE = the new name, each ended by $FF.\nExit: carry set on success; otherwise carry clear and A = the error: $14 bad name, $17 old\nname not found, $18 new name exists, $1C bit 7 of byte 9 set, $1E open, $1F different\ndrives, or an error from the drive.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"Keep the new name"},
        "2426": {"comment":"Old name into the file record at $DF58"},
        "2429": {"comment":"Parse it, no wildcards"},
        "2432": {"comment":"Log in its drive"},
        "2435": {"comment":"HL = the new name"},
        "2436": {"comment":"Keep the old name's record"},
        "2437": {"comment":"New name into the file record at $DF20"},
        "2440": {"comment":"Parse it, no wildcards"},
        "2443": {"comment":"BC = the old name's record"},
        "2444": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2445": {"synopsis":"Renames the file in record BC to the name in the record at $DF20 (step 1 of FILE_RENAME).\nThe file-opening code at $0679 also comes here, after deleting the BAK copy of the name\n(DELETE_FCB from $0703), with $DF20 holding that BAK name.\nEntry: BC = the record with the old name, $DF20 = the record with the new name, IX = the\ndrive's table.\nExit: as FILE_RENAME.","comment":"HL = the drive letter of record BC"},
        "2448": {"comment":"HL = byte $21 of the record"},
        "2449": {"comment":"Same drive as the new name?"},
        "2452": {"comment":"Compare with $DF41, byte $21 of $DF20"},
        "2453": {"comment":"Error $1F: different drives"},
        "2455": {"comment":"Different: return the error"},
        "2456": {"comment":"Can the drive be changed?"},
        "2459": {"comment":"Keep the old name's record"},
        "2460": {"comment":"The new name must not be open"},
        "2466": {"comment":"Look for an entry with the new name"},
        "2472": {"comment":"BC = the old name's record"},
        "2473": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2474": {"comment":"Found: the new name is taken"},
        "2475": {"comment":"Error $18"},
        "2477": {"comment":"Taken: return the error"},
        "2478": {"comment":"Callback for each entry of the old name"},
        "2481": {"synopsis":"Refuses the name in record BC with error $1E when a file record has it open\n(CONFLICT_OTHERS), then\nruns DIR_EACH_MATCH with the callback at HL.","comment":"Keep the callback"},
        "2482": {"comment":"Error $1E if a file record has the name open"},
        "2485": {"comment":"HL = the callback"},
        "2486": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2487": {"synopsis":"Calls the callback at HL for every directory entry (DIR_SCAN), with $DF95 cleared first; the\ncallbacks set $DF95 to $FF when they change an entry. If any entry changed, the changed\nsectors are written (FLUSH_DRIVE); if none did, the result is error $17.\nEntry: HL = the callback, BC = the file record, IX = the drive's table.\nExit: carry set on success; carry clear and A = $17 when nothing matched, or the callback's\nor the drive's error.","comment":"Nothing matched yet"},
        "2491": {"comment":"Call HL for every directory entry"},
        "2494": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2495": {"comment":"Did any entry match?"},
        "2499": {"comment":"None: error $17; else write the changed sectors"},
        "2505": {"synopsis":"DIR_SCAN callback for ATTRIB_SET. When the entry matches record BC's name (MATCH_WILD), sets\nthe attributes given in $DF97, then clears those in $DF96 (ATTRIB_APPLY), and writes the\nentry back (DIR_ENTRY_DONE).","comment":"Entry matches the name?"},
        "2508": {"comment":"No: next entry"},
        "2509": {"comment":"Keep the record"},
        "2510": {"comment":"A = the attributes to set"},
        "2513": {"comment":"C = $FF: set bit 7"},
        "2515": {"comment":"Keep the entry"},
        "2516": {"comment":"Apply them to the entry's letters"},
        "2520": {"comment":"A = the attributes to clear"},
        "2523": {"comment":"C = 0: clear bit 7"},
        "2524": {"comment":"Apply them"},
        "2527": {"comment":"BC = the record"},
        "2528": {"comment":"Write the entry back, note the match"},
        "2530": {"synopsis":"Puts C into bit 7 of the entry's name letters 1-4 and type letters 1-3 where bits 6-0 of A\nare set; the letters of clear bits are left alone.\nEntry: A = the attribute bits, C = $FF to set or 0 to clear, HL = the entry.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.","comment":"Drop bit 7 of A"},
        "2531": {"comment":"Bits 6-3: name letters 1-4"},
        "2533": {"comment":"HL = name letter 1"},
        "2534": {"comment":"Name letters 1-4"},
        "2537": {"comment":"HL = type letter 1"},
        "2538": {"comment":"Past letters 5-8"},
        "2541": {"comment":"Bits 2-0: type letters 1-3"},
        "2543": {"synopsis":"One attribute bit for the letter at HL (B letters).","comment":"This letter's bit set?"},
        "2544": {"comment":"No: leave the letter alone"},
        "2546": {"comment":"Clear its bit 7"},
        "2548": {"comment":"C zero?"},
        "2550": {"comment":"Yes: leave it clear"},
        "2552": {"comment":"No: set it"},
        "2554": {"synopsis":"Next letter.","comment":"Next letter"},
        "2555": {"comment":"Next bit and letter"},
        "2558": {"synopsis":"DIR_SCAN callback for the rename. When the entry has record BC's name (MATCH_WILD), refuses\nbit 7 of its byte 9 (ENTRY_RO_TEST), gives it the user number of the record at $DF20\n(keeping bit 4 of its own byte 0) and that record's 11 name and type bytes, and writes it\nback (DIR_ENTRY_DONE).","comment":"Entry has the old name?"},
        "2561": {"comment":"No: next entry"},
        "2562": {"comment":"Byte 9 bit 7 set? Error $1C"},
        "2565": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2567": {"comment":"DE = the entry, HL = the new name's record"},
        "2568": {"comment":"HL = the new name's record"},
        "2571": {"comment":"Keep bit 4 of the entry's first byte"},
        "2572": {"comment":"Bit 4 only"},
        "2574": {"comment":"Take the user number from the new record"},
        "2575": {"comment":"New byte 0"},
        "2576": {"comment":"Step to the names"},
        "2579": {"comment":"Copy the new name and type"},
        "2582": {"comment":"Into the entry"},
        "2586": {"synopsis":"Writes the entry's copy to its sector buffer (DIR_ENTRY_WRITE) and sets $DF95 to $FF; exits\nwith carry set and NZ so that DIR_SCAN goes on.","comment":"Write the entry back to its sector buffer"},
        "2589": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2590": {"comment":"$DF95 = $FF: a match was found"},
        "2595": {"synopsis":"Fills a buffer with the sorted names of the files matching the text at HL, and their sizes\n(DOS_JUMPS $011E). The buffer has B slots of 13 bytes: the 11 name and type bytes as in the\ndirectory (attribute bits included), then a word with the size in KB. The caller fills the\nfirst slot; only names after it are put in, so a full buffer can be continued by putting its\nlast name into the first slot of the next call.\n1. Parses the name into the record at $DF20 (wildcards allowed), logs in its drive and\n   brings the entries of files open on the drive up to date (FLUSH_DRV_IX).\n2. Each entry with the same byte 0 (user number) and a matching name (CAT_ENTRY) is taken,\n   except one with bit 7 of type letter 2 set unless bit 0 of C is set. Its slot is found in\n   alphabetical order (letters compared without bit 7); a new name is inserted there, moving\n   the later slots up (the last one falls out when the buffer is full), and the entry's KB\n   are added to the slot's size.\nEntry: HL = the name, ended by $FF; DE = the buffer; B = the slots in it; C = flags (bit 0:\ntake every entry).\nExit: carry set on success, carry clear and A = the error otherwise; B = the slots filled,\nthe first one included; C = the slots in the buffer.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX; $DF98-$DF9C.\nObserved: CAT in +3 BASIC listed ltk.dsk as \"DISK . 1K\" and \"124K free\"; a blank disk as\n\"No files found\" and \"173K free\"; after SAVE \"prog\", \"PROG . 1K\" and \"172K free\".\nObserved: CAT in +3 BASIC on the +3E listed ltk.dsk as \"DISK . 1K\" and \"124K free\".","comment":"$DF98 = the buffer"},
        "2599": {"comment":"$DF9A = the flags (C), $DF9B = slots (B)"},
        "2603": {"comment":"One slot filled: the caller's first one"},
        "2605": {"comment":"$DF9C = slots filled"},
        "2608": {"comment":"Scratch file record at $DF20"},
        "2611": {"comment":"Parse HL's name into it, wildcards allowed"},
        "2614": {"comment":"Log in its drive"},
        "2617": {"comment":"Bring entries of files open on it up to date"},
        "2620": {"comment":"Callback for each entry"},
        "2623": {"comment":"Run it over the directory"},
        "2626": {"comment":"C = slots in the buffer, B = slots filled"},
        "2631": {"synopsis":"DIR_SCAN callback for CATALOGUE: puts the entry in the buffer (CAT_ENTRY) and always goes on\n(carry set, NZ)."},
        "2632": {"comment":"Consider this entry"},
        "2636": {"comment":"A = $FF, NZ: go on with the next entry"},
        "2637": {"comment":"A = $FF, NZ"},
        "2639": {"synopsis":"Puts the directory entry at HL into the catalogue buffer ($DF98, $DF9A-$DF9C) if it matches\nrecord BC, is not left out by the flags and sorts after the buffer's first slot (see\nCATALOGUE).\nEntry: HL = the entry's copy, BC = the record.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"Same byte 0 and a matching name?"},
        "2642": {"comment":"No: skip it"},
        "2643": {"comment":"Flags bit 0: include every entry?"},
        "2646": {"comment":"Bit 0 into carry"},
        "2647": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "2650": {"comment":"HL = type letter 2"},
        "2653": {"comment":"HL = byte $0A"},
        "2654": {"comment":"Bit 7 set?"},
        "2656": {"comment":"Yes: skip the entry"},
        "2657": {"comment":"Return: skipped"},
        "2658": {"synopsis":"Compares the name with the first slot's, then looks for its place among the filled slots.","comment":"DE = the first slot"},
        "2662": {"comment":"Name after the first slot's?"},
        "2665": {"comment":"No: skip it"},
        "2666": {"comment":"C = slots in the buffer, B = slots filled"},
        "2670": {"synopsis":"Next slot (C counts the slots left, B the filled ones still to compare)."},
        "2671": {"comment":"DE = the next slot"},
        "2674": {"comment":"DE + 13"},
        "2677": {"comment":"One slot fewer left"},
        "2678": {"comment":"More filled slots to compare?"},
        "2680": {"comment":"None, and no room: skip the entry"},
        "2681": {"comment":"Room: put it in the next free slot"},
        "2683": {"synopsis":"Compares the entry with this filled slot: after it goes on, the same name adds the size,\nbefore it inserts the name here.","comment":"Compare the name with this slot's"},
        "2686": {"comment":"Slot's name first: go on"},
        "2688": {"comment":"Same name: another extent, add its size"},
        "2692": {"comment":"HL = slots in the buffer"},
        "2695": {"comment":"H = 0"},
        "2697": {"comment":"HL = slots - 1"},
        "2698": {"comment":"BC = slots - 1"},
        "2700": {"comment":"Times 13"},
        "2705": {"comment":"HL = the last slot"},
        "2710": {"comment":"BC = bytes from this slot to the last"},
        "2711": {"comment":"A = low byte of the difference"},
        "2713": {"comment":"Then the high byte"},
        "2716": {"comment":"HL = the last byte to move"},
        "2717": {"comment":"DE = 13 bytes further on"},
        "2723": {"comment":"Anything to move?"},
        "2725": {"comment":"No: skip the move"},
        "2727": {"comment":"Move the later slots up one place"},
        "2729": {"synopsis":"The later slots are moved up."},
        "2731": {"synopsis":"Copies the entry's 11 name and type bytes into slot DE, sets its size to 0 and counts one\nmore filled slot, up to the buffer's size."},
        "2733": {"comment":"HL = the entry's name"},
        "2734": {"comment":"Copy the 11 name and type bytes"},
        "2739": {"comment":"Size so far: 0 KB"},
        "2740": {"comment":"0 KB"},
        "2743": {"comment":"L = slots in the buffer, H = slots filled"},
        "2746": {"comment":"One more filled, unless the buffer is full"},
        "2747": {"comment":"Filled below slots?"},
        "2750": {"comment":"Store the count"},
        "2755": {"synopsis":"Adds the KB of the entry's blocks (ENTRY_SIZE_KB) to slot DE's size word.","comment":"HL = the KB this entry takes"},
        "2758": {"comment":"HL = the slot"},
        "2759": {"comment":"HL = the slot's size word"},
        "2762": {"comment":"HL = the size word"},
        "2763": {"comment":"Add the entry's KB to it"},
        "2764": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "2768": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "2771": {"synopsis":"Compares the 11 name and type bytes of the directory entry at HL (from its byte 1) with\nthose of the slot at DE, ignoring bit 7.\nExit: Z if they are the same; carry set if the slot's name comes first; otherwise the\nentry's comes first.\nChanges: AF."},
        "2774": {"comment":"11 name and type bytes"},
        "2776": {"comment":"HL = the entry's first letter"},
        "2777": {"synopsis":"One letter pair.","comment":"C = entry letter, bit 7 dropped"},
        "2778": {"comment":"Bit 7 out"},
        "2780": {"comment":"A = slot letter, bit 7 dropped"},
        "2781": {"comment":"Bit 7 out"},
        "2782": {"comment":"Do they differ?"},
        "2783": {"comment":"Yes: stop"},
        "2785": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "2786": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "2789": {"synopsis":"Restores the registers."},
        "2793": {"synopsis":"Parses a file name like PARSE_NAME, then refuses wildcards: a '?' in the 11 name and type\nbytes (also one from a '*') is error $14. Also from $063A.\nEntry: HL = the text, ended by $FF; BC = the file record to fill.\nExit: carry set on success; carry clear and A = $14 otherwise.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.\nObserved: SAVE \"a?b\" gave the report \"Bad filename, 0:1\".","comment":"Parse the name into record BC"},
        "2796": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2797": {"comment":"HL = the record's name"},
        "2801": {"comment":"11 name and type bytes"},
        "2803": {"synopsis":"One name byte: a wildcard?","comment":"Next byte of the name"},
        "2805": {"comment":"Wildcard?"},
        "2807": {"comment":"Yes: error $14"},
        "2809": {"comment":"Return the error"},
        "2810": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "2811": {"comment":"More bytes?"},
        "2813": {"comment":"Success"},
        "2815": {"synopsis":"Parses a file name into a file record (PARSE_NAME_BC); wildcards are allowed.\nEntry: HL = the text, ended by $FF; BC = the file record to fill.\nExit: carry set on success; carry clear and A = $14 for a bad name.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"Parse with wildcards allowed"},
        "2818": {"synopsis":"Parses what comes before the colon: a user number (PARSE_USER), a drive letter\n(PARSE_DRIVE), or both in that order. When a user number was read the result is success\nwhatever follows it; otherwise it is the drive letter's.","comment":"A user number?"},
        "2821": {"comment":"No: the drive letter decides"},
        "2823": {"comment":"A drive letter may follow"},
        "2826": {"comment":"Success either way"},
        "2828": {"synopsis":"Reads a user number of one or two digits at HL into byte 0 of record BC.\nExit: carry set and A = the number; carry clear for no digit, or for a number over 15 (HL\nthen past the digits).","comment":"First character a digit?"},
        "2831": {"comment":"No: no user number"},
        "2832": {"comment":"E = the first digit"},
        "2833": {"comment":"Is the next character a digit too?"},
        "2836": {"comment":"Digit?"},
        "2839": {"comment":"No: E is the number"},
        "2841": {"comment":"D = the second digit"},
        "2842": {"comment":"E = 10 * the first + the second"},
        "2843": {"comment":"E = first * 2"},
        "2845": {"comment":"Times 8"},
        "2847": {"comment":"Plus the first * 2: times 10"},
        "2848": {"comment":"Plus the second"},
        "2850": {"comment":"Step past it"},
        "2853": {"synopsis":"A = the number: stored if it is 15 or less.","comment":"A = the number"},
        "2854": {"comment":"Over 15?"},
        "2856": {"comment":"Return: carry clear"},
        "2857": {"comment":"Store it in byte 0 of the record"},
        "2859": {"synopsis":"Reads a drive letter A-P at HL, after spaces, into byte $21 of record BC.\nExit: carry set and HL on the next character; carry clear otherwise.","comment":"First character after spaces"},
        "2862": {"comment":"End of the text?"},
        "2863": {"comment":"Below 'A'?"},
        "2865": {"comment":"Carry set if 'A' or more"},
        "2866": {"comment":"Return: not a letter"},
        "2867": {"comment":"After 'P'?"},
        "2869": {"comment":"Return: not a letter"},
        "2871": {"comment":"Store it as the record's drive (+$21)"},
        "2877": {"comment":"Step past it"},
        "2880": {"comment":"Success"},
        "2882": {"synopsis":"Turns a digit character in A into its value.\nExit: carry set and A = 0-9 for a digit; carry clear otherwise.","comment":"A = the digit's value; below '0'?"},
        "2884": {"comment":"Carry set if '0' or more"},
        "2885": {"comment":"Return: not a digit"},
        "2886": {"comment":"Carry set for 0-9"},
        "2889": {"synopsis":"Calls PARSE_FCB keeping BC, and loads A with $14, the error number when it failed.","comment":"Keep the record's address"},
        "2890": {"comment":"Parse the name"},
        "2894": {"comment":"A = $14 in case it failed"},
        "2897": {"synopsis":"Fills file record BC from the file name text at HL. The text ends with $FF; bit 7 of each\ncharacter is dropped and letters are made upper case.\n1. Byte 0 gets the default user number ($DF93) and byte $21 the default drive letter\n   ($DF94).\n2. If the text has a colon, what comes before it is a user number 0-15 and/or a drive letter\n   A-P (PARSE_PREFIX); spaces around them are skipped.\n3. The name (up to 8 characters) and the type (up to 3, after a dot) go into bytes 1-11,\n   padded with spaces; a '*' fills the rest of its field with '?'. No text, or nothing after\n   the colon, gives 11 '?'.\n4. A field ends at a control character, a space or one of BAD_NAME_CHARS; after the name\n   only a dot and the type may follow, perhaps after spaces.\nExit: carry set on success; carry clear for a bad name (a field too long, a name starting\nwith a dot, a bad prefix, or other text after the name or type).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "2898": {"comment":"HL = the record's drive (+$21)"},
        "2902": {"comment":"Default drive into it"},
        "2907": {"comment":"Default user number into byte 0"},
        "2910": {"comment":"Into byte 0"},
        "2911": {"comment":"First character after spaces"},
        "2914": {"comment":"No text: all wildcards"},
        "2916": {"comment":"E = the first character"},
        "2917": {"comment":"Keep the text's start"},
        "2918": {"synopsis":"Looks for a colon anywhere in the text.","comment":"Colon?"},
        "2920": {"comment":"Carry set: a character"},
        "2921": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "2923": {"comment":"Next character; more text?"},
        "2926": {"comment":"More: test it"},
        "2928": {"synopsis":"Back at the text's start: with a colon, parses the prefix first.","comment":"Back to the start of the text"},
        "2929": {"comment":"A = the first character"},
        "2930": {"comment":"No colon: the whole text is the name"},
        "2932": {"comment":"User number and/or drive letter"},
        "2935": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "2936": {"comment":"Next character after spaces"},
        "2939": {"comment":"Text ends there: error"},
        "2940": {"comment":"Must be the colon"},
        "2942": {"comment":"Not a colon: error"},
        "2943": {"comment":"Character after the colon"},
        "2946": {"comment":"There is one: parse the name"},
        "2948": {"synopsis":"No name: 11 wildcards.","comment":"Point at the name field"},
        "2949": {"comment":"11 wildcard bytes"},
        "2951": {"comment":"Success"},
        "2952": {"comment":"Fill and return"},
        "2954": {"synopsis":"Parses the name, then the dot and the type.","comment":"Point at the name field"},
        "2955": {"comment":"Name starting with a dot? Error"},
        "2957": {"comment":"Return: carry clear"},
        "2958": {"comment":"Up to 8 name characters"},
        "2960": {"comment":"Parse them"},
        "2963": {"comment":"Stopped at a character?"},
        "2964": {"comment":"Then up to 3 type characters"},
        "2966": {"comment":"No: pad the type with spaces"},
        "2968": {"comment":"Is it a dot?"},
        "2970": {"comment":"No: error"},
        "2971": {"comment":"Character after the dot"},
        "2974": {"comment":"None: the type is blank"},
        "2976": {"synopsis":"Copies characters from HL into the field at BC (E characters at most), then pads it with\nspaces (PARSE_FIELD_PAD).\nExit: carry set when the text ended; carry clear and A = the character that ended the field;\na field too long returns at once with carry clear."},
        "2977": {"comment":"Control character?"},
        "2979": {"comment":"Or one of the bad characters?"},
        "2982": {"comment":"Look it up"},
        "2986": {"comment":"Yes: the field ends here"},
        "2988": {"comment":"Count it"},
        "2989": {"comment":"Field too long: error"},
        "2990": {"comment":"Star fills the rest with wildcards"},
        "2992": {"comment":"Fill with '?', E becomes 0"},
        "2995": {"comment":"Store the character"},
        "2997": {"comment":"Next character; not a space?"},
        "3000": {"comment":"Not a space: next character"},
        "3002": {"comment":"Space: on to the next character"},
        "3005": {"synopsis":"Pads the rest of the field with spaces and turns the carry round: set when the text ended."},
        "3006": {"comment":"Pad the rest of the field with spaces"},
        "3008": {"comment":"Fill with A"},
        "3012": {"comment":"Carry set if the text ended"},
        "3014": {"synopsis":"Fills the E bytes from BC with '?'.","comment":"A = the wildcard"},
        "3016": {"synopsis":"Fills E bytes from BC with A; BC ends after them and E is 0.","comment":"E = 0?"},
        "3017": {"synopsis":"One byte."},
        "3018": {"comment":"Done?"},
        "3019": {"comment":"Store A, step on"},
        "3023": {"synopsis":"Steps to the next character, then past any spaces (SKIP_SPACES).","comment":"Step to the next character"},
        "3026": {"comment":"End of the text?"},
        "3027": {"synopsis":"Skips spaces from the character at HL.\nExit: carry set, A = the character (upper case, bit 7 dropped) and HL on it; carry clear at\nthe end of the text.","comment":"Is the character a space?"},
        "3030": {"synopsis":"A space: step past it.","comment":"No: done"},
        "3031": {"comment":"Step past the space"},
        "3034": {"comment":"Another character: test it"},
        "3037": {"synopsis":"Steps HL to the next character of the name text, unless it is on the $FF that ends it, then\nreads it (THIS_CHAR).","comment":"End marker?"},
        "3038": {"comment":"Is it $FF?"},
        "3040": {"comment":"Yes: stay on it"},
        "3041": {"comment":"Next character"},
        "3042": {"synopsis":"Reads the character at HL of the name text.\nExit: carry clear and Z at the $FF end; otherwise carry set, A = the character with bit 7\ndropped and in upper case, and Z for a space.","comment":"End marker?"},
        "3043": {"comment":"Is it $FF?"},
        "3045": {"comment":"Yes: carry clear, Z"},
        "3046": {"comment":"Drop bit 7, make it upper case"},
        "3048": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "3051": {"comment":"Z for a space"},
        "3053": {"comment":"Carry set: a character"},
        "3055": {"synopsis":"Looks for A in the character list at HL, which ends before a byte with bit 7 set.\nExit: carry set if it is there.","comment":"This bad character?"},
        "3056": {"comment":"Yes: carry set"},
        "3058": {"comment":"Next one; bit 7 ends the list"},
        "3059": {"comment":"End of the list?"},
        "3061": {"comment":"No: next"},
        "3063": {"comment":"Not found: carry clear"},
        "3065": {"synopsis":"The characters that end a name or type field (PARSE_FIELD, through BAD_CHAR_TEST): ! & ( ) +\n, - . / : ; < = > [ \\ ] |, then $80, which ends the list."},
        "3084": {"synopsis":"Logs in the drive named in byte $21 of record BC (DRIVE_LOGIN).\nEntry: BC = the file record.\nExit: as DRIVE_LOGIN.","comment":"A = the record's drive letter (+$21)"},
        "3085": {"comment":"HL = byte $21"},
        "3091": {"synopsis":"Selects drive A and, if it is not logged in yet, reads its directory to set up its tables.\nAlso from $05D2 and $08FF.\n1. DRIVE_SELECT selects the drive and points IX at its table.\n2. If bit 0 of (IX+$1B) is set the drive is logged in already. Otherwise the block bitmap is\n   cleared with the directory's blocks marked (BITMAP_INIT), bit 1 of (IX+$1B) is set so\n   that DIR_SECTOR_READ stores the directory sectors' sums, the free-entry count (IX+$22) is\n   cleared and every directory entry is read (LOGIN_ONE): free ones are counted, the blocks\n   of the others are marked used.\n3. (IX+$24), where later searches stop, becomes the number of the last entry in use; bit 0\n   of (IX+$1B) is set and bit 1 cleared.\nEntry: A = the drive letter.\nExit: carry set and IX = the drive's table; carry clear and A = the error otherwise.\nChanges: AF, IX.","comment":"Select the drive; IX = its table"},
        "3094": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "3095": {"comment":"Logged in already?"},
        "3099": {"comment":"Yes: success"},
        "3100": {"comment":"Return: logged in"},
        "3104": {"comment":"Clear the bitmap, mark the directory's blocks"},
        "3107": {"comment":"Logging in: store the sector sums"},
        "3111": {"comment":"No free entries counted yet"},
        "3112": {"comment":"Free entries count = 0"},
        "3118": {"comment":"Search every entry"},
        "3121": {"comment":"BC = the last entry in use so far"},
        "3124": {"comment":"Callback for each entry"},
        "3127": {"comment":"Run it over the directory"},
        "3130": {"comment":"Later searches stop at the last used entry"},
        "3139": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "3140": {"comment":"Logged in"},
        "3144": {"comment":"No longer logging in"},
        "3149": {"synopsis":"DIR_SCAN callback for DRIVE_LOGIN (LOGIN_ENTRY); always goes on.","comment":"Account for this entry"},
        "3152": {"comment":"A = $FF, NZ: next entry"},
        "3155": {"synopsis":"Counts a free entry ($E5 in byte 0) with DIR_FREE_INC; for any other entry sets BC to its\nnumber and marks its blocks used (ENTRY_BLOCKS_SET).\nEntry: HL = the entry, DE = its number.","comment":"Free entry ($E5)?"},
        "3156": {"comment":"Free?"},
        "3158": {"comment":"Yes: count it"},
        "3161": {"comment":"BC = this entry's number: last used so far"},
        "3163": {"comment":"Mark its blocks used"},
        "3165": {"comment":"Mark it"},
        "3168": {"synopsis":"Sets the search limit (IX+$24) to the directory's last entry number (IX+$07), so that\nDIR_SCAN reads every entry.","comment":"Search limit = the directory's last entry"},
        "3181": {"synopsis":"Makes record BC hold the directory entry that covers the file's 128-byte record DE, for\nreading (from $12F6). If the held entry covers it (EXTENT_HOLD_TEST) nothing is done;\notherwise\nthe held one is written back if changed (EXTENT_STORE) and EXTENT_LOAD reads the right one.\nEntry: BC = the file record, DE = the record number, IX = the drive's table.\nExit: carry set on success; carry clear and A = $19 when the entry is not in the directory\n(bit 2 of byte $22 then set), or another error.","comment":"Record DE in the held entry?"},
        "3184": {"comment":"Yes: nothing to do"},
        "3186": {"comment":"Write the held entry back if changed"},
        "3190": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "3191": {"synopsis":"Puts the extent bytes for the wanted record into record BC (H into byte $0C, L into byte\n$0E, as EXTENT_HOLDS returns them), clears bytes $0F-$1F (the record count and the block\nnumbers) and reads the matching entry from the directory (EXTENT_FIND). If it is not found,\nsets bit 2 of byte $22.\nExit: carry set if found; carry clear and A = $19 when it is not there, or another error.","comment":"DE = the extent bytes for record DE"},
        "3192": {"comment":"HL = the record's extent number (+$0C)"},
        "3196": {"comment":"Into byte $0C"},
        "3197": {"comment":"Step to +$0E"},
        "3199": {"comment":"High extent byte"},
        "3200": {"comment":"17 bytes: record count and block numbers"},
        "3202": {"comment":"Clear them"},
        "3203": {"synopsis":"One byte."},
        "3208": {"comment":"Read the matching entry into the record"},
        "3211": {"comment":"Found: done"},
        "3212": {"comment":"Not there: flag bit 2 of +$22"},
        "3216": {"comment":"Bit 2: not on disk"},
        "3218": {"comment":"Carry clear: A = the error"},
        "3220": {"synopsis":"Makes record BC hold the directory entry that covers the file's 128-byte record DE, for\nwriting (from $12DD). Like EXTENT_FOR_READ, but an entry that is not in the directory is\nclaimed from the free entries (DIR_SLOT_CLAIM, error $1B when there are none).\nEntry: BC = the file record, DE = the record number, IX = the drive's table.\nExit: carry set on success; carry clear and A = the error otherwise.","comment":"Record DE in the held entry?"},
        "3223": {"comment":"No: change entry"},
        "3225": {"comment":"Entry still to be made (bit 2)?"},
        "3229": {"comment":"Bit 2 of the flags"},
        "3231": {"comment":"Yes: claim a free directory entry"},
        "3234": {"comment":"No: success"},
        "3236": {"synopsis":"Another entry: write the held one back first."},
        "3237": {"comment":"Write the held entry back if changed"},
        "3241": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "3242": {"synopsis":"Loads the entry with the extent bytes in H and L (EXTENT_LOAD), claiming a new one when it\nis not there. Also from $06C0 with HL = 0, the file's first entry.","comment":"Load the entry for record DE"},
        "3245": {"comment":"Found: done"},
        "3246": {"comment":"Error other than $19?"},
        "3248": {"comment":"Then return it, carry clear"},
        "3250": {"comment":"Return: the error"},
        "3251": {"comment":"Not there: claim a free directory entry"},
        "3254": {"synopsis":"Writes the entry held in record BC back to the directory as bits 0 (changed) and 1 (new) of\nthe record's byte $22 say:\n- neither: nothing;\n- bit 1 only (claimed but never changed): gives the free entry back (DIR_SLOT_RETURN);\n- both: finds a free slot (DIR_SLOT_FIND) and clears this entry's 10 bytes in the fourth\n  entry of its group when that one is marked $21 (ENTRY_STAMP_ADDR);\n- bit 0 only: finds the entry's slot (MATCH_EXTENT; error $20 if it is not there).\nThen the 32 bytes are copied into the slot, written to the sector buffer (DIR_ENTRY_WRITE),\nthe changed sectors are written (FLUSH_DRIVE) and bit 0 is cleared. Also from $0767.\nEntry: BC = the file record, IX = the drive's table.\nExit: carry set; carry clear and A = the error only when finding the slot failed (a failed\nwrite is not returned).","comment":"HL = the record's flags (+$22)"},
        "3258": {"comment":"Bit 0 changed, bit 1 new"},
        "3261": {"comment":"Neither: nothing to write"},
        "3262": {"comment":"Return: nothing to do"},
        "3263": {"comment":"New but unchanged?"},
        "3265": {"comment":"Yes: give the free entry back"},
        "3268": {"comment":"New and changed?"},
        "3270": {"comment":"Yes: find a free slot for it"},
        "3272": {"comment":"Find the held entry's slot on disk"},
        "3275": {"comment":"Search the directory"},
        "3278": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "3279": {"comment":"Not there: error $20"},
        "3282": {"comment":"Return: not found"},
        "3283": {"comment":"Copy the record into the slot"},
        "3285": {"synopsis":"A new entry: find a free slot for it.","comment":"Find a free directory slot"},
        "3288": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "3292": {"comment":"Group's fourth entry marked $21?"},
        "3295": {"comment":"No"},
        "3297": {"comment":"Clear this entry's 10 bytes there"},
        "3299": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Clear a byte"},
        "3304": {"synopsis":"Restores the registers."},
        "3307": {"synopsis":"Copies the record's 32-byte entry into the slot's copy at HL and writes it back.","comment":"Keep the entry number"},
        "3309": {"comment":"DE = the slot's copy, HL = the record"},
        "3310": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "3312": {"comment":"Copy the 32-byte entry"},
        "3319": {"comment":"Write the slot back to its sector buffer"},
        "3322": {"comment":"Then write the changed sectors"},
        "3325": {"comment":"Entry no longer changed"},
        "3329": {"comment":"Bit 0: unchanged now"},
        "3331": {"comment":"Success, even if writing failed"},
        "3333": {"synopsis":"Works out the extent bytes for the file's 128-byte record DE: L = DE / 4096, H = DE / 128\nwith the bits of the mask at (IX+$04) cleared. EXTENT_HOLD_TEST compares them with the entry\nheld in a file record; also called from $3910.\nEntry: DE = the record number, IX = the drive.\nExit: H, L the extent bytes; A = the bits outside the mask (NOT (IX+$04) AND $1F).\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "3334": {"comment":"B = the extent bits an entry stands for"},
        "3337": {"comment":"Complement the extent mask"},
        "3338": {"comment":"Low 5 bits"},
        "3341": {"comment":"L = record DE / 4096"},
        "3342": {"comment":"A = D / 16"},
        "3348": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "3349": {"comment":"A = record DE / 128"},
        "3350": {"comment":"Bit 7 of E into carry"},
        "3353": {"comment":"Keep the masked bits"},
        "3354": {"comment":"H = the extent number for record DE"},
        "3355": {"comment":"A = the mask"},
        "3358": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the directory entry held in record BC covers the file's 128-byte record DE:\nits byte $0E must equal DE / 4096, and its byte $0C must equal DE / 128 in the bits outside\nthe mask at (IX+$04) (EXTENT_HOLDS works them out). Called from $0C6D and $0C94.\nExit: carry set if it does; H = DE / 128 with the masked bits cleared, L = DE / 4096 (the\nextent bytes for record DE).\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"H, L = the extent bytes, A = the mask"},
        "3361": {"comment":"Registers kept"},
        "3364": {"comment":"DE = the extent bytes for record DE"},
        "3365": {"comment":"HL = the record's high extent byte (+$0E)"},
        "3368": {"comment":"HL = byte $0E"},
        "3369": {"comment":"B = the bits outside the mask"},
        "3370": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "3371": {"comment":"Compare with L"},
        "3372": {"comment":"No"},
        "3374": {"comment":"HL = the record's extent number (+$0C)"},
        "3375": {"comment":"Back to byte $0C"},
        "3376": {"comment":"The same in the masked bits?"},
        "3377": {"comment":"Compare with H"},
        "3379": {"comment":"No"},
        "3381": {"comment":"Yes: carry set"},
        "3382": {"synopsis":"Restores the registers."},
        "3386": {"synopsis":"Looks for the directory entry with record BC's byte 0, name and extent bytes (MATCH_EXTENT)\nand copies it into the record. Also from $06CC.\nExit: carry set if found; carry clear and A = $19 if not, or another error.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"Callback: same name and extent"},
        "3389": {"comment":"Search the directory"},
        "3392": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "3393": {"comment":"Not found: error $19"},
        "3394": {"comment":"Error $19"},
        "3398": {"comment":"DE = the record"},
        "3400": {"comment":"Copy the entry into it"},
        "3403": {"comment":"Copy the entry"},
        "3406": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3408": {"synopsis":"Compare callback: the entry at HL matches record BC if byte 0 is the same, the name and type\nmatch (NAME_MATCH), byte $0C is the same outside the mask at (IX+$04) and byte $0E is the\nsame; $FF in the record's byte $0C or $0E matches any.\nExit: carry set; Z for a match."},
        "3411": {"comment":"Same byte 0?"},
        "3413": {"comment":"And the same name and type?"},
        "3416": {"comment":"No"},
        "3418": {"comment":"Any extent ($FF)?"},
        "3419": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "3420": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "3422": {"comment":"B = the extent bits an entry stands for"},
        "3425": {"comment":"Complement of the mask"},
        "3427": {"comment":"Same extent number in those bits?"},
        "3430": {"comment":"No"},
        "3432": {"synopsis":"The extent number agrees: test byte $0E.","comment":"Step to the high extent bytes"},
        "3436": {"comment":"Any ($FF)?"},
        "3437": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "3439": {"comment":"Yes: Z"},
        "3441": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "3442": {"synopsis":"Z for a match.","comment":"Z for a match"},
        "3444": {"synopsis":"Compare callback: the entry at HL matches record BC if byte 0 is the same apart from bit 4\nand the name and type match, with '?' wildcards (NAME_MATCH).\nExit: carry set; Z for a match.","comment":"Same byte 0, bit 4 ignored?"},
        "3448": {"comment":"Compare the name"},
        "3450": {"synopsis":"Compare callback like MATCH_WILD, but byte 0 must be the same in all bits. Also from $05AB,\n$064D and $0897.","comment":"Same byte 0?"},
        "3452": {"synopsis":"Byte 0 compared (Z if it agrees): now the name."},
        "3455": {"comment":"Yes: compare the name and type"},
        "3458": {"synopsis":"Restores the registers; carry set, Z for a match."},
        "3461": {"comment":"Carry set; Z for a match"},
        "3463": {"synopsis":"Compares the 11 name and type bytes of record BC with those of the entry at HL; a '?' in the\nrecord matches anything and bit 7 is ignored.\nExit: Z if they match.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "3464": {"comment":"DE = the record's name"},
        "3467": {"comment":"HL = the entry's name"},
        "3468": {"comment":"11 name and type bytes"},
        "3470": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Wildcard?"},
        "3471": {"comment":"Wildcard?"},
        "3473": {"comment":"Yes: it matches anything"},
        "3475": {"comment":"Same letter, bit 7 ignored?"},
        "3476": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "3478": {"comment":"No: NZ"},
        "3480": {"synopsis":"Next pair.","comment":"Next pair"},
        "3484": {"synopsis":"Restores BC."},
        "3486": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine at HL for each directory entry in turn, from entry 0 up to the search\nlimit at (IX+$24). Every 16th entry reads the next directory sector (DIR_SECTOR_READ); each\nentry is copied from the sector buffer to $DFA2 in bank 7, and the callback runs with HL =\n$DFA2, DE = the entry number, and BC and IX as given. The callback returns carry clear to\nstop with an error, carry set and Z to stop, carry set and NZ to go on. CACHE_DROP_DIR is\ncalled\nbefore the scan.\nEntry: HL = the callback, BC = for the callback (a file record), IX = the drive's table.\nExit: carry clear and A = the error; carry set and Z when the callback stopped, DE = that\nentry's number; carry set and NZ when every entry was seen. HL = $DFA2.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL; $DFA0, $DFA2-$DFC1.","comment":"Keep the callback"},
        "3489": {"comment":"Before the scan"},
        "3492": {"comment":"DE = entry 0"},
        "3495": {"comment":"Keep AF"},
        "3496": {"synopsis":"One entry; a new sector every 16 entries.","comment":"First entry of a sector?"},
        "3497": {"comment":"Within the sector"},
        "3499": {"comment":"No: the sector is in the buffer"},
        "3501": {"comment":"Drop the bank"},
        "3502": {"comment":"Read the sector; A = its buffer's bank"},
        "3505": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "3506": {"comment":"Keep the bank"},
        "3507": {"synopsis":"Copies the entry to $DFA2 and calls the callback.","comment":"A = the buffer's bank"},
        "3514": {"comment":"C = the buffer's bank, B = bank 7"},
        "3515": {"comment":"Into bank 7"},
        "3517": {"comment":"HL = the entry, DE = $DFA2"},
        "3518": {"comment":"HL = the entry in the buffer"},
        "3521": {"comment":"Copy the 32 bytes into $DFA2"},
        "3529": {"comment":"Call the callback with HL = $DFA2"},
        "3534": {"comment":"Callback error: stop"},
        "3536": {"comment":"Callback asked to stop"},
        "3538": {"comment":"Next entry; past the search limit?"},
        "3541": {"comment":"No: next entry"},
        "3543": {"synopsis":"HL = $DFA2; drops the saved bank.","comment":"HL = the copy of the entry"},
        "3546": {"comment":"Drop the saved bank"},
        "3547": {"comment":"Drop the saved AF"},
        "3549": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the callback kept at $DFA0, with HL = $DFA2.","comment":"HL = the callback"},
        "3552": {"comment":"Return into it"},
        "3553": {"comment":"With HL = the entry's copy"},
        "3557": {"synopsis":"Next entry number; carry set when it is past the search limit (IX+$24).","comment":"Next entry"},
        "3558": {"comment":"Past the search limit (+$24)?"},
        "3567": {"synopsis":"Reads the directory sector that holds entry DE into a buffer (SECTOR_BUF_READ) and checks\nit. For a\nsector in the checked part of the directory (DIR_SECTOR_SUM), the sum of its bytes must\nequal the one stored for it or, while logging in (bit 1 of (IX+$1B)), is stored. When the\nsums differ, CACHE_DROP_CLEAN is called and error $08 is reported for the drive through\nCDV_ASK_RETRY; Z from\nit reads the sector again.\nEntry: DE = the entry number, IX = the drive's table.\nExit: carry set, A = the buffer's bank and HL = the buffer; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "3571": {"comment":"Shift right 2"},
        "3574": {"comment":"DE = the sector holding it"},
        "3577": {"synopsis":"Reads the sector and checks its sum.","comment":"Read the sector; HL = buffer, A = bank"},
        "3580": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "3582": {"comment":"B = the bank"},
        "3584": {"comment":"Sum the sector, if it is checked"},
        "3587": {"comment":"Not checked: done"},
        "3589": {"comment":"Logging in?"},
        "3593": {"comment":"No"},
        "3595": {"comment":"Yes: store the sum"},
        "3596": {"synopsis":"Compares the sum with the stored one.","comment":"Same as the stored sum?"},
        "3598": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "3600": {"comment":"Sums differ"},
        "3603": {"comment":"Error $08 for the drive"},
        "3605": {"comment":"Report it"},
        "3608": {"comment":"NZ: give up"},
        "3610": {"comment":"Read the sector again"},
        "3611": {"comment":"Again"},
        "3613": {"synopsis":"Carry set: A = the buffer's bank."},
        "3614": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "3616": {"comment":"A = the buffer's bank"},
        "3617": {"synopsis":"Restores DE and BC."},
        "3620": {"synopsis":"Copies the entry at $DFA2 (bank 7) into its slot in the buffer of its directory sector,\nwhich SECTOR_DIRTY marks as changed, and updates the sector's stored sum if it is a checked\none.\nThe sector itself is written later (FLUSH_DRIVE).\nEntry: DE = the entry number, IX = the drive's table.\nExit: carry set on success; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF."},
        "3623": {"comment":"C = the entry number"},
        "3626": {"comment":"Shift right 2"},
        "3629": {"comment":"DE = the sector holding it"},
        "3633": {"comment":"Get its buffer for changing"},
        "3636": {"comment":"Get the buffer for changing"},
