        "4191": {"synopsis":"Returns the file pointer of file B (DOS_JUMPS $0133): the 24-bit offset of the next byte to\nread or write, bytes $26-$28 of its file record.\nEntry: B = the file number, 0-15.\nExit: carry set, E:HL = the pointer, D = 0, BC = the file record; carry clear and A = the\nerror ($15 bad number, $1D not open).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Is file B open?"},
        "4194": {"comment":"Error?"},
