        "4474": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "4475": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4476": {"synopsis":"Restores DE and HL."},
        "4479": {"synopsis":"Writes DE bytes from memory at HL in RAM bank C to file B at its pointer (DOS_JUMPS $0115);\nthe pointer moves on and the length follows it (LEN_EXTEND).\nEntry: B = the file number, C = the bank, HL = the address, DE = the count.\nExit: carry set on success; carry clear, A = the error ($1D not open for writing, or a disk\nerror) and DE = the bytes not written.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; $DFD0-$DFD2.","comment":"$DFD0 = the bank the bytes come from"},
        "4480": {"comment":"$DFD1 = their address"},
        "4483": {"comment":"$DFD1 = the address of the next byte to write"},
        "4486": {"comment":"BC = file B's record; open for writing?"},
        "4489": {"comment":"No: the error"},
        "4490": {"comment":"HL = the end of the source"},
        "4491": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "4492": {"comment":"Write the bytes"},
        "4495": {"comment":"Length raised to the pointer if it passed it"},
        "4498": {"comment":"HL = the end again"},
        "4499": {"comment":"All written"},
        "4500": {"comment":"Keep the error"},
        "4501": {"comment":"DE = the next byte not written"},
        "4505": {"comment":"DE = the end minus it: the bytes not written"},
        "4509": {"comment":"Error back"},
        "4511": {"synopsis":"Writes DE bytes from the caller's memory ($DFD0 the bank, $DFD1 the address) to file record\nBC at its pointer:\n1. Single bytes up to the next 128-byte record boundary.\n2. Whole records, copied straight into the record's buffer (WRITE_WHOLE_REC), while 128 or\n   more are left.\n3. The rest byte by byte.\n$DFD1 moves on past every byte written.\nEntry: BC = the file record, DE = the count (1 or more).\nExit: carry set when all are written; otherwise carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"DE = bytes left - 1: Z after the last one"},
        "4512": {"synopsis":"One byte while the pointer is inside a record (WRITE_BYTES).","comment":"HL = the pointer's low byte"},
        "4516": {"comment":"Pointer at a record boundary?"},
        "4521": {"comment":"No: write one byte"},
        "4524": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4525": {"comment":"All written"},
        "4526": {"comment":"Until the boundary"},
        "4528": {"synopsis":"One whole record while 128 bytes or more are left (WRITE_BYTES).","comment":"128 bytes or more left?"},
        "4532": {"comment":"No: the rest one at a time"},
        "4534": {"comment":"Yes: copy a whole record"},
        "4537": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4538": {"comment":"All written"},
        "4539": {"comment":"Another record"},
        "4541": {"synopsis":"One byte of the last part record (WRITE_BYTES).","comment":"Write one byte"},
        "4544": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4545": {"comment":"All written"},
        "4546": {"comment":"Next one"},
        "4548": {"synopsis":"Writes the next byte of the caller's memory (bank $DFD0, address $DFD1) to file record BC\n(PUT_FILE_BYTE) and moves $DFD1 on.\nEntry: BC = the file record, DE = bytes left - 1.\nExit: carry set, DE one less, Z when that was the last byte; or carry clear and A = the\nerror.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"A = the caller's bank"},
        "4551": {"comment":"HL = the next source byte"},
        "4554": {"comment":"Page the caller's bank in"},
        "4557": {"comment":"L = the byte"},
        "4558": {"comment":"Previous bank back"},
        "4561": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "4562": {"comment":"Write it to the file"},
        "4565": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4566": {"comment":"Source address one on"},
        "4573": {"comment":"Was it the last byte?"},
        "4575": {"comment":"One fewer to go"},
        "4576": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4578": {"synopsis":"Copies 128 bytes from the caller's memory (bank $DFD0, address $DFD1) into the buffer of the\n128-byte record at the file pointer, marks the record written to (flags bit 4) and moves\nboth the pointer and $DFD1 on by 128.\nEntry: BC = the file record, its pointer at a record boundary; DE = bytes left - 1 (127 or\nmore).\nExit: carry set, DE 128 less, Z when nothing is left; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"Keep the count"},
        "4579": {"comment":"Map the pointer's record for writing"},
        "4582": {"comment":"Count back"},
        "4583": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4584": {"comment":"Flags: the record written to (bit 4)"},
        "4590": {"comment":"Keep the count"},
        "4591": {"comment":"Pointer 128 on"},
        "4594": {"comment":"DE = the record's address in its buffer"},
        "4598": {"comment":"E = its low byte"},
        "4600": {"comment":"D = its high byte"},
        "4601": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's bank"},
        "4602": {"comment":"Keep the file record"},
        "4603": {"comment":"B = the buffer's bank: the destination"},
        "4604": {"comment":"C = the caller's bank: the source"},
        "4608": {"comment":"HL = the source"},
        "4611": {"comment":"128 bytes"},
        "4615": {"comment":"Copy them across the banks"},
        "4618": {"comment":"File record back"},
        "4619": {"comment":"Source address past them"},
        "4622": {"comment":"Count back"},
        "4623": {"comment":"Count 127 less; the DEC makes it 128"},
        "4628": {"comment":"Nothing left?"},
        "4630": {"comment":"One less"},
        "4631": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4633": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $011B) Writes one byte to an open file at its pointer and moves the pointer on,\nraising the file's length when the pointer passes it.\nEntry: B = the file number (0-15), C = the byte.\nExit: carry set on success; otherwise carry clear and A = the error ($15 for a file number\nover 15, $1D when the file is not open for writing).\nChanges: AF, BC (left pointing at the file's record), DE, HL.","comment":"E = the byte"},
        "4634": {"comment":"BC = file B's record; open for writing?"},
        "4637": {"comment":"No: the error"},
        "4638": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "4639": {"comment":"Write it"},
        "4642": {"comment":"Length raised to the pointer if it passed it"},
        "4646": {"synopsis":"Writes A to file record BC at its pointer: maps the pointer's record for writing unless it\nis mapped already (flags bit 5), stores the byte in the record's buffer, marks the record\nwritten to (bit 4) and moves the pointer one on.\nEntry: A = the byte, BC = the file record.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Keep HL and DE"},
        "4648": {"comment":"E = the byte"},
        "4649": {"comment":"HL = the flags"},
        "4653": {"comment":"Pointer's record mapped (bit 5)?"},
        "4657": {"comment":"No: map it for writing"},
        "4659": {"comment":"Map the pointer's record"},
        "4662": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "4664": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4666": {"synopsis":"Stores the byte in the mapped record (PUT_FILE_BYTE).","comment":"The record written to"},
        "4668": {"comment":"A = the byte's offset in the record"},
        "4675": {"comment":"Plus the record's address in the buffer"},
        "4679": {"comment":"Keep the byte"},
        "4680": {"comment":"DE = the byte's address in the buffer"},
        "4682": {"comment":"Carry into the high byte"},
        "4686": {"comment":"A = the buffer's bank"},
        "4688": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "4689": {"comment":"E = the byte"},
        "4690": {"comment":"Page the buffer in"},
        "4693": {"comment":"Store the byte"},
        "4694": {"comment":"Previous bank back"},
        "4697": {"comment":"Pointer one on"},
        "4700": {"synopsis":"HL and DE back (PUT_FILE_BYTE).","comment":"DE back"},
        "4702": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4703": {"synopsis":"Checks the sum byte of a file's first 128-byte record: byte 127 must equal the low byte of\nthe sum of bytes 0-126. Leaves the pointer at 0.\nEntry: BC = the file record.\nExit: carry set, Z on a match and NZ otherwise; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"E = the sum, D = byte 127"},
        "4706": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4707": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "4709": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4711": {"synopsis":"Stores the sum of bytes 0-126 of a file's first 128-byte record in its byte 127, then sets\nthe pointer to 128 and raises the file's length to at least 128.\nEntry: BC = the file record.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"E = the sum, HL = byte 127, A = the bank"},
        "4714": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4715": {"comment":"Page the buffer in"},
        "4718": {"comment":"Byte 127 = the sum"},
        "4719": {"comment":"Previous bank back"},
        "4722": {"comment":"Pointer 0 + 128"},
        "4725": {"comment":"Length at least the pointer"},
        "4728": {"synopsis":"Sets the pointer of file record BC to 0, maps record 0 for reading unless it is the mapped\none already (flags bit 5), and sums its bytes 0-126.\nEntry: BC = the file record.\nExit: carry set, E = the low byte of the sum, D = byte 127, HL = the address of byte 127 in\nthe buffer, A = the buffer's bank; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"Pointer = 0"},
        "4735": {"comment":"HL = the flags"},
        "4739": {"comment":"Pointer's record mapped (bit 5)?"},
        "4743": {"comment":"No: map record 0 for reading"},
        "4746": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4747": {"synopsis":"Sums the mapped record 0 (HDR_SUM).","comment":"HL = the record's address in its buffer"},
        "4751": {"comment":"HL = the address's low byte"},
        "4753": {"comment":"D = its high byte"},
        "4755": {"comment":"A = the buffer's bank"},
        "4756": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "4757": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "4758": {"comment":"Page it in"},
        "4761": {"comment":"Keep the previous bank"},
        "4762": {"comment":"Sum = 0"},
        "4763": {"comment":"127 bytes"},
        "4765": {"synopsis":"One byte into the sum (HDR_SUM).","comment":"Add one"},
        "4766": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "4767": {"comment":"Bytes left?"},
        "4770": {"comment":"E = the sum"},
        "4771": {"comment":"D = byte 127"},
        "4772": {"comment":"Previous bank back"},
        "4776": {"comment":"A = the buffer's bank"},
        "4777": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4779": {"synopsis":"Lets go of the record mapped in file record BC: when one is mapped (flags bit 3) and has\nbeen written to (bit 4), the cached sector holding it is marked changed (SECTOR_DIRTY); then\nflags bits 3, 4 and 5 are cleared.\nEntry: BC = the file record.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error ($21 when the sector is no longer in the\ncache).\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Keep HL"},
        "4780": {"comment":"HL = the flags"},
        "4784": {"comment":"A record mapped (bit 3)?"},
        "4788": {"comment":"Written to (bit 4)?"},
        "4792": {"comment":"Keep the pointers"},
        "4794": {"comment":"DE = the record's sector"},
        "4798": {"comment":"E = the sector's low byte"},
        "4800": {"comment":"D = its high byte"},
        "4801": {"comment":"Mark the cached sector changed"},
        "4804": {"comment":"Pointers back"},
        "4806": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4808": {"synopsis":"Clears flags bits 3, 4 and 5: nothing mapped (REC_RELEASE).","comment":"Bits 3, 4 and 5 off"},
        "4812": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4813": {"synopsis":"HL back (REC_RELEASE)."},
        "4815": {"synopsis":"Maps the 128-byte record at the pointer of file record BC for writing: through MAP_REC with\nMAP_WRITE_FILE as the handler, or with MAP_RAW_SECTOR when byte 0 of the file record is $22.\nEntry: BC = the file record.\nExit: as MAP_REC.","comment":"Byte 0 of the file record $22?"},
        "4818": {"comment":"No: the file handler"},
        "4823": {"comment":"Yes: the raw-sector handler"},
        "4828": {"synopsis":"Handler for MAP_REC, writing to a file: finds the directory entry covering record DE, making\none if there is none (EXTENT_FOR_WRITE), gives the record a sector buffer (REC_SECT_WRITE,\nallocating a\nblock if it has none), and when the record lies at or past the entry's recorded end, extends\nthe entry to it (ENTRY_EXTEND).\nEntry: DE = the record number, BC = the file record, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set, HL = the record's address in its buffer, A = the buffer's bank, DE = the\nsector; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"Keep the record number"},
        "4829": {"comment":"Directory entry covering it, made if needed"},
        "4832": {"comment":"Record number back"},
        "4833": {"comment":"Give the record a sector buffer"},
        "4836": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4837": {"comment":"Keep the results"},
        "4840": {"comment":"DE = the record number"},
        "4843": {"comment":"Before the entry's recorded end?"},
        "4846": {"comment":"No: extend the entry to it"},
        "4849": {"comment":"Results back"},
        "4850": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "4852": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4853": {"synopsis":"Handler for MAP_REC, reading a file: finds the directory entry covering record DE\n(EXTENT_FOR_READ),\nthen the buffer of the sector holding the record, read from the disk if it is not cached\n(REC_SECT_READ).\nEntry: DE = the record number, BC = the file record, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set, HL = the record's address in its buffer, A = the buffer's bank, DE = the\nsector; or carry clear and A = the error ($19 past the end of the file).","comment":"Keep the record number"},
        "4854": {"comment":"Directory entry covering it"},
        "4857": {"comment":"Record number back"},
        "4858": {"comment":"The record's sector buffer"},
        "4862": {"synopsis":"Maps the 128-byte record at the pointer of file record BC for reading: through MAP_REC with\nMAP_READ_FILE as the handler, or with MAP_RAW_SECTOR when byte 0 of the file record is $22.\nEntry: BC = the file record.\nExit: as MAP_REC.","comment":"Byte 0 of the file record $22?"},
        "4865": {"comment":"No: the file handler"},
        "4870": {"comment":"Yes: the raw-sector handler"},
        "4873": {"synopsis":"Maps the 128-byte record at the file pointer into a sector buffer, so that bytes $29-$2F of\nfile record BC describe it: $29-$2A the record number, $2B-$2C the sector, $2D-$2E the\nrecord's address in the buffer, $2F the buffer's bank.\n1. The record number is the pointer divided by 128 (PTR_TO_RECNO; error $22 if it does not\n   fit 16 bits).\n2. If that record is the mapped one already (flags bit 3 and the same number), only the\n   flags are set.\n3. Otherwise the file's drive is selected and logged in (FCB_DRIVE_LOGIN), the record mapped\n   before is\n   let go (REC_RELEASE), and the handler in HL finds the record's buffer.\n4. Flags bits 3 and 5 are set: a record is mapped, and it is the pointer's.\nEntry: BC = the file record, HL = the handler (MAP_WRITE_FILE, MAP_READ_FILE or\nMAP_RAW_SECTOR).\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX (the drive).","comment":"DE = the pointer's record number"},
        "4876": {"comment":"Too far"},
        "4877": {"comment":"Keep the handler"},
        "4878": {"comment":"HL = the flags"},
        "4882": {"comment":"A record mapped (bit 3)?"},
        "4884": {"comment":"Handler back"},
        "4885": {"comment":"No"},
        "4887": {"comment":"Keep the handler"},
        "4888": {"comment":"HL = the pointer's record number"},
        "4889": {"comment":"DE = the mapped record's number"},
        "4892": {"comment":"DE = the pointer's again"},
        "4893": {"comment":"The same record?"},
        "4896": {"comment":"Handler back"},
        "4897": {"comment":"Yes: only the flags"},
        "4899": {"synopsis":"Maps a record other than the one mapped (MAP_REC).","comment":"Select the file's drive, logged in"},
        "4902": {"comment":"Let go of the record mapped before"},
        "4905": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4906": {"comment":"Keep the handler"},
        "4907": {"comment":"$29-$2A = the record number"},
        "4911": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "4913": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "4914": {"comment":"Handler back"},
        "4915": {"comment":"DE = the record number"},
        "4918": {"comment":"Call the handler"},
        "4921": {"comment":"Error"},
        "4922": {"comment":"Keep the buffer address"},
        "4923": {"comment":"$2B-$2C = the sector"},
        "4927": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "4929": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "4930": {"comment":"DE = the buffer address"},
        "4931": {"comment":"$2D-$2E = it"},
        "4932": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "4934": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "4935": {"comment":"$2F = the buffer's bank"},
        "4937": {"synopsis":"Sets flags bits 3 and 5: a record is mapped, and it is the pointer's (MAP_REC).","comment":"HL = the flags"},
        "4941": {"comment":"Bits 3 and 5 on"},
        "4945": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4947": {"synopsis":"DE = the number of the record mapped in file record BC (bytes $29-$2A).\nChanges: DE."},
        "4948": {"comment":"HL = the record number's place"},
        "4952": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "4954": {"comment":"D = the high byte"},
        "4955": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4957": {"synopsis":"DE = the 128-byte record number of the pointer of file record BC (bytes $26-$28 divided by\n128).\nExit: carry set, or carry clear when the pointer is $800000 or more; A = $22 either way.\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"Keep HL"},
        "4958": {"comment":"HL = the pointer"},
        "4962": {"comment":"A = its low byte"},
        "4964": {"comment":"DE = its high two"},
        "4967": {"comment":"Shift the 24 bits left once: HL = pointer / 128"},
        "4971": {"comment":"DE = the record number"},
        "4972": {"comment":"Carry = below $800000"},
        "4973": {"comment":"The error if not"},
        "4977": {"synopsis":"Finds the sector buffer for writing record DE of file record BC. A record whose place in the\ndirectory entry has no block gets a new one from the drive's free blocks (BLOCK_ALLOCATE),\nstored in\nthe entry's block list (one byte per block, or two when IX+$06 is not 0). The sector is read\nfrom the disk first, unless the block is new, or the record starts a sector and lies at or\npast the entry's recorded end (REC_IN_ENTRY).\nEntry: DE = the record number, BC = the file record, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set, HL = the record's address in its buffer, A = the buffer's bank, DE = the\nsector; or carry clear and A = the error ($1A when the disk is full).","comment":"Keep the record number"},
        "4978": {"comment":"HL = its block, DE = its offset in the block"},
        "4981": {"comment":"Offset to the stack, DE = the record number"},
        "4984": {"comment":"Has it a block?"},
        "4986": {"comment":"No: DE = a new block"},
        "4989": {"comment":"Disk full"},
        "4991": {"comment":"Into the entry's block list"},
        "4992": {"comment":"Two-byte block numbers?"},
        "4998": {"comment":"Yes: the high byte too"},
        "5000": {"synopsis":"A new block: its sectors are not read (REC_SECT_WRITE).","comment":"HL = the block"},
        "5001": {"comment":"Carry clear: no read"},
        "5003": {"synopsis":"The record has a block (REC_SECT_WRITE).","comment":"Record at the start of a sector?"},
        "5006": {"comment":"Carry: read the sector"},
        "5007": {"comment":"Yes: read only if before the entry's end"},
        "5010": {"synopsis":"Turns carry into A: $FF to read the sector, 0 not to (REC_SECT_WRITE).","comment":"A = $FF: read it; 0: no need"},
        "5011": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5012": {"synopsis":"Finds the sector and its buffer (REC_SECT_WRITE).","comment":"DE = the offset in the block"},
        "5013": {"comment":"DE = the sector, HL = the offset in it"},
        "5016": {"comment":"Keep the offset"},
        "5017": {"comment":"Get the sector's buffer"},
        "5020": {"comment":"HL = the record's address in it"},
        "5022": {"synopsis":"Gets the buffer of sector DE: with Z set without reading the sector (SECTOR_BUF_NEW),\notherwise read from the disk if it is not cached (SECTOR_BUF_READ).","comment":"No read wanted?"},
        "5025": {"comment":"Read it if not cached"},
        "5028": {"synopsis":"Finds the buffer of the sector holding record DE of file record BC for reading, reading the\nsector if it is not cached.\nEntry: DE = the record number, BC = the file record holding the directory entry, IX = the\ndrive.\nExit: carry set, HL = the record's address in the buffer, A = the buffer's bank, DE = the\nsector; or carry clear and A = the error ($19 when the record has no block or lies at or\npast the entry's recorded end).","comment":"Keep the record number"},
        "5029": {"comment":"HL = its block, DE = its offset in the block"},
        "5032": {"comment":"Offset to the stack, DE = the record number"},
        "5035": {"comment":"Has a block: before the entry's end?"},
        "5038": {"comment":"DE = the offset in the block"},
        "5039": {"comment":"DE = the sector, HL = the offset in it"},
        "5042": {"synopsis":"With carry set, gets the buffer of sector DE (read if it is not cached) and makes HL the\naddress of the record in it; shared with MAP_RAW_SECTOR.","comment":"Keep the offset"},
        "5043": {"comment":"HL = the sector's buffer, A = its bank"},
        "5046": {"synopsis":"HL = the buffer plus the offset, DE = the sector (REC_SECT_WRITE, REC_BUF_FETCH).","comment":"DE = the buffer, HL = the sector"},
        "5047": {"comment":"Sector to the stack, HL = the offset"},
        "5048": {"comment":"Keep the bank and the flags"},
        "5049": {"comment":"HL = the record's address in the buffer"},
        "5051": {"comment":"DE = the sector"},
        "5053": {"synopsis":"Finds the disk sector holding a byte of a block: the block's first record (block number\ntimes 2 to the power IX+$02) becomes its first sector (REC_TO_SECTOR), and the byte offset /\n512 is added.\nEntry: HL = the block number, DE = the byte offset within the block, IX = the drive.\nExit: DE = the sector, HL = the offset within that 512-byte sector.\nChanges: DE, HL.","comment":"Keep BC and AF"},
        "5055": {"comment":"DE = the block, HL = the offset"},
        "5056": {"comment":"A = the records per block, as a shift"},
        "5064": {"comment":"DE = the block's first sector"},
        "5067": {"comment":"HL = that sector, DE = the offset"},
        "5068": {"comment":"B = the offset's high byte"},
        "5069": {"comment":"DE = the offset within a 512-byte sector"},
        "5073": {"comment":"DE = the first sector, HL = that offset"},
        "5074": {"comment":"A = the offset's high byte, bit 0 cleared"},
        "5075": {"comment":"A = the offset / 512: the sector in the block"},
        "5076": {"comment":"DE = the block's first sector + that"},
        "5077": {"comment":"E = the low byte"},
        "5078": {"comment":"Carry into the high byte"},
        "5081": {"comment":"BC and AF back"},
        "5084": {"synopsis":"Looks up the block holding record DE in the directory entry kept in file record BC: bytes\n$10-$1F hold sixteen one-byte block numbers, or eight two-byte ones when IX+$06 is not 0.\nEntry: DE = the record number, BC = the file record, IX = the drive.\nExit: DE = the record's byte offset within its block; carry set and HL = the block number,\nor carry clear, A = $19 and HL = the address of the empty place in the block list.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"Keep BC"},
        "5085": {"comment":"HL = the file record"},
        "5087": {"comment":"A = the record's place in its block"},
        "5091": {"comment":"BC = that x 128: the byte offset"},
        "5092": {"comment":"B = the place / 2"},
        "5095": {"comment":"Bit 0 of the place to bit 7"},
        "5096": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "5097": {"comment":"A = the records per block, as a shift"},
        "5100": {"comment":"E = the record's block index"},
        "5103": {"comment":"Only the low byte counts"},
        "5105": {"comment":"Two-byte block numbers?"},
        "5109": {"comment":"A = the block index"},
        "5110": {"comment":"No"},
        "5112": {"comment":"Yes: place $11 + 2 x (index mod 8)"},
        "5114": {"comment":"x 2"},
        "5115": {"comment":"Place $11 + it: the high byte"},
        "5118": {"comment":"HL = the high byte's place"},
        "5119": {"comment":"D = the high byte"},
        "5120": {"comment":"HL = the low byte's place"},
        "5121": {"comment":"E = the low byte"},
        "5123": {"synopsis":"One-byte block numbers: place $10 + (index mod 16) (REC_BLOCK).","comment":"Index mod 16"},
        "5125": {"comment":"Place $10 + it"},
        "5128": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "5129": {"synopsis":"Reads the low byte and tests the block number (REC_BLOCK).","comment":"E = the low byte"},
        "5130": {"comment":"Any block?"},
        "5132": {"comment":"The error if not"},
        "5134": {"comment":"No block"},
        "5136": {"comment":"HL = the block"},
        "5137": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5138": {"synopsis":"DE = the offset in the block (REC_BLOCK).","comment":"DE = the byte offset in the block"},
        "5140": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "5142": {"synopsis":"Extends the directory entry kept in file record BC to end at record DE: byte $0F (the\nrecords in the entry) = (DE mod 128) + 1, byte $0C = (DE / 128) mod 32, and flags bit 0 is\nset (the entry has changed).\nEntry: DE = the record number, BC = the file record.\nExit: carry set.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Keep HL"},
        "5143": {"comment":"A = (record mod 128) + 1"},
        "5147": {"comment":"Byte $0F = it"},
        "5152": {"comment":"A = (record / 128) mod 32"},
        "5153": {"comment":"Carry = record bit 7"},
        "5154": {"comment":"A = record bits 7-14, shifted"},
        "5156": {"comment":"Mod 32"},
        "5158": {"comment":"Byte $0C = it"},
        "5161": {"comment":"Byte $0C = it"},
        "5162": {"comment":"Flags: the entry changed (bit 0)"},
        "5168": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5171": {"synopsis":"Is record DE before the end recorded by the directory entry in file record BC\n(ENTRY_REC_COUNT)?\nEntry: DE = the record number, BC = the file record.\nExit: carry set when it is; carry clear with A = $19 when it is at or past the end, or A =\n$22 when the count does not fit 16 bits.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Keep DE and HL"},
        "5173": {"comment":"HL = the records up to the entry's end"},
        "5176": {"comment":"More than 16 bits?"},
        "5177": {"comment":"The error if so"},
        "5181": {"comment":"Record below the count?"},
        "5184": {"comment":"The error if not"},
        "5186": {"synopsis":"HL and DE back (REC_IN_ENTRY)."},
        "5187": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "5189": {"synopsis":"Counts the records up to the end of the directory entry kept in file record BC: byte $0E x\n4096 + byte $0C x 128 + byte $0F (at most 128).\nEntry: BC = the file record.\nExit: HL = the count's low 16 bits, A = the bits above them.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"Keep DE"},
        "5190": {"comment":"D = byte $0C"},
        "5195": {"comment":"DE = byte $0C x 128"},
        "5201": {"comment":"A = byte $0F, the records in the entry"},
        "5204": {"comment":"A = byte $0F"},
        "5205": {"comment":"128 or more?"},
        "5209": {"comment":"Yes: 128"},
        "5211": {"synopsis":"Adds the records and byte $0E's part (ENTRY_REC_COUNT).","comment":"DE = DE + A"},
        "5213": {"comment":"Carry into D"},
        "5215": {"comment":"HL = byte $0E x 16"},
        "5216": {"comment":"L = byte $0E"},
        "5219": {"comment":"x 16"},
        "5223": {"comment":"Added to D; A = the carry out"},
        "5225": {"comment":"A = the carry out"},
        "5227": {"comment":"HL = the count"},
        "5228": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "5230": {"synopsis":"Handler for MAP_REC when the file record is a whole-disk one (byte 0 = $22), for reading and\nwriting: record DE is the disk's 128-byte record DE counted from track 0, four to a sector,\nand its sector is read if it is not cached. Error $19 when the sector lies past the disk's\nend: the records of all IX+$05-$06 + 1 blocks plus the reserved tracks.\nEntry: DE = the record number, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set, HL = the record's address in its buffer, A = the buffer's bank, DE = the\nsector; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"H = record mod 4"},
        "5234": {"comment":"HL = that x 128: the offset in the sector"},
        "5240": {"comment":"DE = record / 4: the sector"},
        "5245": {"comment":"Keep both"},
        "5247": {"comment":"HL = the sector"},
        "5248": {"comment":"A = the records per block, as a shift"},
        "5251": {"comment":"DE = the number of blocks"},
        "5263": {"comment":"DE = the sector past the disk's end"},
        "5266": {"comment":"Sector before it?"},
        "5269": {"comment":"DE = the sector"},
        "5270": {"comment":"HL = the offset in it"},
        "5271": {"comment":"The error if not"},
        "5273": {"comment":"Buffer and record address"},
        "5276": {"synopsis":"DE = the 512-byte buffers of the sector cache: D = the first buffer number given to it, E =\nhow many it took ($E290-$E291, set by CACHE_BUILD).\nChanges: DE.","comment":"E = buffers taken, D = the first"},
        "5281": {"synopsis":"Writes back every changed cached sector (CACHE_FLUSH_ALL), then builds the sector cache\nafresh from buffers D onwards (CACHE_BUILD).\nEntry: D = the first buffer, E = the number of buffers.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"Write back all changed sectors"},
        "5284": {"comment":"Error"},
        "5285": {"synopsis":"Builds the sector cache: an empty in-use list (head at $E292) and a free list (head at\n$E294) of up to 16 entries of 11 bytes from $DFE0. The first entry's buffer is $E090 in RAM\nbank 7; the others take the 512-byte buffers D, D+1, ... (at most E of them), BLOCK_ADDRESS\ngiving\neach one's address and bank.\nAn entry holds: +$00-$01 the next entry (0 at the end), +$02 bit 0 set when changed,\n+$03-$04 the BC given when it was marked changed (a file record), +$05 the drive letter,\n+$06-$07 the sector, +$08-$09 the buffer's address, +$0A its bank.\n$E291 = D, $E290 = the number of buffers taken.\nEntry: D = the first buffer, E = the number of buffers.\nExit: carry set.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"Both lists empty"},
        "5294": {"comment":"$E290 = none taken, $E291 = the first buffer"},
        "5298": {"comment":"IX = the first entry"},
        "5302": {"comment":"16 entries"},
        "5304": {"comment":"The first one's buffer: $E090 in bank 7"},
        "5306": {"comment":"HL = $E090"},
        "5309": {"comment":"Fill it in"},
        "5311": {"synopsis":"One more entry, with a buffer from the range (CACHE_BUILD).","comment":"Buffers left?"},
        "5313": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5314": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "5315": {"comment":"One more taken"},
        "5319": {"comment":"A = the buffer number"},
        "5320": {"comment":"D = the next one"},
        "5321": {"comment":"One fewer left"},
        "5322": {"comment":"HL = its address, A = its bank"},
        "5325": {"synopsis":"Fills in entry IX and puts it at the head of the free list (CACHE_BUILD).","comment":"+$08-$09 = the buffer's address"},
        "5331": {"comment":"+$0A = its bank"},
        "5334": {"comment":"HL = the free list's head"},
        "5337": {"comment":"+$00-$01 = it"},
        "5343": {"comment":"The head = this entry"},
        "5347": {"comment":"Keep the buffer number"},
        "5348": {"comment":"IX = the next entry"},
        "5353": {"comment":"Buffer number back"},
        "5354": {"comment":"Next entry"},
        "5356": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5358": {"synopsis":"Looks for sector BC of drive IX in the in-use list of the sector cache.\nEntry: BC = the sector, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set, DE = the entry, HL = the address of the link that points to it; or carry\nclear and A = $21 when it is not cached.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"From the in-use list's head"},
        "5361": {"synopsis":"One entry of the in-use list (CACHE_FIND).","comment":"HL = the link"},
        "5362": {"comment":"DE = the entry; end of the list?"},
        "5365": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "5366": {"comment":"Not cached"},
        "5368": {"comment":"End: the error"},
        "5369": {"comment":"Keep the link"},
        "5370": {"comment":"HL = the entry's drive letter"},
        "5374": {"comment":"Drive IX's?"},
        "5378": {"comment":"No"},
        "5380": {"comment":"HL = its sector"},
        "5383": {"comment":"H = the high byte"},
        "5384": {"comment":"L = the low byte"},
        "5385": {"comment":"The sector in BC?"},
        "5388": {"synopsis":"Back to the entry, and on unless it matched (CACHE_FIND).","comment":"HL = the entry: its link"},
        "5389": {"comment":"Not this one: on"},
        "5391": {"comment":"Found"},
        "5393": {"synopsis":"Gets a cache entry for sector BC of drive IX: the head of the free list or, when that is\nempty, the last (least recently used) entry of the in-use list. That one is unmapped from\nthe file records (CACHE_UNMAP), written back if it is changed (with its drive's other\nchanged sectors, CACHE_FLUSH_IF) and moved to the free list. The entry is left at the head\nof the free list, set to the sector, not changed.\nEntry: BC = the sector, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set, DE = the entry, HL = $E294 (the link pointing to it); or carry clear and A\n= the error.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"A free entry?"},
        "5396": {"comment":"Yes: take it"},
        "5398": {"comment":"No: from the in-use list's head"},
        "5401": {"synopsis":"Walks to the last entry of the in-use list (CACHE_GET_FREE).","comment":"HL = the link"},
        "5402": {"comment":"DE = the entry; end of the list?"},
        "5405": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "5406": {"comment":"The error for an empty list"},
        "5408": {"comment":"Empty"},
        "5409": {"comment":"The last one?"},
        "5412": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5414": {"comment":"Unmap it from the file records"},
        "5417": {"comment":"Write back if it is changed"},
        "5420": {"comment":"Error"},
        "5421": {"comment":"Onto the free list"},
        "5424": {"synopsis":"Sets entry DE for sector BC of drive IX, not changed (CACHE_GET_FREE).","comment":"Keep HL"},
        "5425": {"comment":"HL = the entry's +$02"},
        "5429": {"comment":"+$02-$04 = 0: not changed, no file record"},
        "5430": {"comment":"+$02 = 0"},
        "5432": {"comment":"+$03 = 0"},
        "5434": {"comment":"+$04 = 0"},
        "5436": {"comment":"+$05 = the drive letter"},
        "5441": {"comment":"+$06-$07 = the sector"},
        "5443": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "5444": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5445": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5447": {"synopsis":"Passes the drive letter (D) and sector (HL) of cache entry DE to FLUSH_SECTOR_BUF, which\nmakes every\nopen file record mapped onto that sector let go of it.\nEntry: DE = the entry.\nChanges: AF; IX, HL, DE and BC are kept.","comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "5452": {"comment":"HL = the entry's +$05"},
        "5456": {"comment":"A = the drive letter"},
        "5458": {"comment":"DE = the sector"},
        "5461": {"comment":"HL = the sector"},
        "5462": {"comment":"D = the drive letter"},
        "5463": {"comment":"File records let go of it"},
        "5466": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "5469": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "5472": {"synopsis":"Gets the buffer holding sector DE of drive IX, reading the sector from the disk\n(CACHE_GET_FREE, SECTOR_READ_IN) when it is not cached; its entry goes to the head of the\nin-use list. On the RAM disk (IX+$1B bit 3) the sector is its own buffer (RAMDISK_SECTOR).\nEntry: DE = the sector, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set, HL = the buffer's address, A = its bank; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"RAM disk?"},
        "5479": {"comment":"Keep DE and BC"},
        "5481": {"comment":"BC = the sector"},
        "5483": {"comment":"Cached?"},
        "5486": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "5488": {"comment":"No: an entry for it"},
        "5491": {"comment":"Read the sector into it"},
        "5494": {"synopsis":"To the end shared with SECTOR_BUF_NEW (SECTOR_BUF_READ).","comment":"Move it to the front"},
        "5496": {"synopsis":"As SECTOR_BUF_READ, but a sector that is not cached gets a buffer without being read: for a\nsector about to be filled from scratch.\nEntry: DE = the sector, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set, HL = the buffer's address, A = its bank; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"RAM disk?"},
        "5503": {"comment":"Keep DE and BC"},
        "5505": {"comment":"BC = the sector"},
        "5507": {"comment":"Cached?"},
        "5510": {"comment":"No: an entry for it"},
        "5513": {"synopsis":"With carry set, moves entry DE to the head of the in-use list, then gives its buffer\n(SECTOR_BUF_READ, SECTOR_BUF_NEW).","comment":"Keep the result"},
        "5514": {"comment":"Entry to the head of the in-use list"},
        "5517": {"comment":"Result back"},
        "5518": {"comment":"Its buffer"},
        "5520": {"synopsis":"Marks cached sector DE of drive IX changed, keeping BC (the file record that changed it) in\nthe entry's +$03-$04. On the RAM disk only the buffer is given (RAMDISK_SECTOR).\nEntry: DE = the sector, BC = the file record, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set, HL = the buffer's address, A = its bank; or carry clear and A = $21 when\nthe sector is not cached.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"RAM disk?"},
        "5527": {"comment":"Keep DE and BC"},
        "5529": {"comment":"BC again for below"},
        "5530": {"comment":"BC = the sector"},
        "5532": {"comment":"Find its entry"},
        "5535": {"comment":"BC = the file record"},
        "5536": {"comment":"Not cached"},
        "5538": {"comment":"Keep HL"},
        "5539": {"comment":"+$02 bit 0: changed"},
        "5545": {"comment":"+$03-$04 = the file record"},
        "5547": {"comment":"+$04 = the high byte"},
        "5549": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5550": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5551": {"synopsis":"On success HL = the entry's buffer and A = its bank (SECTOR_BUF_READ, SECTOR_BUF_NEW,\nSECTOR_DIRTY).","comment":"Error?"},
        "5553": {"comment":"HL = the entry's +$08"},
        "5557": {"comment":"DE = the buffer's address"},
        "5559": {"comment":"D = the high byte"},
        "5561": {"comment":"A = its bank"},
        "5562": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "5563": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5564": {"synopsis":"BC and DE back (SECTOR_BUF_ADDR)."},
        "5566": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5567": {"synopsis":"If drive IX has not been used in the last 100 frames (DRIVE_RECENT), drops from the cache\nits unchanged sectors up to the last sector of the directory, so that the directory is read\nafresh.\nEntry: IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set.\nChanges: AF; HL, DE and BC are kept.","comment":"Used in the last 100 frames?"},
        "5570": {"comment":"Yes: keep everything"},
        "5571": {"comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "5574": {"comment":"DE = the directory entries: IX+$07-$08 + 1"},
        "5586": {"comment":"DE = the sector after the directory"},
        "5589": {"comment":"DE = its last sector"},
        "5590": {"comment":"Drop up to it"},
        "5592": {"synopsis":"Drops from the cache every unchanged sector of drive IX.\nEntry: IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set.\nChanges: AF; HL, DE and BC are kept.","comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "5595": {"comment":"Every sector"},
        "5598": {"synopsis":"Drops the unchanged cached sectors of drive IX numbered up to DE; every such sector, changed\nor not, is first unmapped from the file records (CACHE_UNMAP) (CACHE_DROP_DIR,\nCACHE_DROP_CLEAN).","comment":"BC = the highest sector"},
        "5600": {"comment":"From the in-use list's head"},
        "5603": {"synopsis":"On to the next entry (CACHE_DROP_UPTO).","comment":"HL = the entry: its link"},
        "5604": {"synopsis":"The entry after the link at HL (CACHE_DROP_UPTO).","comment":"DE = the entry; end of the list?"},
        "5607": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5609": {"comment":"Keep the link"},
        "5610": {"comment":"HL = the entry's drive letter"},
        "5614": {"comment":"Drive IX's?"},
        "5618": {"comment":"No: skip it"},
        "5620": {"comment":"Sector at most BC?"},
        "5626": {"comment":"No: skip it"},
        "5628": {"comment":"Unmap it from the file records"},
        "5631": {"comment":"HL = the entry's +$02"},
        "5632": {"comment":"Back to +$02"},
        "5636": {"comment":"Changed?"},
        "5638": {"comment":"Yes: keep it"},
        "5640": {"comment":"HL = the link"},
        "5642": {"comment":"Onto the free list"},
        "5645": {"comment":"HL = the link"},
        "5646": {"comment":"Same link: its new successor"},
        "5648": {"synopsis":"Entry kept: on along the list (CACHE_DROP_UPTO).","comment":"HL = the link"},
        "5649": {"comment":"On from this entry"},
        "5651": {"synopsis":"Drops every cached sector of drive IX, changed or not, onto the free list.\nEntry: IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set.\nChanges: AF; HL, DE and BC are kept.","comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "5654": {"comment":"From the in-use list's head"},
        "5657": {"synopsis":"On to the next entry (CACHE_DROP_DRIVE).","comment":"HL = the entry: its link"},
        "5658": {"synopsis":"The entry after the link at HL (CACHE_DROP_DRIVE).","comment":"DE = the entry; end of the list?"},
        "5661": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5663": {"comment":"Keep the link"},
        "5664": {"comment":"A = the entry's drive letter"},
        "5669": {"comment":"HL = the link"},
        "5670": {"comment":"Drive IX's?"},
        "5673": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5675": {"comment":"Yes: onto the free list"},
        "5680": {"comment":"Same link: its new successor"},
        "5682": {"synopsis":"Drops from the cache, without writing them back, every sector that file record BC marked\nchanged (+$03-$04 = BC).\nEntry: BC = the file record.\nExit: carry set.\nChanges: AF; HL, DE and BC are kept.","comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "5685": {"comment":"From the in-use list's head"},
        "5688": {"synopsis":"On to the next entry (CACHE_DROP_FILE).","comment":"HL = the entry: its link"},
        "5689": {"synopsis":"The entry after the link at HL (CACHE_DROP_FILE).","comment":"DE = the entry; end of the list?"},
        "5692": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5694": {"comment":"Keep the link"},
        "5695": {"comment":"HL = the entry's +$03-$04"},
        "5699": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "5701": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "5703": {"comment":"Changed by file record BC?"},
        "5706": {"comment":"HL = the link"},
        "5707": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5709": {"comment":"Yes: onto the free list"},
        "5714": {"comment":"Same link: its new successor"},
        "5716": {"synopsis":"BC, DE and HL back (CACHE_DROP_UPTO, CACHE_DROP_DRIVE, CACHE_DROP_FILE)."},
        "5719": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5720": {"synopsis":"If cache entry DE is changed, finds its drive from the letter at +$05 and writes back every\nchanged cached sector of that drive (FLUSH_DRIVE).\nEntry: DE = the entry.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF; IX and HL are kept.","comment":"Keep IX and HL"},
        "5723": {"comment":"HL = the entry's +$02"},
        "5727": {"comment":"Changed?"},
        "5729": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5730": {"comment":"No: nothing to do"},
        "5732": {"comment":"A = its drive letter"},
        "5735": {"comment":"A = +$05"},
        "5736": {"comment":"IX = that drive"},
        "5739": {"comment":"Write back its changed sectors"},
        "5742": {"synopsis":"HL and IX back (CACHE_FLUSH_IF)."},
        "5743": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "5746": {"synopsis":"Writes back every changed sector in the cache, drive by drive (CACHE_FLUSH_IF for each entry\nof the in-use list).\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, IX; HL and DE are kept.","comment":"Keep HL and DE"},
        "5748": {"comment":"From the in-use list's head"},
        "5751": {"synopsis":"One entry of the in-use list (CACHE_FLUSH_ALL).","comment":"HL = the entry: its link"},
        "5752": {"comment":"DE = the next entry; end of the list?"},
        "5755": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5757": {"comment":"Write back its drive if it is changed"},
        "5760": {"comment":"On unless an error"},
        "5762": {"synopsis":"DE and HL back (CACHE_FLUSH_ALL)."},
        "5763": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5765": {"synopsis":"Writes back every changed cached sector of drive IX, lowest sector number first, each one\nthen marked unchanged (SECTOR_FLUSH).\nEntry: IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF; HL, DE and BC are kept.","comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "5768": {"synopsis":"Finds and writes back the lowest changed sector left (FLUSH_DRIVE).","comment":"From the in-use list's head"},
        "5771": {"comment":"Any sector number"},
        "5774": {"comment":"A changed sector of the drive?"},
        "5777": {"comment":"None left"},
        "5779": {"synopsis":"Keeps the lowest found so far and looks on for a lower one (FLUSH_DRIVE).","comment":"Keep it"},
        "5780": {"comment":"One with a sector at most BC further on?"},
        "5783": {"comment":"None"},
        "5785": {"comment":"Yes: drop the one kept"},
        "5788": {"synopsis":"Writes back the lowest changed sector (FLUSH_DRIVE).","comment":"DE = the lowest"},
        "5789": {"comment":"Write it back"},
        "5792": {"comment":"Again for the next"},
        "5794": {"synopsis":"BC, DE and HL back (FLUSH_DRIVE)."},
        "5797": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5798": {"synopsis":"Searches the in-use list after entry DE (or from the head when DE = $E292) for a changed\nentry of drive IX whose sector is at most BC.\nEntry: DE = where to start, BC = the highest sector, IX = the drive.\nExit: Z at the end of the list; otherwise NZ, carry set, DE = the entry and BC = its sector.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL; BC when found.","comment":"HL = the entry: its link"},
        "5799": {"comment":"DE = the next entry; end of the list?"},
        "5802": {"comment":"Yes: Z"},
        "5803": {"comment":"HL = its +$02"},
        "5807": {"comment":"Changed?"},
        "5809": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5811": {"comment":"A = its drive letter"},
        "5815": {"comment":"Drive IX's?"},
        "5818": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5820": {"comment":"HL = its sector"},
        "5821": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "5823": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "5825": {"comment":"At most BC?"},
        "5829": {"comment":"Equal"},
        "5831": {"comment":"Above: on"},
        "5833": {"synopsis":"BC = the sector found (FIND_DIRTY_LE).","comment":"BC = the sector"},
        "5835": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "5836": {"comment":"A = $FF: NZ"},
        "5838": {"synopsis":"Writes the sector of cache entry DE to the disk (the drive's write routine, CALL_WRITE_VEC)\nand marks the entry unchanged (+$02 bit 0 and +$03-$04 cleared).\nEntry: DE = the entry, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"Keep the entry"},
        "5839": {"comment":"B, HL = the buffer; D, E = the track and sector"},
        "5842": {"comment":"Write it"},
        "5845": {"comment":"Entry back"},
        "5846": {"comment":"Error"},
        "5847": {"comment":"HL = its +$02"},
        "5851": {"comment":"Not changed"},
        "5853": {"comment":"+$03-$04 = 0: no file record"},
        "5854": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "5857": {"comment":"+$04 = 0"},
        "5858": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5860": {"synopsis":"Reads the sector of cache entry DE from the disk into its buffer (the drive's read routine,\nCALL_READ_VEC).\nEntry: DE = the entry, IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "5863": {"comment":"B, HL = the buffer; D, E = the track and sector"},
        "5866": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "5869": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "5872": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5873": {"synopsis":"Sets up a sector transfer for cache entry DE: B = its buffer's bank, HL = the buffer's\naddress, D = the track and E = the sector within the track (SECTOR_TO_TRACK).\nEntry: DE = the entry, IX = the drive.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = the entry's +$0A"},
        "5877": {"comment":"B = the buffer's bank"},
        "5878": {"comment":"DE = the buffer's address"},
        "5879": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "5881": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "5882": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "5883": {"comment":"DE = the sector"},
        "5884": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "5886": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "5887": {"comment":"D = the track, E = the sector in it"},
        "5890": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "5892": {"synopsis":"DE = the first entry of the cache's free list (head at $E294).\nExit: carry set, Z when the list is empty; HL = $E294.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = the free list's head"},
        "5895": {"synopsis":"DE = the entry the link at HL points to.\nExit: carry set, Z when it is 0 (the end of the list).\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"DE = the link"},
        "5898": {"comment":"HL back on its low byte"},
        "5899": {"comment":"Z if the end"},
        "5901": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "5903": {"synopsis":"Z when entry DE is the last of its list (its own link is 0).\nChanges: AF.","comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "5904": {"comment":"Its link 0?"},
        "5906": {"comment":"Or the high byte"},
        "5908": {"comment":"HL and DE back"},
        "5910": {"synopsis":"Takes entry DE out of its list (HL = the link pointing to it) and puts it at the head of the\nfree list ($E294).\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"Out of its list"},
        "5913": {"comment":"Onto the free list"},
        "5918": {"synopsis":"Takes entry DE out of its list (HL = the link pointing to it) and puts it at the head of the\nin-use list ($E292), the most recently used place.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"Out of its list"},
        "5921": {"comment":"Onto the in-use list"},
        "5924": {"synopsis":"Puts entry DE at the head of the list whose head is at HL (TO_FREE_LIST, TO_USED_LIST).","comment":"The entry's link = the old head"},
        "5925": {"comment":"Low byte to the entry"},
        "5928": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "5930": {"comment":"DE back on the entry"},
        "5931": {"comment":"The head = the entry"},
        "5933": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "5934": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5935": {"synopsis":"Unlinks entry DE: the link at HL takes the entry's own link.\nChanges: A, HL (one on).","comment":"The link = the entry's link"},
        "5939": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "5941": {"comment":"DE back on the entry"},
        "5943": {"synopsis":"Sets up drives A and B: notes A as the letter last used on unit 0 ($E3EA); copies\nDRIVE_A_TEMPL into drive A's parameter block from IX+$1B (block $E2C0) and enters drive A in\nthe drive table ($E2A0); copies DRIVE_B_TEMPL into drive B's (block $E32D) and enters drive\nB ($E2A2); sets drive B up as unit 1 (DRIVE_B_SET with C = 1). When unit 1 has a drive\n(UNIT1_PRESENT) it goes on at L3227, the target of $00F1 in JUMPS_00A0, with A = 3 and\nL = 'B'. Called from SETUP_ALL at $01C1 when a disk controller answers.\nExit: carry clear when unit 1 has no drive; otherwise as L3227.","comment":"'A': the letter last used on unit 0"},
        "5948": {"comment":"Drive A's template to $E2C0 + $1B"},
        "5957": {"comment":"21 bytes"},
        "5959": {"comment":"Drive A in the table"},
        "5965": {"comment":"Drive B's template to $E32D + $1B"},
        "5974": {"comment":"21 bytes"},
        "5976": {"comment":"Drive B in the table"},
        "5982": {"comment":"C = 1: unit 1"},
        "5984": {"comment":"Drive B set up (DRIVE_B_SET)"},
        "5987": {"comment":"A drive on unit 1?"},
        "5990": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "5991": {"comment":"A = 3, L = 'B' for L3227"},
        "5998": {"synopsis":"Template for drive A's parameter block from IX+$1B on (21 bytes, copied by DRIVES_AB_INIT):\n+$1B flags $04 (bit 2: DRIVE_WRITE_CHK checks the drive before writing), +$1C the letter\n'A', +$1D unit 0, +$1E-$25 zero (the FRAMES stamp of the last use at +$1E-$20, the open-file\ncount at +$21, counters), +$26 $E2F0 and +$28 $E300 (two work areas; BITMAP_ADDR reads\n+$28), then\nthe addresses of the routines that check the disk (+$2A, $1988), read a sector (+$2C, $197C)\nand write one (+$2E, $1982)."},
        "6019": {"synopsis":"Template for drive B's parameter block from IX+$1B on (21 bytes, copied by DRIVES_AB_INIT to\n$E348): as drive A's, with the letter 'B', unit 1 and the work areas $E35D and $E36D."},
        "6040": {"synopsis":"Sets up drive M's parameter block (block $E39A) from DRIVE_M_TEMPL, enters it in the drive\ntable ($E2B8, the entry for M), then makes the RAM disk in buffers H to H+L-1\n(RAMDISK_SETUP). Called from SETUP_ALL at $01CB.\nEntry: H = the first 512-byte buffer, L = the number of buffers.\nExit: carry set.","comment":"Keep the buffers"},
        "6041": {"comment":"Drive M's template to $E39A + $1B"},
        "6050": {"comment":"21 bytes"},
        "6052": {"comment":"Drive M in the table"},
        "6058": {"comment":"The buffers back"},
        "6059": {"comment":"The RAM disk made"},
        "6062": {"synopsis":"Template for drive M's parameter block from IX+$1B on (21 bytes, copied by DRIVE_M_INIT to\n$E3B5): flags $08 (bit 3: RAM disk), the letter 'M', unit $FF, zero up to +$27, +$28 $E3CA,\nand DRIVE_M_NOP as the routine for checking, reading and writing."},
        "6083": {"synopsis":"Drive M's routine for checking the disk and for reading and writing a sector: nothing to do,\nsince the RAM disk's sectors are their own buffers (RAMDISK_SECTOR).\nExit: carry set.","comment":"Success"},
        "6085": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0151) Finds the parameter block of the drive whose letter is in A (a-p taken as\nA-P).\nEntry: A = the drive letter.\nExit: carry set and IX = the drive's parameter block; carry clear with A = $15 for a letter\noutside A-P, or A = $16 and IX = 0 when the drive is not set up. HL = $E2A0, the drive\ntable.\nChanges: AF, HL, IX.","comment":"Upper case"},
        "6088": {"comment":"HL = the drive table"},
        "6091": {"synopsis":"Finds the parameter block of drive A in the table of 16 words at $E2A0 (A to P; 0 for a\ndrive not set up).\nEntry: A = the letter, in upper case.\nExit: as DRIVE_FIND; HL is kept.\nChanges: AF, IX.","comment":"A = 0 for 'A'"},
        "6093": {"comment":"Below 'A'?"},
        "6095": {"comment":"Past 'P'?"},
        "6099": {"comment":"Keep HL"},
        "6100": {"comment":"HL = the letter's word in the table"},
        "6101": {"comment":"Plus $E2A0"},
        "6104": {"comment":"Carry into the high byte"},
        "6108": {"comment":"HL = the parameter block"},
        "6110": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "6112": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "6115": {"comment":"Carry if it is not 0"},
        "6119": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6120": {"comment":"The error for a drive not set up"},
        "6123": {"synopsis":"Bad letter: A = $15, carry clear (DRIVE_FIND_UC).","comment":"The error"},
        "6125": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "6127": {"synopsis":"Selects drive A for use: finds its parameter block, logs it out if it has been idle\n(DRIVE_IDLE_OUT), and when it is not logged in (IX+$1B bit 0) runs its disk check\n(DRIVE_CHECK_DISK).\nEntry: A = the drive letter, in upper case.\nExit: carry set and IX = the parameter block; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, IX.","comment":"IX = the drive's block"},
        "6130": {"comment":"Error"},
        "6131": {"comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "6134": {"comment":"Log it out if idle"},
        "6137": {"comment":"Logged in?"},
        "6141": {"comment":"Success"},
        "6142": {"comment":"No: check the disk"},
        "6145": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "6147": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6149": {"synopsis":"Runs drive IX's disk check routine (CALL_CHECK_VEC) unless IX+$1A bit 7 is set.\nEntry: IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"IX+$1A bit 7 set?"},
        "6153": {"comment":"Yes: no check"},
        "6154": {"comment":"Check through the drive's routine"},
        "6157": {"synopsis":"Logs drive IX out (DRIVE_LOG_OUT) when it is logged in, has no open files and has not been\nused in the last 100 frames (DRIVE_RECENT, which also stamps it as used now).\nEntry: IX = the drive.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Logged in?"},
        "6161": {"comment":"No"},
        "6162": {"comment":"Any open files?"},
        "6166": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6167": {"comment":"Used in the last 100 frames?"},
        "6170": {"comment":"Yes: stay logged in"},
        "6171": {"synopsis":"Logs drive IX out: error $24 if it has open files (IX+$21); otherwise IX+$1B bit 0 is\ncleared and all its cached sectors, changed or not, are dropped (CACHE_DROP_DRIVE).\nEntry: IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = $24.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Open files?"},
        "6175": {"comment":"The error if so"},
        "6177": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6178": {"comment":"Not logged in"},
        "6182": {"comment":"Drop its cached sectors"},
        "6185": {"synopsis":"Was drive IX used in the last 100 frames? Compares FRAMES with the stamp at IX+$1E-$20 plus\n100, then stamps the drive with FRAMES. A drive with IX+$0C bit 7 set always counts as\nrecent, and is not stamped.\nEntry: IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set when recent.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"IX+$0C bit 7 set?"},
        "6189": {"comment":"Carry: recent"},
        "6190": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6191": {"comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "6194": {"comment":"P/V = the interrupt state"},
        "6196": {"comment":"Read FRAMES whole"},
        "6197": {"comment":"A = its low byte"},
        "6200": {"comment":"HL = its high two"},
        "6203": {"comment":"Interrupts were off?"},
        "6206": {"comment":"No: back on"},
        "6207": {"synopsis":"FRAMES read (DRIVE_RECENT).","comment":"B = FRAMES' low byte"},
        "6208": {"comment":"A = the stamp's low byte"},
        "6211": {"comment":"DE = its high two"},
        "6217": {"comment":"Plus 100"},
        "6222": {"synopsis":"Compares FRAMES with the stamp + 100 (DRIVE_RECENT).","comment":"C = the low byte"},
        "6223": {"comment":"FRAMES - (stamp + 100): carry if recent"},
        "6227": {"comment":"Keep the answer"},
        "6228": {"comment":"Stamp = FRAMES now"},
        "6231": {"comment":"P/V = the interrupt state"},
        "6233": {"comment":"Read FRAMES whole"},
        "6235": {"comment":"Stamp's low byte"},
        "6240": {"comment":"Middle byte"},
        "6245": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "6248": {"comment":"Interrupts were off?"},
        "6251": {"comment":"No: back on"},
        "6252": {"synopsis":"The answer and the registers back (DRIVE_RECENT).","comment":"The answer"},
        "6253": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "6257": {"synopsis":"DRIVE_WRITE_CHK, keeping HL, DE and BC.\nEntry: IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "6260": {"comment":"Check the drive"},
        "6263": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "6265": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6267": {"synopsis":"Before a write: for a drive with IX+$1B bit 2 set, selects its unit (DRIVE_UNIT), runs\nWRITE_ALLOWED (DOS_JUMPS $0172 target) and reads the drive's status byte (DRIVE_STATUS,\nDOS_JUMPS $017E target): error 0 when bit 5 is clear, error 1 when bit 6 is set.\nEntry: IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Checked before writes (IX+$1B bit 2)?"},
        "6271": {"comment":"Carry: fine"},
        "6272": {"comment":"No"},
        "6273": {"comment":"C = the unit"},
        "6276": {"comment":"WRITE_ALLOWED says yes?"},
        "6279": {"comment":"No: its error"},
        "6280": {"comment":"A = the drive's status byte"},
        "6283": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "6284": {"comment":"Bit 5 (ready)?"},
        "6286": {"comment":"No: error 0"},
        "6287": {"comment":"Bit 6 (write-protected)?"},
        "6289": {"comment":"The error if so"},
        "6291": {"comment":"Yes: error 1"},
        "6292": {"comment":"Success"},
        "6294": {"synopsis":"Adds the sectors of the reserved tracks to sector number DE: DE = DE + IX+$00-$01 / 4 x\nIX+$0D-$0E (the records per track over four, the sectors per track, times the reserved\ntracks). Called from $0738 and from the routines that read and write sectors.\nEntry: DE = the sector, IX = the drive.\nExit: DE = the sector counted from track 0.\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"Keep HL"},
        "6296": {"comment":"BC = the reserved tracks"},
        "6302": {"comment":"HL = the sector number"},
        "6303": {"comment":"DE = the records per track"},
        "6309": {"comment":"Divided by 4: sectors per track"},
        "6314": {"comment":"Add them BC times"},
        "6316": {"synopsis":"Adds one track's records (REC_TO_SECTOR).","comment":"One track more"},
        "6318": {"synopsis":"Tracks left? (REC_TO_SECTOR).","comment":"Tracks left?"},
        "6322": {"comment":"DE = the total"},
        "6323": {"comment":"HL and BC back"},
        "6326": {"synopsis":"Turns a sector number into a track and a sector within it, dividing DE by the sectors per\ntrack (IX+$00-$01 / 4). Called from $16FF and RAMDISK_SECTOR.\nEntry: DE = the sector, IX = the drive.\nExit: D = the track, E = the sector within the track.\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"HL and BC kept"},
        "6328": {"comment":"HL = the sector"},
        "6329": {"comment":"DE = the records per track"},
        "6335": {"comment":"Divided by 4: sectors per track"},
        "6340": {"comment":"BC = -1: tracks counted"},
        "6343": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "6344": {"synopsis":"One more track (SECTOR_TO_TRACK).","comment":"One track more"},
        "6345": {"comment":"Take a track's records"},
        "6347": {"comment":"Until it goes below 0"},
        "6349": {"comment":"HL = the records left over"},
        "6350": {"comment":"DE = them"},
        "6351": {"comment":"D = the track"},
        "6352": {"comment":"BC and HL back"},
        "6355": {"synopsis":"Calls drive IX's disk check routine (IX+$2A) through CALL_DRIVE_VEC, with DE = 0.","comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "6362": {"comment":"DE = 0"},
        "6367": {"synopsis":"Calls drive IX's sector read routine (IX+$2C) through CALL_DRIVE_VEC.","comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "6368": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "6371": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "6374": {"comment":"Call it"},
        "6376": {"synopsis":"Calls drive IX's sector write routine (IX+$2E) through CALL_DRIVE_VEC.","comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "6383": {"synopsis":"Calls the drive routine whose address is in HL (kept at $E3ED), with the routine's registers\nkept for each try; after a failure asks CDV_ASK_RETRY and calls it again while the answer is\nto retry.\nEntry: HL = the routine's address, the caller's HL on the stack; the routine's other\nregisters set.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The routine to call"},
        "6386": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6387": {"synopsis":"One try (CALL_DRIVE_VEC).","comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "6390": {"comment":"Call the routine"},
        "6393": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "6396": {"comment":"Success"},
        "6397": {"comment":"Try again?"},
        "6400": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6403": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the routine at $E3ED, HL kept.","comment":"Keep HL"},
        "6404": {"comment":"HL = the routine's address"},
        "6407": {"comment":"Address to the stack, HL back"},
        "6408": {"comment":"Jump to it"},
        "6409": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL: a CALL to here calls the routine at HL. Called from $1BED (the sector hook) and\n$1F45 (the operation of RUN_WITH_TRIES).","comment":"To HL"},
        "6410": {"synopsis":"Loads C with drive IX's unit (IX+$1D). On unit 0, when the drive's letter is not the one\nlast used on that unit ($E3EA), notes the new letter and calls DRIVE_SWAP_CALL, so that the\ndisk can be changed. Called from DRIVE_WRITE_CHK and the routines at $197C-$1988.\nEntry: IX = the drive.\nExit: C = the unit.\nChanges: AF, C.","comment":"Keep HL"},
        "6411": {"comment":"C = the unit"},
        "6414": {"comment":"Unit 0?"},
        "6416": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "6418": {"comment":"HL = the letter last used on unit 0"},
        "6421": {"comment":"This drive's letter the same?"},
        "6425": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "6427": {"comment":"No: note it"},
        "6428": {"comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "6432": {"comment":"Ask for the disk"},
        "6435": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "6437": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "6439": {"synopsis":"HL back (DRIVE_UNIT).","comment":"HL back"},
        "6441": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine at $E3EB (set by DRIVE_B_SET) with A = the drive letter and HL = the text\nMSG_INSERT_DISK makes at $DB29 from message 10 of DOS_MESSAGES, C being the letter.\nEntry: A = the drive letter.","comment":"Keep the letter"},
        "6442": {"comment":"C = the letter"},
        "6443": {"comment":"HL = message 10's text"},
        "6446": {"comment":"A = the letter"},
        "6447": {"comment":"Jump to the routine at $E3EB, HL kept"},
        "6448": {"comment":"HL = the routine's address"},
        "6451": {"comment":"Address to the stack, HL back"},
        "6452": {"comment":"Jump to it"},
        "6453": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0154) Sets up drive B (block $E32D) as unit C. With C = 0 drive B is unit 0,\nthe same drive as A, and HL is the routine called whenever the other letter is used on it\n(DRIVE_SWAP_CALL); with C not 0 there is no such routine.\n1. Drive B is logged out (DRIVE_LOG_OUT: error $24 if it has open files).\n2. $E3EB = HL (0 for C not 0); drive B's unit (IX+$1D) = C.\n3. When a disk controller answers (FDC_PRESENT) and C is not 0 but unit 1 has no drive\n(UNIT1_PRESENT), the unit becomes 0. The drive table is not changed.\nEntry: C = the unit, HL = the routine.\nExit: carry set and HL = the old routine; or carry clear and A = $24.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"IX = drive B's block"},
        "6457": {"comment":"Logged out (DRIVE_LOG_OUT)"},
        "6460": {"comment":"Error: files open"},
        "6461": {"comment":"Unit 0?"},
        "6465": {"comment":"No: no swap routine"},
        "6468": {"synopsis":"Stores the swap routine and sets drive B's unit (DRIVE_B_SET).","comment":"DE = the old routine"},
        "6472": {"comment":"The new one"},
        "6479": {"comment":"Its unit = C"},
        "6482": {"comment":"A disk controller?"},
        "6485": {"comment":"No: the unit stays"},
        "6487": {"comment":"Unit 0?"},
        "6489": {"comment":"Carry: nothing to test"},
        "6490": {"comment":"A drive on unit 1?"},
        "6493": {"comment":"Yes: the unit stays"},
        "6495": {"comment":"No: drive B shares unit 0"},
        "6499": {"synopsis":"Success; HL = the old routine (DRIVE_B_SET).","comment":"Success"},
        "6500": {"comment":"HL = the old routine"},
        "6502": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0160) Sets how many times RUN_WITH_TRIES and SEEK_TRACK_HL try: $E42D = A.\nEntry: A = the tries.","comment":"The tries"},
        "6506": {"synopsis":"Shows message 10 of COLOUR_MESSAGES, the request to put in the disk for drive C, through\nSHOW_MESSAGE, entered at $22C4 with A = 10 and NZ. Reached from $0005.\nEntry: C = the drive letter.\nExit: as SHOW_MESSAGE.","comment":"Message 10"},
        "6508": {"comment":"NZ for the other ROM"},
        "6509": {"comment":"Shown"},
        "6512": {"synopsis":"Unused: twelve bytes of $00."},
        "6524": {"synopsis":"Drive A's and B's sector read routine (+$2C): C = the unit (DRIVE_UNIT, which may ask for\nthe disk to be changed), then SECTOR_READ (DOS_JUMPS $0163 target).\nEntry: B = the buffer's bank, HL = its address, D = the track, E = the sector, IX = the\ndrive.","comment":"C = the unit"},
        "6527": {"comment":"Read the sector"},
        "6530": {"synopsis":"Drive A's and B's sector write routine (+$2E): C = the unit (DRIVE_UNIT), then SECTOR_WRITE\n(DOS_JUMPS $0166 target).\nEntry: B = the buffer's bank, HL = its address, D = the track, E = the sector, IX = the\ndrive.","comment":"C = the unit"},
        "6533": {"comment":"Write the sector"},
        "6536": {"synopsis":"Drive A's and B's disk check routine (+$2A): C = the unit (DRIVE_UNIT), then DISK_IDENTIFY\n(DOS_JUMPS $0175 target), which fills in the parameter block from the disk. Error 6 unless\nIX+$0F is 2, or when DE / 2 as DISK_IDENTIFY leaves it is 46 or more. IX+$0B-$0C (bit 7\naside) is then limited to $40.\nEntry: IX = the drive.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"C = the unit"},
        "6539": {"comment":"Read the disk's format"},
        "6542": {"comment":"Error"},
        "6543": {"comment":"IX+$0F 2?"},
        "6548": {"comment":"The error if not"},
        "6550": {"comment":"Not 2: error 6"},
        "6551": {"comment":"DE / 2 below 46?"},
        "6555": {"comment":"Minus 46"},
        "6559": {"comment":"Carry clear if not"},
        "6560": {"comment":"No: error 6"},
        "6561": {"comment":"DE = IX+$0B-$0C without bit 7"},
        "6567": {"comment":"Bit 7 aside"},
        "6570": {"comment":"Below $41?"},
        "6574": {"comment":"Carry if so"},
        "6575": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "6576": {"comment":"No: $40, bit 7 kept"},
        "6580": {"comment":"IX+$0C: only bit 7 kept"},
        "6587": {"comment":"High byte 0 apart from bit 7"},
        "6590": {"comment":"Success"},
        "6592": {"synopsis":"Reads DE bytes from file B at its pointer into memory at HL in RAM bank C (DOS_JUMPS $0112).\n1. $DFD0 = C, $DFD1 = HL; the file must be open for reading (FILE_READABLE).\n2. FILE_READ_SIZE compares the count with the bytes left before the file's length: when it\nfits all of it is read, otherwise the bytes left are read and error $19 follows.\n3. FILE_READ_DATA reads the bytes: 512 or more straight from the disk interface when L3886\naccepts the file, otherwise byte by byte to a 128-byte boundary (READ_ONE_BYTE), whole\nrecords (READ_ONE_RECORD) and the rest byte by byte.\nThe pointer moves on by the bytes read.\nEntry: B = the file number, C = the bank, HL = the address, DE = the count.\nExit: carry set on success; carry clear, A = the error ($19 at the length, $1D not open for\nreading, or a disk error) and DE = the bytes not read.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX; $DFD0-$DFD2.","comment":"The bank"},
        "6596": {"comment":"The address"},
        "6599": {"comment":"Open for reading?"},
        "6602": {"comment":"No"},
        "6603": {"comment":"HL = the end address"},
        "6605": {"comment":"Read"},
        "6609": {"comment":"Success"},
        "6610": {"comment":"Error kept"},
        "6611": {"comment":"DE = the end less $DFD1"},
        "6618": {"comment":"DE = the bytes not read"},
        "6621": {"synopsis":"Reads DE bytes of file record BC, or as many as are left before the file's length followed\nby\nerror $19: A:HL = the length (record + $23-$25) less the pointer (+$26-$28) less 1; at or\npast\nthe length error $19 at once (FILE_READ_EOF).\nEntry: BC = the record, DE = the count.\nExit: as FILE_READ_DATA; or carry clear and A = $19."},
        "6623": {"comment":"HL = the length (+$23)"},
        "6627": {"comment":"E, D, B = its three bytes"},
        "6633": {"comment":"Less the pointer (+$26) less 1"},
        "6644": {"comment":"A:HL = the bytes left less 1"},
        "6647": {"comment":"None left: error $19"},
        "6649": {"comment":"DE = the count less 1"},
        "6650": {"comment":"Fewer left than the count?"},
        "6653": {"comment":"...in the top byte too"},
        "6655": {"comment":"No: read them all"},
        "6657": {"comment":"Yes: DE = the bytes left less 1"},
        "6658": {"comment":"Read those"},
        "6661": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "6662": {"synopsis":"Error $19: the file ends.","comment":"Error $19"},
        "6664": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "6666": {"synopsis":"Reads DE + 1 bytes of file record BC to $DFD1 in bank $DFD0. With 512 or more, L3886 (A = 0,\nHL = $F516) is asked whether the file can be read straight from its drive; when it can\n(carry), the pointer at +$26-$28 moves on by them all, bit 5 of +$22 is cleared, and the\nbytes come from the interface: L2776 for each sector and L25B9 for each piece (FRD_SECTOR),\nthe unwanted bytes dropped (L27CB, L27D7). Otherwise FILE_READ_BYTES.\nEntry: BC = the record, DE = the count less 1.\nExit: carry set on success, $DFD1 past the bytes; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"DE = the count"},
        "6667": {"comment":"512 or more?"},
        "6670": {"comment":"No: through the records"},
        "6674": {"comment":"A = 0, HL = $F516"},
        "6678": {"comment":"Straight from the drive?"},
        "6683": {"comment":"No: through the records"},
        "6685": {"comment":"IX = $F518"},
        "6689": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "6690": {"comment":"The pointer (+$26) on by DE"},
        "6701": {"comment":"...its top byte"},
        "6706": {"comment":"Bit 5 of +$22 cleared"},
        "6712": {"comment":"HL = the word at $F516"},
        "6718": {"comment":"The first sector"},
        "6721": {"comment":"Bytes before the first dropped"},
        "6724": {"comment":"HL = the destination"},
        "6729": {"synopsis":"The next sector from the interface (L2776).","comment":"The next sector"},
        "6732": {"synopsis":"One piece of DE bytes into the destination, bank $DFD0 paged in, until the count is used up.","comment":"The bank paged in"},
        "6738": {"comment":"HL = the bytes left"},
        "6739": {"comment":"Fewer than a piece?"},
        "6742": {"comment":"Yes: the last piece"},
        "6744": {"comment":"HL = the destination"},
        "6745": {"comment":"The piece in"},
        "6748": {"comment":"Any left?"},
        "6752": {"comment":"Yes: the next sector"},
        "6754": {"comment":"Drop the count"},
        "6755": {"comment":"Done"},
        "6757": {"synopsis":"Reads through the file's records: single bytes (READ_ONE_BYTE) while the pointer is inside a\n128-byte record, each followed by a new start at FILE_READ_DATA; then whole records and the\nrest byte by byte.","comment":"DE = the count less 1"},
        "6758": {"comment":"Pointer inside a record?"},
        "6765": {"comment":"No: whole records"},
        "6767": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "6770": {"comment":"Error"},
        "6771": {"comment":"That was the last"},
        "6772": {"comment":"Again from the top"},
        "6775": {"synopsis":"Whole records while 128 bytes or more are left (READ_ONE_RECORD).","comment":"128 or more left?"},
        "6779": {"comment":"No: single bytes"},
        "6781": {"comment":"One record"},
        "6784": {"comment":"Error"},
        "6785": {"comment":"That was the last"},
        "6788": {"synopsis":"The rest byte by byte (READ_ONE_BYTE).","comment":"One byte"},
        "6791": {"comment":"Error"},
        "6792": {"comment":"That was the last"},
        "6795": {"synopsis":"The last piece: only the bytes still wanted are read in (L25B9) and the sector's other bytes\nare dropped (L27D7).","comment":"HL = the bytes left"},
        "6796": {"comment":"DE = them, HL = the piece"},
        "6798": {"comment":"HL = the bytes to drop"},
        "6800": {"comment":"HL = the destination"},
        "6801": {"comment":"The bytes left in"},
        "6804": {"comment":"DE = the bytes to drop"},
        "6805": {"comment":"Dropped"},
        "6808": {"synopsis":"$DFD1 = where the next byte would go; success.","comment":"The destination now"},
        "6811": {"comment":"Success"},
        "6813": {"synopsis":"After a disk error: turns the disk motor off at once (L3EE6, DOS_JUMPS $019C target) and\npasses the error and the drive letter to ASK_RETRY, which gives Z when the operation is to\nbe tried again.\nEntry: A = the error, IX = the drive.\nExit: Z to retry; A = the error.\nChanges: AF; IX, HL, DE and BC are kept.","comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "6818": {"comment":"Motor off now"},
        "6821": {"comment":"C = the drive letter"},
        "6824": {"comment":"Try again? (Z)"},
        "6827": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "6829": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6833": {"synopsis":"H = the RAM disk's first 512-byte buffer ($E3F4), L = its number of buffers ($E3F1 - $E3F4).\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"H = the first buffer"},
        "6837": {"comment":"L = the buffer after the last - the first"},
        "6840": {"comment":"Minus the first"},
        "6841": {"comment":"L = the count"},
        "6843": {"synopsis":"Makes the RAM disk afresh in the buffers given: when drive M (block $E39A) has a letter\n(IX+$1C) it is logged out first (DRIVE_LOG_OUT: error $24 if it has open files), then\nRAMDISK_SETUP. Called from $01FC.\nEntry: H = the first buffer, L = the number of buffers.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"IX = drive M's block"},
        "6847": {"comment":"Has it a letter?"},
        "6851": {"comment":"No: just make it"},
        "6853": {"comment":"Yes: log it out"},
        "6856": {"comment":"Error"},
        "6857": {"synopsis":"Makes the RAM disk, drive M, from the 512-byte buffers H to H+L-1:\n1. RAMDISK_SPEC is copied to $E3EF.\n2. With fewer than 4 buffers there is no RAM disk (RAMDISK_NONE, with IX = drive M's block).\n3. Otherwise $E3F1 (byte 2 of the copy) = H+L and $E3F4 (byte 5) = H, and every buffer is\n   filled with $E5.\n4. PARAMS_FROM_SPEC (DOS_JUMPS $018A target) builds drive M's parameter block at $E39A from\n   the copy; IX+$0B = 0, IX+$0C = $80 (bit 7: DRIVE_RECENT always true). The drive table\n   entry is DRIVE_M_INIT's.\nEvery track of the RAM disk is one sector and track n is buffer n; the first H tracks count\nas reserved, so its sectors are buffers H onwards (RAMDISK_SECTOR).\nEntry: H = the first buffer, L = the number of buffers.\nExit: carry set.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"Keep the buffers"},
        "6858": {"comment":"The format to $E3EF"},
        "6861": {"comment":"To $E3EF"},
        "6864": {"comment":"8 bytes"},
        "6869": {"comment":"D = the first buffer, E = how many"},
        "6870": {"comment":"Fewer than 4 buffers?"},
        "6873": {"comment":"Yes: no RAM disk"},
        "6875": {"comment":"$E3F1 = the buffer after the last"},
        "6879": {"comment":"$E3F4 = the first"},
        "6883": {"synopsis":"Fills one buffer with $E5 (RAMDISK_SETUP).","comment":"A = the buffer number"},
        "6884": {"comment":"Keep the counters"},
        "6885": {"comment":"HL = its address, A = its bank"},
        "6888": {"comment":"Page it in"},
        "6891": {"comment":"DE = HL + 1"},
        "6894": {"comment":"First byte $E5"},
        "6896": {"comment":"The other 511 likewise"},
        "6901": {"comment":"Previous bank back"},
        "6904": {"comment":"Counters back"},
        "6905": {"comment":"Next buffer"},
        "6906": {"comment":"Buffers left?"},
        "6909": {"comment":"IX = drive M's block"},
        "6913": {"comment":"Build it from the format"},
        "6919": {"comment":"IX+$0B-$0C = $8000"},
        "6929": {"synopsis":"No RAM disk: the letter at IX+$1C is taken and cleared, and that letter's entry in the drive\ntable ($E2A0 + 2 x (letter - A)) is cleared; nothing more when there was no letter.\nEntry: IX = drive M's block.\nExit: carry set.","comment":"A = the letter"},
        "6932": {"comment":"No letter now"},
        "6936": {"comment":"A capital"},
        "6939": {"comment":"Letter - A"},
        "6941": {"comment":"No letter: done"},
        "6942": {"comment":"DE = its number"},
        "6945": {"comment":"HL = its table entry"},
        "6950": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "6955": {"comment":"Success"},
        "6957": {"synopsis":"The RAM disk's format, 8 bytes copied to $E3EF by RAMDISK_SETUP and read by\nPARAMS_FROM_SPEC: byte 2 is\nreplaced by the buffer after the last and byte 5 by the first buffer (IX+$0D, the reserved\ntracks); byte 3 = 1 and byte 4 = 2 make the records per track (IX+$00) 1 x 2^2 = 4 and\nIX+$0F = 2; byte 6 = 3 gives IX+$02, 8 records to a block."},
        "6965": {"synopsis":"Gives the buffer of sector DE of the RAM disk: SECTOR_TO_TRACK turns DE into track D and\nsector E; with one sector to a track E must be 0, and the sector is buffer D, which must lie\nbelow $E3F1. Used for every sector of a drive with IX+$1B bit 3 set.\nEntry: DE = the sector, IX = drive M.\nExit: carry set, HL = the buffer's address, A = its bank; or carry clear and A = 2.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"Keep the sector"},
        "6966": {"comment":"D = the track, E = the sector in it"},
        "6969": {"comment":"Sector 0 of the track?"},
        "6971": {"comment":"No: error"},
        "6973": {"comment":"A = the track: the buffer"},
        "6974": {"comment":"Below the RAM disk's end?"},
        "6978": {"comment":"No: error"},
        "6980": {"comment":"HL = its address, A = its bank"},
        "6983": {"comment":"Success"},
        "6984": {"synopsis":"The sector back; error 2 unless carry is set (RAMDISK_SECTOR).","comment":"Sector back"},
        "6986": {"comment":"The error"},
        "6989": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $012A) Starts the program in the boot sector of the disk in drive A:\n1. Drive A is selected (DRIVE_SELECT), logged out (DRIVE_LOG_OUT: error $24 if it has open\n   files) and its sector 0 read into the cache (SECTOR_BUF_READ).\n2. The 512 bytes are summed: error $23 unless the low byte of the sum is 3.\n3. With interrupts off, the sector is copied to $FE00 in RAM bank 3, bank 3 is paged in at\n   $C000 and the five bytes at $1BA1 go to $FDFB; with SP = $FE00 they write 7 to port\n   $1FFD, leaving RAM in all four quarters with bank 3 at $C000, and jump to $FE10, byte $10\n   of the sector.\nExit (only on failure): carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"Drive A"},
        "6991": {"comment":"Select it"},
        "6994": {"comment":"Log it out: its cache dropped"},
        "6997": {"comment":"Sector 0"},
        "7000": {"comment":"HL = its buffer, A = the bank"},
        "7003": {"comment":"Error"},
        "7004": {"comment":"C = the bank"},
        "7005": {"comment":"Keep the buffer's address"},
        "7006": {"comment":"Page it in"},
        "7009": {"comment":"Keep the previous bank"},
        "7010": {"comment":"Sum 2 x 256 bytes"},
        "7014": {"synopsis":"One byte into the sum (BOOT_DISK).","comment":"Add one"},
        "7016": {"comment":"Next in this 256"},
        "7018": {"comment":"The second 256?"},
        "7021": {"comment":"E = the sum"},
        "7022": {"comment":"Previous bank back"},
        "7026": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "7027": {"comment":"Sum 3?"},
        "7030": {"comment":"The error if not"},
        "7032": {"comment":"No"},
        "7033": {"comment":"No interrupts from here on"},
        "7034": {"comment":"To $FE00 in bank 3"},
        "7039": {"comment":"IX = 512 bytes"},
        "7043": {"comment":"The sector to $FE00 in bank 3"},
        "7046": {"comment":"Bank 3 at $C000"},
        "7051": {"comment":"The 5-byte stub (BOOT_JUMP_STUB)"},
        "7054": {"comment":"...to $FDFB, just below the sector"},
        "7062": {"comment":"BC = port $1FFD for the stub"},
        "7065": {"comment":"The value it gets"},
        "7067": {"comment":"The stack below the boot code"},
        "7070": {"comment":"Into the stub: the OUT, then $FE10"},
        "7073": {"synopsis":"Five bytes the boot code at $1B4D copies to $FDFB in bank 3 and jumps to, with BC = $1FFD\nand A = 7: the OUT writes 7 to port $1FFD and the JP goes on at $FE10, 16 bytes into the\nboot sector copied to $FE00. They run only from that copy.","comment":"Port $1FFD = A"},
        "7075": {"comment":"Into the boot sector's code"},
        "7078": {"synopsis":"Builds the 765's FORMAT A TRACK command in the command block at $E400 (bank 7): the command\nbyte $0D with only the MF bit of the 765 flags (+$19 of the parameter block); the bank,\nbuffer, unit and head as CMD_HEAD_BUILD sets them; then N (the sector size code, +$0F), the\nsectors per track (+$13), the format gap (+$18) and the filler byte; 6 command bytes.\nEntry: IX = the parameter block, B = the bank and HL = the buffer of ID fields, C = the\nunit, D = the logical track, E = the filler byte.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"The 765 flags"},
        "7081": {"comment":"Only MF"},
        "7083": {"comment":"$0D: FORMAT A TRACK"},
        "7085": {"comment":"Bank, buffer, unit and head"},
        "7088": {"comment":"N = the sector size code"},
        "7091": {"comment":"The sectors per track"},
        "7094": {"comment":"Command bytes 3 and 4"},
        "7097": {"comment":"The filler byte"},
        "7098": {"comment":"The format gap"},
        "7101": {"comment":"Command bytes 5 and 6"},
        "7104": {"comment":"6 command bytes"},
        "7110": {"synopsis":"Builds the 765's SCAN EQUAL command ($11 with the 765 flags at +$19) for one sector, as\nSECTOR_CMD_BUILD does, with its last byte (STP) 1 in place of DTL.\nEntry and Changes: as SECTOR_CMD_BUILD.","comment":"The 765 flags"},
        "7113": {"comment":"$11: SCAN EQUAL"},
        "7115": {"comment":"The sector's command"},
        "7118": {"comment":"STP = 1"},
        "7121": {"synopsis":"Builds the 765's READ DATA command ($06 with the 765 flags at +$19) for one sector\n(SECTOR_CMD_BUILD).\nEntry and Changes: as SECTOR_CMD_BUILD.","comment":"The 765 flags"},
        "7124": {"comment":"$06: READ DATA"},
        "7128": {"synopsis":"Builds the 765's WRITE DATA command ($05 with the MT and MF bits of the 765 flags at +$19,\nnever SK) for one sector, falling into SECTOR_CMD_BUILD.\nEntry and Changes: as SECTOR_CMD_BUILD.","comment":"The 765 flags"},
        "7131": {"comment":"MT and MF only"},
        "7133": {"comment":"$05: WRITE DATA"},
        "7135": {"synopsis":"Builds a one-sector 765 command in the command block at $E400 (bank 7), the command byte in\nA:\n1. The bank, buffer, unit and head (CMD_HEAD_BUILD), the logical track turned into track and\n   head.\n2. The sector number: E + the format's first sector number (+$14), passed to the sector hook\n   at $E419 when one is set (SECTOR_HOOK_SET), which may change E.\n3. The command bytes C = the track, H = the head, R = EOT = the sector, N (+$0F), GPL (the\n   read/write gap, +$17), DTL $FF; 9 bytes.\nEntry: A = the command byte, IX = the parameter block, B = the bank, HL = the buffer, C =\nthe unit, D = the logical track, E = the sector (0 for the first).\nExit: HL = $E40E, the last command byte; D = the track, E = the sector number before the\nhook; B = the head, C = the unit with the head in bit 2.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Bank, buffer, unit and head"},
        "7138": {"comment":"The sector"},
        "7139": {"comment":"...+ the format's first sector number"},
        "7143": {"comment":"Kept for the exit"},
        "7144": {"comment":"The sector hook"},
        "7147": {"comment":"One set?"},
        "7149": {"comment":"It may change E"},
        "7152": {"comment":"R = the sector"},
        "7156": {"comment":"N = the sector size code"},
        "7159": {"comment":"EOT = the same sector: one sector"},
        "7160": {"comment":"Command bytes 5 and 6"},
        "7163": {"comment":"GPL = the read/write gap"},
        "7166": {"comment":"Command byte 7"},
        "7169": {"comment":"H = the head"},
        "7170": {"comment":"C = the track"},
        "7171": {"comment":"Command bytes 2 and 3"},
        "7174": {"comment":"9 command bytes"},
        "7179": {"comment":"DTL = $FF"},
        "7184": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "7186": {"synopsis":"Starts the command block at $E400: +0 the bank (B), +1 the buffer (HL), +6 the command byte\n(A), +7 the unit with the head in bit 2, +3 the byte count = the sector size (+$15). The\nlogical track in D is turned into track and head first (TRACK_TO_SIDE).\nEntry: A = the command byte, B = the bank, HL = the buffer, C = the unit, D = the logical\ntrack, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: B = the head, C = the unit and head, D = the track.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"+1: the buffer"},
        "7189": {"comment":"L = the command byte"},
        "7190": {"comment":"+0: the bank"},
        "7194": {"comment":"D, B, C: track and head"},
        "7197": {"comment":"H = the unit and head"},
        "7198": {"comment":"+6, +7: the command's first two bytes"},
        "7201": {"comment":"The sector size"},
        "7207": {"comment":"+3: the byte count"},
        "7211": {"synopsis":"Turns a logical track into the track and head, by the sides byte (+$11) with bit 7 left out:\n0 one side (head 0, the track as it is); 1 sides alternating (track D / 2, the head D's low\nbit); anything else the sides one after the other (below the tracks per side (+$12) head 0;\nfrom there head 1, the track 2 x tracks per side - 1 - D, counted back from the last).\nEntry: D = the logical track, C = the unit, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: D = the track, B = the head, C = the unit with the head in bit 2 (unchanged for one\nside).\nChanges: AF, B, C, D.","comment":"The sides byte"},
        "7214": {"comment":"Bit 7 aside"},
        "7216": {"comment":"Head 0"},
        "7218": {"comment":"One side: done"},
        "7219": {"comment":"Sides alternating?"},
        "7222": {"comment":"Track / 2"},
        "7225": {"comment":"...the low bit is the head"},
        "7228": {"comment":"Into C"},
        "7230": {"synopsis":"Sides one after the other: from the tracks per side up, head 1 and the track counted back.","comment":"Track - tracks per side"},
        "7234": {"comment":"On side 0?"},
        "7236": {"comment":"Track - 2 x tracks per side"},
        "7239": {"comment":"Counted back from the last track"},
        "7241": {"comment":"Head 1"},
        "7242": {"synopsis":"The head into bit 2 of C.","comment":"Head x 4"},
        "7245": {"comment":"Into the unit byte"},
        "7248": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0184) Sets the sector hook, the routine whose address is at $E419 (0 for none):\nSECTOR_CMD_BUILD calls it before each sector command with E = the sector number, D = the\ntrack, B = the head, C = the unit and head, and puts the E it returns into the command. A =\n0 removes the hook; otherwise HL is the routine.\nEntry: A = 0 for none, else HL = the routine.\nExit: HL = the hook it replaced (0 for none).\nChanges: F, DE, HL.","comment":"No hook?"},
        "7251": {"comment":"0: none"},
        "7254": {"synopsis":"The new hook in, the old one out to HL.","comment":"DE = the old hook"},
        "7258": {"comment":"The new one"},
        "7261": {"comment":"HL = the old one"},
        "7263": {"synopsis":"Reads the first A bytes of a sector (READ DATA; the rest of the sector is read and dropped),\nwith the motor on, the tries and the time-out of RUN_DISK_OP.\nEntry: A = the byte count, IX = the parameter block, B = the bank, HL = the buffer, C = the\nunit, D = the logical track, E = the sector (0 for the first).\nExit: carry set: read; no carry: A = the error (RUN_WITH_TRIES).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "7264": {"comment":"READ DATA's command block"},
        "7268": {"comment":"HL = the count"},
        "7271": {"comment":"+3: the byte count"},
        "7274": {"comment":"The operation"},
        "7277": {"comment":"Motor, tries, time-out"},
        "7279": {"synopsis":"SECTOR_READ_PART's operation, run at each try: CMD_READ_PART on the command block at $E400.","comment":"The command block"},
        "7285": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0163) Reads one sector: READ DATA in the command block at $E400\n(READ_CMD_BUILD), run with the motor on, the tries and the time-out (RUN_DISK_OP).\nEntry: IX = the parameter block, B = the bank (paged in at $C000 for the transfer), HL = the\nbuffer, C = the unit, D = the logical track, E = the sector (0 for the first).\nExit: carry set: read; no carry: A = the error (RUN_WITH_TRIES).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"READ DATA's command block"},
        "7288": {"comment":"The operation"},
        "7291": {"comment":"Motor, tries, time-out"},
        "7293": {"synopsis":"SECTOR_READ's operation, run at each try: CMD_READ on the command block at $E400.","comment":"The command block"},
        "7299": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0166) Writes one sector: refused with A = 9 when WRITE_ALLOWED says no;\notherwise WRITE DATA (WRITE_CMD_BUILD) with the buffer's bytes sent (RUN_WRITE_OP).\nEntry: as SECTOR_READ.\nExit: carry set: written; no carry: A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Writing allowed?"},
        "7302": {"comment":"No: A = 9"},
        "7303": {"comment":"WRITE DATA's command block"},
        "7306": {"comment":"Run it"},
        "7308": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0169) Compares a sector with the buffer: SCAN EQUAL (SCAN_CMD_BUILD), which\ntakes the buffer's bytes from the CPU (RUN_WRITE_OP).\nEntry: as SECTOR_READ.\nExit: carry set: the command worked, and Z when ST2 is $08 (only the scan-hit bit: the same\nbytes); no carry: A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"SCAN EQUAL's command block"},
        "7311": {"comment":"The buffer to the 765"},
        "7314": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "7315": {"comment":"ST2"},
        "7318": {"comment":"Only SH set: the same?"},
        "7320": {"comment":"Carry: the command worked"},
        "7322": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $016C) Formats a track: refused with A = 9 when WRITE_ALLOWED says no; otherwise\nFORMAT A TRACK (FMT_CMD_BUILD), the buffer's ID fields sent to the 765 (RUN_WRITE_OP).\nEntry: IX = the parameter block, B = the bank, HL = the ID fields (C, H, R, N for each\nsector), C = the unit, D = the logical track, E = the filler byte.\nExit: carry set: formatted; no carry: A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Writing allowed?"},
        "7325": {"comment":"No: A = 9"},
        "7326": {"comment":"FORMAT's command block"},
        "7329": {"synopsis":"Runs the command block at $E400 with its data sent from the buffer (OP_WRITE), through\nRUN_DISK_OP.","comment":"The operation"},
        "7332": {"comment":"Motor, tries, time-out"},
        "7334": {"synopsis":"RUN_WRITE_OP's operation, run at each try: CMD_WRITE on the command block at $E400.","comment":"The command block"},
        "7340": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $016F) Reads the next sector ID on a track: READ ID on logical track D, with the\nmotor on, the tries and the time-out.\nEntry: IX = the parameter block, C = the unit, D = the logical track.\nExit: carry set: A = the ID's sector number (R), HL = $E430 (the result count, then ST0,\nST1, ST2, C, H, R, N); no carry: A = the error, HL = $E430.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"The ID read"},
        "7343": {"comment":"The results"},
        "7346": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "7347": {"comment":"R: the ID's sector number"},
        "7351": {"synopsis":"READ ID on logical track D: the track turned into track and head (TRACK_TO_SIDE), then\nOP_READ_ID run through RUN_DISK_OP.","comment":"Track and head"},
        "7354": {"comment":"The operation"},
        "7359": {"synopsis":"ID_READ_TRACK's operation, run at each try: READ ID with the 765 flags (+$19) for the unit\nand head in C (CMD_READ_ID).","comment":"The 765 flags"},
        "7365": {"synopsis":"Runs a disk operation with the motor on: MOTOR_ON, the operation at HL through\nRUN_WITH_TRIES, then the motor's time-out started (MOTOR_TIMER_SET).\nEntry: HL = the operation, C = the unit and head, D = the track, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: as RUN_WITH_TRIES: carry set for success, else A = the error.","comment":"Motor on"},
        "7368": {"comment":"Seek, run, try again"},
        "7371": {"comment":"The motor's time-out"},
        "7374": {"synopsis":"Four built-in disk formats, 10 bytes each, read by FORMAT_SELECT at $1CCE + 10 x the number\nand by DISK_IDENTIFY. The layout, which a disk's own first sector can also carry\n(DISK_IDENTIFY):\n+0 the format number (1 makes the sectors count from $41, 2 from $C1, any other from $01:\nFORMAT_FROM_SPEC); +1 the sides byte (0 one side, 1 sides alternating, 2 one side after the\nother; bit 7: never stepped twice, see SEEK_CMD); +2 tracks per side; +3 sectors per track;\n+4 the sector size code (128 x 2^n bytes); +5 reserved tracks; +6 the block size code (128 x\n2^n bytes); +7 the directory blocks (0: worked out); +8 the read/write gap; +9 the format\ngap.\n0: one side, 40 tracks of 9 512-byte sectors, 1 reserved track, 1K blocks, 2 directory\nblocks.\n1: the same with 2 reserved tracks.\n2: the same with none.\n3: two sides alternating with bit 7, 80 tracks of 9 512-byte sectors, 1 reserved track, 2K\nblocks, 4 directory blocks.\nThe gaps are $2A and $52 in all four."},
        "7414": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0175) Finds the format of the disk in a unit and sets the parameter block for\nit:\n1. Format 0 into IX (FORMAT_SELECT), so that track 0 can be read.\n2. READ ID on track 0 (ID_READ): a sector number with its top two bits 01 means format 1,\nwith 11 format 2 (IDENT_BY_ID).\n3. Otherwise the first 10 bytes of track 0's first sector are read to $E40F in bank 7\n(IDENT_BY_SECTOR). Ten equal bytes mean format 0 (FORMAT_SPECS); other bytes are taken as\na format of FORMAT_SPECS' layout, which must have a number below 4 (IDENT_SPEC_USE).\n4. The drive checked against the format (DRIVE_FORMAT_FIT).\nEntry: IX = the parameter block, C = the unit.\nExit: carry set: A = the format number, IX's block set, DE and HL as PARAMS_FROM_SPEC leaves\nthem; no carry: A = the error (6 for a format not recognised, which an error 8 from the read\nbecomes too).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"Format 0"},
        "7415": {"comment":"Into IX"},
        "7418": {"comment":"Track 0"},
        "7420": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "7421": {"comment":"A = the first ID's sector number"},
        "7425": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "7426": {"comment":"Its top two bits"},
        "7428": {"comment":"Format 1"},
        "7430": {"comment":"...for 01?"},
        "7434": {"comment":"Format 2"},
        "7435": {"comment":"...for 11?"},
        "7437": {"comment":"Neither: the first sector's bytes"},
        "7439": {"synopsis":"The format found from the sector numbers: into IX (FORMAT_SELECT), then the drive checked.","comment":"The format number"},
        "7440": {"comment":"Into IX"},
        "7443": {"comment":"The drive checked"},
        "7445": {"synopsis":"Reads the first 10 bytes of track 0's first sector to $E40F in bank 7; error 8 becomes error\n6.","comment":"The unit kept"},
        "7446": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "7449": {"comment":"Track 0, the first sector"},
        "7452": {"comment":"In bank 7"},
        "7454": {"comment":"10 bytes"},
        "7457": {"comment":"Read"},
        "7461": {"comment":"The unit back"},
        "7462": {"comment":"Read?"},
        "7464": {"comment":"Error 8?"},
        "7466": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "7468": {"comment":"...and other errors as they are"},
        "7469": {"comment":"Error 8 becomes 6"},
        "7472": {"synopsis":"Ten equal bytes (a sector filled with one value) give format 0; other bytes are the disk's\nown format.","comment":"The unit kept"},
        "7473": {"comment":"DE = the bytes"},
        "7475": {"comment":"C = the first"},
        "7476": {"comment":"Ten bytes"},
        "7478": {"synopsis":"One byte compared with the first.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "7480": {"comment":"The same as the first?"},
        "7483": {"comment":"Next"},
        "7485": {"comment":"All the same: format 0"},
        "7488": {"synopsis":"The format at HL into IX when its number is below 4 (FORMAT_FROM_SPEC); otherwise A = 6, no\ncarry.","comment":"The unit back"},
        "7489": {"comment":"The format's number"},
        "7490": {"comment":"Below 4?"},
        "7492": {"comment":"Otherwise error 6"},
        "7494": {"comment":"Into IX"},
        "7497": {"synopsis":"The drive checked against the format, when one was set (carry): DRIVE_FORMAT_FIT.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "7499": {"comment":"Does the drive suit it?"},
        "7505": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0178) Sets the parameter block for built-in format A (0-3) from FORMAT_SPECS,\nthrough FORMAT_FROM_SPEC.\nEntry: A = the format number, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: as FORMAT_FROM_SPEC; for A from 4 up no carry, A = 6.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"E = the number"},
        "7506": {"comment":"Built in?"},
        "7508": {"comment":"No: error 6"},
        "7511": {"comment":"A x 2"},
        "7514": {"comment":"x 8"},
        "7516": {"comment":"x 10"},
        "7520": {"comment":"H = $1C + the carry"},
        "7524": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0187) Sets the parameter block at IX from a 10-byte format at HL (FORMAT_SPECS'\nlayout): +$14 the first sector number ($41 for format number 1, $C1 for 2, $01 for any\nother), +$11 the sides byte, +$12 tracks per side, +$13 sectors per track, +$17 and +$18 the\ntwo gaps, +$15 the sector size in bytes, +$19 the 765 flags $60 (MF and SK); then the rest\nthrough PARAMS_FROM_SPEC.\nEntry: HL = the format, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: as PARAMS_FROM_SPEC.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"The format kept"},
        "7526": {"comment":"Its number"},
        "7527": {"comment":"Sectors from $41"},
        "7529": {"comment":"...for number 1?"},
        "7532": {"comment":"Sectors from $C1"},
        "7534": {"comment":"...for number 2?"},
        "7537": {"comment":"Otherwise from $01"},
        "7539": {"synopsis":"The first sector number and the rest of the format into IX.","comment":"+$14: the first sector number"},
        "7542": {"comment":"The sides byte"},
        "7544": {"comment":"+$11"},
        "7547": {"comment":"Tracks per side"},
        "7549": {"comment":"+$12"},
        "7552": {"comment":"Sectors per track"},
        "7554": {"comment":"+$13"},
        "7557": {"comment":"B = the sector size code"},
        "7559": {"comment":"Past +5 to +7"},
        "7563": {"comment":"The read/write gap"},
        "7564": {"comment":"+$17"},
        "7567": {"comment":"The format gap"},
        "7569": {"comment":"+$18"},
        "7572": {"comment":"128 x 2^code"},
        "7578": {"comment":"+$15: the sector size"},
        "7584": {"comment":"+$19: MF and SK"},
        "7588": {"comment":"BC and HL back"},
        "7590": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $018A) Works out the rest of the parameter block at IX from a 10-byte format at\nHL (FORMAT_SPECS' layout), with c the block size code and n the sector size code:\n+$00 the 128-byte records per track (sectors per track x 2^n);\n+$02 c, and +$03 2^c - 1;\n+$04 2^(c - 3) - 1, or 2^(c - 4) - 1 when there are more than 256 blocks;\n+$05 the blocks on the disk less 1: the sectors on the tracks that are not reserved (on both\nsides when the sides byte, bit 7 aside, is not 0) / the sectors per block;\n+$07 the directory entries less 1: the directory blocks x 2^(c + 2), 32 bytes each;\n+$09 (high) and +$0A (low): a bit for each directory block, from bit 7 of +$09 down;\n+$0B (the directory entries - 1) / 4 + 1;\n+$0D the reserved tracks (+$0E 0);\n+$0F n, and +$10 2^n - 1.\nWith +7 of the format 0, the directory blocks are (blocks - 1) x 2 / 256 + 1, at least 2.\nEntry: HL = the format, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: carry set; A = the format's number (its first byte); DE = (blocks - 1) / 4 + 2; HL = 4\nx the directory entries.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"BC and the format kept"},
        "7592": {"comment":"DE = the format"},
        "7593": {"comment":"+4"},
        "7597": {"comment":"The sector size code"},
        "7598": {"comment":"+$0F"},
        "7601": {"comment":"Kept for the shift"},
        "7602": {"comment":"2^n - 1"},
        "7605": {"comment":"+$10"},
        "7608": {"comment":"+3"},
        "7609": {"comment":"Sectors per track"},
        "7612": {"comment":"B = n"},
        "7613": {"comment":"x 2^n: records per track"},
        "7616": {"comment":"+$00"},
        "7622": {"comment":"+6"},
        "7626": {"comment":"The block size code"},
        "7627": {"comment":"+$02"},
        "7630": {"comment":"C = c"},
        "7631": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "7632": {"comment":"2^c - 1"},
        "7635": {"comment":"+$03"},
        "7638": {"comment":"+5"},
        "7639": {"comment":"The reserved tracks"},
        "7640": {"comment":"+$0D"},
        "7643": {"comment":"+$0E = 0"},
        "7647": {"comment":"+3"},
        "7649": {"comment":"B = sectors per track"},
        "7650": {"comment":"+2"},
        "7651": {"comment":"D = tracks per side"},
        "7652": {"comment":"+1"},
        "7653": {"comment":"The sides byte"},
        "7654": {"comment":"HL = tracks per side"},
        "7657": {"comment":"DE = the reserved tracks"},
        "7658": {"comment":"Two sides?"},
        "7662": {"comment":"Twice the tracks"},
        "7663": {"synopsis":"The tracks less the reserved ones, times the sectors per track.","comment":"Less the reserved tracks"},
        "7665": {"comment":"DE = the tracks"},
        "7666": {"comment":"HL = 0"},
        "7669": {"synopsis":"One more track's worth: the tracks added B times.","comment":"+ the tracks"},
        "7670": {"comment":"For each sector per track"},
        "7672": {"comment":"c - n"},
        "7676": {"comment":"...the sectors per block as a shift"},
        "7677": {"comment":"HL = the blocks"},
        "7680": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "7681": {"comment":"+$05"},
        "7687": {"comment":"3"},
        "7689": {"comment":"More than 256 blocks?"},
        "7693": {"comment":"...or 4"},
        "7694": {"synopsis":"+$04 = 2^(c - B) - 1; then the directory.","comment":"c - 3 or c - 4"},
        "7696": {"comment":"2^that - 1"},
        "7699": {"comment":"+$04"},
        "7702": {"comment":"DE = the format's +6"},
        "7703": {"comment":"The blocks - 1 kept"},
        "7704": {"comment":"/ 4"},
        "7709": {"comment":"+ 2"},
        "7711": {"comment":"Kept for DE; HL = blocks - 1"},
        "7712": {"comment":"+7"},
        "7713": {"comment":"The directory blocks"},
        "7714": {"comment":"Given?"},
        "7717": {"comment":"(Blocks - 1) x 2"},
        "7718": {"comment":"...H + 1"},
        "7720": {"comment":"At least 2?"},
        "7724": {"comment":"1 becomes 2"},
        "7725": {"synopsis":"B = the directory blocks: as many bits from the top into +$09 and +$0A.","comment":"B = the directory blocks"},
        "7726": {"comment":"No bits yet"},
        "7729": {"synopsis":"One more bit set from the top.","comment":"A 1 in from the top"},
        "7734": {"comment":"For each directory block"},
        "7736": {"comment":"+$09: the high byte"},
        "7739": {"comment":"+$0A: the low byte"},
        "7742": {"comment":"HL = the directory blocks"},
        "7745": {"comment":"c + 2"},
        "7748": {"comment":"x 2^(c + 2): the directory entries"},
        "7751": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "7752": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "7753": {"comment":"+$07"},
        "7759": {"comment":"/ 4"},
        "7764": {"comment":"+ 1"},
        "7765": {"comment":"+$0B"},
        "7771": {"comment":"The entries"},
        "7772": {"comment":"x 4"},
        "7774": {"comment":"DE = (blocks - 1) / 4 + 2"},
        "7775": {"comment":"BC = the format"},
        "7776": {"comment":"A = its number"},
        "7777": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "7778": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "7780": {"synopsis":"Checks that the unit's drive suits the format in IX, finding the drive's kind first when it\nis not known (DRIVE_KIND_FIND): a two-sided format needs bit 1 of the unit's state (an ID\nread with head 1 that carried head 1); a format with bit 7 of its sides byte needs bit 3.\nEntry: A = the format number, C = the unit, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: carry set: A = the format number; no carry: A = 9 (the drive does not suit), or\nDRIVE_KIND_FIND's error.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.","comment":"B = the format number"},
        "7783": {"comment":"The drive's kind"},
        "7788": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "7789": {"comment":"The sides"},
        "7792": {"comment":"One side?"},
        "7796": {"comment":"Head 1 read as head 1?"},
        "7798": {"comment":"No: does not suit"},
        "7800": {"synopsis":"The tracks: a format with bit 7 of its sides byte needs bit 3 of the unit's state.","comment":"A = the format number"},
        "7802": {"comment":"Bit 7 of the sides byte?"},
        "7806": {"comment":"No: suits"},
        "7807": {"comment":"State bit 3?"},
        "7809": {"comment":"Set: suits"},
        "7810": {"synopsis":"Error 9: the drive does not suit the format.","comment":"Error 9"},
        "7812": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "7814": {"synopsis":"Finds the kind of a unit's drive into its state byte (UNIT_STATE), when neither bit 2 nor\nbit 3 is set yet, or the format has two sides and neither bit 0 nor bit 1 is set:\n1. READ ID on the logical track that is track 2 on the format's last side: 2 for one side, 5\n   for sides alternating, 2 x tracks per side - 3 for one side after the other (ID_READ).\n2. For a two-sided format: bit 1 when the ID carried head 1, bit 0 when not.\n3. Bit 3 when the ID's track is 2 and the format has bit 7 of its sides byte, or the track\n   is not 2 and the format has not; bit 2 otherwise.\nEntry: C = the unit, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: carry set: HL = the state byte; no carry: A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = the unit's state"},
        "7817": {"comment":"Tracks known?"},
        "7820": {"comment":"No: find them"},
        "7822": {"comment":"Sides known?"},
        "7825": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "7827": {"comment":"A one-sided format?"},
        "7832": {"comment":"Then done"},
        "7834": {"synopsis":"The logical track that is track 2 on the last side.","comment":"The sides"},
        "7839": {"comment":"One side: track 2"},
        "7843": {"comment":"Sides alternating?"},
        "7844": {"comment":"Track 2, head 1"},
        "7848": {"comment":"One after the other"},
        "7851": {"comment":"...2 x tracks - 3: track 2, head 1"},
        "7855": {"synopsis":"READ ID there; the state bits from the ID.","comment":"The state kept"},
        "7856": {"comment":"READ ID"},
        "7860": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "7861": {"comment":"E = the ID's track, D its head"},
        "7865": {"comment":"A two-sided format?"},
        "7872": {"comment":"Head 1 in the ID?"},
        "7875": {"comment":"No: bit 0"},
        "7879": {"synopsis":"Bit 1: the ID read with head 1 carried head 1.","comment":"Bit 1"},
        "7881": {"synopsis":"Bit 3 or bit 2, from the ID's track and bit 7 of the sides byte.","comment":"The sides byte"},
        "7884": {"comment":"Track 2 in the ID?"},
        "7886": {"comment":"Yes: bit 7 as it is"},
        "7888": {"comment":"No: bit 7 turned over"},
        "7889": {"synopsis":"That bit into the carry: set gives bit 3, clear bit 2.","comment":"Into the carry"},
        "7890": {"comment":"Clear: bit 2"},
        "7892": {"comment":"Bit 3, carry set"},
        "7895": {"synopsis":"Bit 2, carry set.","comment":"Bit 2"},
        "7897": {"comment":"Done"},
        "7899": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0172) Says whether a unit may write the format in IX: not when bit 3 of the\nunit's state is set (DRIVE_KIND_FIND) and bit 7 of the format's sides byte is clear.\nEntry: C = the unit, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: carry set: allowed; no carry: A = 9.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "7900": {"comment":"The unit's state"},
        "7903": {"comment":"Bit 3?"},
        "7906": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "7907": {"comment":"...clear: allowed"},
        "7908": {"comment":"The sides byte"},
        "7911": {"comment":"Carry = bit 7"},
        "7912": {"comment":"Error 9 when clear"},
        "7915": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0181) A = bits 0-3 of a unit's state, the bits DRIVE_KIND_FIND sets.\nEntry: C = the unit.\nExit: A; HL = the state byte.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"HL = the unit's state"},
        "7919": {"comment":"The drive's kind"},
        "7922": {"synopsis":"Runs a disk operation until it works, up to $E42D times (ONE_TRY each; the count of tries\nleft decides when the head goes first to the last track or is recalibrated):\n1. Success returns at once, and so does a not-ready (0) or write-protect (1) error or a\n   failed seek.\n2. Error 4 (ST1's no-data bit): READ ID on the track; an ID whose sector number differs in\n   its top two bits from the format's first sector number (+$14) ends with error 8;\n   otherwise the next try.\n3. Other errors: the next try. After the last, the last error.\nEntry: HL = the operation, C = the unit and head, D = the track, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: carry set: done; no carry: A = the error: 0 not ready, 1 write protected, 2 seek\nfailed, 3 data error, 4 no data, 5 missing address mark, 7 another 765 error, 8 sectors of\nanother format.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"The tries"},
        "7925": {"comment":"B = tries left"},
        "7926": {"synopsis":"One try.","comment":"Kept"},
        "7927": {"comment":"Seek and run"},
        "7931": {"comment":"Done, or not worth retrying"},
        "7932": {"comment":"No data?"},
        "7934": {"comment":"No: try again"},
        "7936": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "7939": {"comment":"The 765 flags"},
        "7942": {"comment":"READ ID on the track"},
        "7945": {"comment":"Its result"},
        "7951": {"comment":"Failed: try again"},
        "7953": {"comment":"Not worth retrying"},
        "7954": {"comment":"The ID's sector number"},
        "7957": {"comment":"Against the format's first"},
        "7960": {"comment":"Top two bits differ?"},
        "7962": {"comment":"Error 8: another format"},
        "7965": {"comment":"Else error 4 again"},
        "7966": {"synopsis":"The next try; after the last, the error with no carry.","comment":"Next try"},
        "7968": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "7970": {"synopsis":"One try of RUN_WITH_TRIES's operation, B being the tries left: when B is a multiple of 8,\nthe head goes to the last track first; when it is 4 more than one, the unit's track is\nforgotten (state bit 6 cleared) so that the seek recalibrates. Then the seek to track D\n(SEEK_TRACK), the operation at HL and its result (RESULT_TEST).\nEntry: B = the tries left, HL = the operation, C = the unit and head, D = the track, IX =\nthe parameter block.\nExit: Z and carry: done; Z, no carry: A = an error not worth retrying; NZ: A = the error.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"The tries left"},
        "7971": {"comment":"A multiple of 8?"},
        "7975": {"comment":"Not 4 more either?"},
        "7979": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "7980": {"comment":"The unit's state"},
        "7983": {"comment":"Track forgotten: recalibrate"},
        "7986": {"comment":"The seek"},
        "7988": {"synopsis":"To the last track first.","comment":"The track kept"},
        "7989": {"comment":"The last track"},
        "7993": {"comment":"Seek there"},
        "7997": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "7998": {"synopsis":"Seek to track D, run the operation, test its result.","comment":"Seek to track D"},
        "8001": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "8002": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "8005": {"comment":"The operation"},
        "8010": {"comment":"Its result"},
        "8015": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $017B) Tells whether unit 1 has a drive: SENSE DRIVE STATUS for it\n(DRIVE_STATUS); a drive when ST3 has ready or write protected set (bit 5 or 6).\nExit: carry set: a drive; A = ST3's bits 5 and 6.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The unit kept"},
        "8016": {"comment":"Unit 1"},
        "8018": {"comment":"ST3"},
        "8022": {"comment":"Ready or write protected?"},
        "8024": {"comment":"Neither: no carry"},
        "8025": {"comment":"A drive"},
        "8027": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $017E) SENSE DRIVE STATUS for a unit, with the motor on, then the motor's\ntime-out started.\nEntry: C = the unit (head in bit 2).\nExit: A = ST3, HL = $E430 (the result count, then ST3).\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"Motor on"},
        "8030": {"comment":"SENSE DRIVE STATUS"},
        "8033": {"comment":"The motor's time-out"},
        "8036": {"synopsis":"A = 2^A - 1, the low A bits set (0 for 0).\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"No bits?"},
        "8038": {"comment":"B = the bits"},
        "8039": {"comment":"2^0"},
        "8041": {"synopsis":"Doubled for each bit.","comment":"x 2"},
        "8044": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "8046": {"synopsis":"HL = HL x 2^B.\nChanges: AF, B (0 after a shift), HL.","comment":"No shift?"},
        "8049": {"synopsis":"One bit left.","comment":"x 2"},
        "8053": {"synopsis":"HL = HL / 2^B, rounded down.\nChanges: AF, B (0 after a shift), HL.","comment":"No shift?"},
        "8056": {"synopsis":"One bit right.","comment":"/ 2"},
        "8063": {"synopsis":"The drive timings DISK_INIT sets (through TIMINGS_SET), 7 bytes: +0 $0A (10), the motor's\nstart-up wait in rounds of about 0.1 s (MOTOR_ON); +1 $32 (50), the motor's time-out count\n(MOTOR_TIMER_SET); +2 $AF (175), the wait after a write in rounds of 34 T-states\n(CMD_WRITE); +3 $1E (30), the head's settling time in ms; +4 $0C (12), the step time in ms\n(STEP_SEND_WAIT, and SPECIFY's step rate); +5 $0F, the low four bits of SPECIFY's first byte\n(the head unload time); +6 $03, SPECIFY's second byte (the head load time and the non-DMA\nbit)."},
        "8070": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0157) Tells whether a disk controller answers: carry set unless the 765's main\nstatus register (port $2FFD) reads $FF.\nExit: carry set: there is one.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "8071": {"comment":"The 765's status port"},
        "8074": {"comment":"Main status"},
        "8076": {"comment":"$FF gives carry"},
        "8078": {"comment":"...so carry for anything else"},
        "8081": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $015A) Sets up the disk driver: the 16 bytes from $E420 cleared (the four units'\nstates: nothing known, and the timings), 15 tries ($E42D), the motor off (MOTOR_OFF), and\nthe timings from DRIVE_TIMINGS (TIMINGS_SET), which ends with SPECIFY.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The units' states and the timings"},
        "8084": {"comment":"16 bytes"},
        "8086": {"synopsis":"One byte cleared.","comment":"Cleared"},
        "8091": {"comment":"15 tries"},
        "8096": {"comment":"Motor off"},
        "8099": {"comment":"The default timings"},
        "8102": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $015D) Sets the drive timings from 7 bytes at HL (DRIVE_TIMINGS' layout): the\nfirst five into $E428-$E42C, then the 765's SPECIFY command, its first byte the step rate 15\n- (step time - 1) / 2 in bits 4-7 with +5 below it, its second +6.\nEntry: HL = the 7 bytes.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"To $E428-$E42C"},
        "8105": {"comment":"5 bytes"},
        "8110": {"comment":"The step time in ms"},
        "8113": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "8114": {"comment":"x 8: half of it in bits 4-7"},
        "8117": {"comment":"15 less that"},
        "8118": {"comment":"The step rate in bits 4-7"},
        "8120": {"comment":"The head unload time below it"},
        "8121": {"comment":"+6"},
        "8122": {"comment":"H = the head load time, non-DMA"},
        "8123": {"comment":"L = the first byte"},
        "8124": {"comment":"$03: SPECIFY"},
        "8129": {"comment":"The first byte"},
        "8133": {"comment":"The second byte"},
        "8137": {"synopsis":"HL = the state of unit C (bits 0-1): two bytes at $E420 + 2 x the unit. +0 the drive's bits:\n0 and 1 from DRIVE_KIND_FIND's ID read with head 1 (bit 1: it carried head 1), 2 and 3 from\nits track test, 6 the head's track known; +1 the track the head is on.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The unit"},
        "8140": {"comment":"x 2"},
        "8141": {"comment":"L = $20 + that"},
        "8144": {"comment":"H = $E4 + the carry"},
        "8149": {"synopsis":"Moves unit C's head to track D (SEEK_TRACK_HL), keeping HL.\nExit: as SEEK_TRACK_HL.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "8150": {"comment":"The unit's state"},
        "8153": {"comment":"The seek"},
        "8158": {"synopsis":"Moves a unit's head to track D, trying up to $E42D times: when the head's track is not known\n(state bit 6 clear), to track 0 by recalibrating (RECAL_TWICE), then bit 6 set; already on\nD: done; else to track 0 by recalibrating, or to D by SEEK (SEEK_CMD). A failure forgets the\ntrack; not ready ends it at once.\nEntry: HL = the unit's state, C = the unit and head, D = the track, IX = the parameter\nblock.\nExit: carry set: on track D (+1 of the state = D); no carry and Z: A = the error (0 not\nready, 2 seek failed).\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"The tries"},
        "8162": {"synopsis":"One try.","comment":"Track known?"},
        "8166": {"comment":"No: track 0"},
        "8170": {"comment":"...by recalibrating"},
        "8173": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "8175": {"comment":"Known now"},
        "8177": {"synopsis":"The head's track known: to D.","comment":"Already on D?"},
        "8181": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "8183": {"comment":"Track 0?"},
        "8186": {"comment":"Recalibrate"},
        "8191": {"synopsis":"SEEK to D.","comment":"SEEK"},
        "8194": {"synopsis":"Done: the head's track noted.","comment":"Failed?"},
        "8196": {"comment":"+1: the head's track"},
        "8199": {"synopsis":"Recalibrating failed: unless the drive is not ready, a SEEK to the last track first.","comment":"The track kept"},
        "8200": {"comment":"Unless not ready: the last track"},
        "8204": {"synopsis":"Failed: the track forgotten; not ready ends it, other errors try again.","comment":"Track forgotten"},
        "8206": {"comment":"Not ready: given up"},
        "8207": {"comment":"Interrupts cleared"},
        "8210": {"comment":"Next try"},
        "8212": {"comment":"Z, no carry: failed"},
        "8214": {"synopsis":"RECALIBRATE, and again unless the first ended with Z (done, or not ready).\nExit: as SEEK_END_TEST.","comment":"Once"},
        "8217": {"comment":"Done or not ready"},
        "8218": {"synopsis":"The 765's RECALIBRATE for a unit, then a wait of a step time for each track (tracks per side\n- 1; twice that when state bit 3 is set and the format's bit 7 is not) and the settling\ntime, then SENSE INTERRUPT STATUS and its test (STEP_SEND_WAIT).\nEntry: HL = the unit's state, C = the unit, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: as SEEK_END_TEST: carry and Z for done.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "8219": {"comment":"Tracks per side"},
        "8222": {"comment":"...less 1: the steps"},
        "8223": {"comment":"Bit 7 of the sides byte?"},
        "8227": {"comment":"Yes: as they are"},
        "8229": {"comment":"State bit 3?"},
        "8233": {"comment":"Twice the steps"},
        "8236": {"synopsis":"RECALIBRATE and its unit byte.","comment":"$07: RECALIBRATE"},
        "8241": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "8242": {"comment":"...bits 0-1 only"},
        "8244": {"comment":"Sent, then the waits"},
        "8246": {"synopsis":"SEEK to the last track (tracks per side - 1).","comment":"Tracks per side"},
        "8249": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "8250": {"synopsis":"The 765's SEEK for a unit to track D: B = the steps, the distance from the head's track (+1\nof the state); with state bit 3 set and the format's bit 7 clear, the steps and the track\nsent are doubled. Then the waits and the test (STEP_SEND_WAIT).\nEntry: HL = the unit's state, C = the unit and head, D = the track, IX = the parameter\nblock.\nExit: as SEEK_END_TEST.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "8251": {"comment":"The track"},
        "8252": {"comment":"...less the head's"},
        "8255": {"comment":"Not below it?"},
        "8257": {"comment":"Negated"},
        "8259": {"synopsis":"B = the steps; SEEK, the unit and the track sent.","comment":"B = the steps"},
        "8260": {"comment":"$0F: SEEK"},
        "8265": {"comment":"The unit and head"},
        "8269": {"comment":"The track"},
        "8270": {"comment":"Bit 7 of the sides byte?"},
        "8274": {"comment":"Yes: as it is"},
        "8276": {"comment":"State bit 3?"},
        "8280": {"comment":"Twice the steps"},
        "8283": {"comment":"Twice the track"},
        "8285": {"synopsis":"Sends the command's last byte (A), waits B step times ($E42C ms each; B = 0 is 256) and the\nsettling time ($E42B ms), then SENSE INTERRUPT STATUS into $E430 and its test\n(SEEK_END_TEST); HL and BC back from the stack.","comment":"The state kept"},
        "8286": {"comment":"The last byte"},
        "8289": {"synopsis":"One step time.","comment":"The step time in ms"},
        "8295": {"comment":"For each step"},
        "8297": {"comment":"The settling time"},
        "8303": {"comment":"The results"},
        "8306": {"comment":"SENSE INTERRUPT STATUS"},
        "8309": {"comment":"Its test"},
        "8312": {"comment":"The state back"},
        "8315": {"synopsis":"Waits A x about 3,540 T-states (about 1 ms at 3.5 MHz); A = 0 is 256.\nChanges: AF, L.","comment":"220 rounds"},
        "8317": {"synopsis":"16 T-states a round.","comment":"Round down"},
        "8320": {"comment":"For each ms"},
        "8324": {"synopsis":"Tests SENSE INTERRUPT STATUS's results (at HL) after a SEEK or RECALIBRATE of unit C:\n- ST0 = $20 (seek end) with the unit, the head bit aside: carry and Z, done;\n- ST0's top two bits 10 (invalid command, so nothing pending): A = 2, NZ;\n- ST0 for another unit: SENSE INTERRUPT STATUS again and its test;\n- this unit not ready (ST0 bit 3): A = 0, Z, no carry; otherwise A = 2, NZ, no carry.\nEntry: HL = the results' count ($E430), C = the unit.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"Seek end + the unit"},
        "8327": {"comment":"ST0"},
        "8328": {"comment":"The same"},
        "8329": {"comment":"...the head bit aside?"},
        "8331": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8333": {"comment":"Its top two bits"},
        "8336": {"comment":"10: nothing pending?"},
        "8340": {"comment":"Another unit's?"},
        "8344": {"comment":"No"},
        "8346": {"comment":"Sense again"},
        "8349": {"comment":"Test that"},
        "8351": {"synopsis":"This unit ended badly: not ready is A = 0 with Z; anything else A = 2.","comment":"Not ready?"},
        "8356": {"comment":"Yes: A = 0, Z"},
        "8357": {"synopsis":"A = 2, NZ, no carry: the seek failed.","comment":"Error 2"},
        "8359": {"comment":"NZ, no carry"},
        "8361": {"synopsis":"Tests a read, write or READ ID result (HL = $E430: +1 ST0, +2 ST1) for the unit and head in\nC:\n- ST0 = C exactly (a normal end), or ST1 = $80 (end of cylinder only, as a one-sector\n  command with EOT = R ends): carry and Z;\n- ST0 bit 3 (not ready): A = 0, Z, no carry;\n- ST1 = $02 (not writable only): A = 1, Z, no carry;\n- otherwise NZ, no carry, A = 3 for ST1 bit 5 (data error), 4 for bit 2 (no data), 5 for bit\n  0 (missing address mark), 7 for anything else.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"ST0"},
        "8363": {"comment":"A normal end for this unit?"},
        "8365": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8366": {"comment":"Not ready?"},
        "8370": {"comment":"A = 0, Z"},
        "8371": {"comment":"ST1"},
        "8373": {"comment":"End of cylinder only?"},
        "8375": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8377": {"comment":"Not writable only?"},
        "8379": {"comment":"A = 1"},
        "8382": {"comment":"3"},
        "8384": {"comment":"...for a data error?"},
        "8387": {"comment":"4"},
        "8388": {"comment":"...for no data?"},
        "8391": {"comment":"5"},
        "8392": {"comment":"...for a missing address mark?"},
        "8395": {"comment":"7: anything else"},
        "8398": {"synopsis":"Clears the 765's pending interrupts: SENSE INTERRUPT STATUS (into $E430) again and again\nuntil ST0's top two bits are 10 (invalid command: none left).\nKeeps AF and HL.","comment":"Kept"},
        "8400": {"comment":"The results"},
        "8403": {"synopsis":"One SENSE INTERRUPT STATUS.","comment":"SENSE INTERRUPT STATUS"},
        "8406": {"comment":"ST0's top bits"},
        "8408": {"comment":"10: none left?"},
        "8412": {"comment":"Back"},
        "8415": {"synopsis":"The 765's SENSE INTERRUPT STATUS, its results read to HL (RESULTS_READ_HL).\nEntry: HL = the results' place.\nExit: A = ST0.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"$08: SENSE INTERRUPT STATUS"},
        "8420": {"comment":"The results"},
        "8422": {"synopsis":"The 765's SENSE DRIVE STATUS for the unit and head in C, its result (ST3) read to $E430.\nExit: A = ST3, HL = $E430.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"$04: SENSE DRIVE STATUS"},
        "8427": {"comment":"The unit and head"},
        "8431": {"synopsis":"Reads the 765's result bytes to $E430 (RESULTS_READ_HL).","comment":"The results' place"},
        "8434": {"synopsis":"Reads the 765's result phase: the bytes to HL + 1 on, while the 765 has bytes for the CPU\n(main status RQM, then DIO set), and their count to HL.\nEntry: HL = the place.\nExit: A = the first result; HL as at entry.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Kept"},
        "8436": {"comment":"The status port"},
        "8439": {"comment":"No bytes yet"},
        "8441": {"comment":"The first byte's place"},
        "8442": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "8443": {"synopsis":"Waits for the 765, then one result byte if it has one.","comment":"Main status"},
        "8445": {"comment":"RQM into the carry"},
        "8446": {"comment":"Wait for it"},
        "8448": {"comment":"DIO clear: no more bytes"},
        "8451": {"comment":"The data port"},
        "8453": {"comment":"A result byte"},
        "8455": {"comment":"The status port again"},
        "8457": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "8459": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "8460": {"comment":"A short wait"},
        "8466": {"synopsis":"The count stored; A = the first result.","comment":"The first byte's place"},
        "8467": {"comment":"A = the first result"},
        "8468": {"comment":"The count's place"},
        "8469": {"comment":"The count"},
        "8473": {"synopsis":"Runs the command block at HL with a read whose execution phase keeps only the first E bytes\n(the low byte of the block's count, +3) and drops the rest (EXEC_READ_PART), then reads the\nresults to $E430.\nEntry: HL = the command block (CMD_WRITE's layout).\nExit: as CMD_WRITE.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"All but the last command byte"},
        "8476": {"comment":"The last byte, then the data in"},
        "8479": {"comment":"The results"},
        "8482": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0193) Runs a command block with a write execution phase: the buffer's bytes are\nsent while the 765 takes them, its bank paged in at $C000 (EXEC_WRITE); then a wait of $E42A\nx 34 T-states and the results to $E430.\nThe block: +0 the bank, +1 the buffer, +3 the byte count, +5 the command's length, +6 on the\ncommand's bytes.\nEntry: HL = the block.\nExit: A = ST0, HL = $E430 (the result count, then the results); interrupts on, the paging\nfrom $5B5C.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"All but the last command byte"},
        "8485": {"comment":"The last byte, then the data out"},
        "8488": {"comment":"The wait after a write"},
        "8491": {"synopsis":"34 T-states a round.","comment":"Round down"},
        "8492": {"comment":"Only time"},
        "8497": {"comment":"The results"},
        "8500": {"synopsis":"Starts a command block: the pending interrupts cleared (INT_CLEAR), then all its command\nbytes but the last sent (FDC_BYTE_OUT).\nEntry: HL = the block.\nExit: A = the last command byte, HL = the buffer, D = the paging byte $5B5C with the block's\nbank in bits 0-2, E = the count's low byte, BC = $7FFD; interrupts off.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Nothing pending"},
        "8503": {"comment":"The paging byte"},
        "8506": {"comment":"...with the bank"},
        "8508": {"comment":"...from +0"},
        "8509": {"comment":"B = the port value"},
        "8510": {"comment":"+1, +2: the buffer"},
        "8514": {"comment":"+3: the count's low byte"},
        "8516": {"comment":"Kept for DE"},
        "8517": {"comment":"+5"},
        "8519": {"comment":"B = the command's length"},
        "8520": {"comment":"+6: the command"},
        "8521": {"comment":"All but the last"},
        "8522": {"synopsis":"One command byte sent.","comment":"A command byte"},
        "8524": {"comment":"Sent"},
        "8527": {"comment":"Next"},
        "8529": {"comment":"A = the last byte"},
        "8530": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "8531": {"comment":"D = the port value, E = the count"},
        "8532": {"comment":"The paging port"},
        "8535": {"comment":"Interrupts off for the transfer"},
        "8537": {"synopsis":"The 765's READ ID for the unit and head in C, with the MF bit from bit 6 of A, the pending\ninterrupts cleared first; results to $E430.\nEntry: A = the 765 flags, C = the unit and head.\nExit: A = ST0, HL = $E430.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"Nothing pending"},
        "8540": {"comment":"MF only"},
        "8542": {"comment":"$0A: READ ID"},
        "8547": {"comment":"The unit and head"},
        "8551": {"comment":"The results"},
        "8554": {"synopsis":"Sends A to the 765's data register (port $3FFD) when it asks: waits for RQM (main status bit\n7, port $2FFD); when DIO (bit 6) says the 765 has a byte for the CPU, A is not sent.\nEntry: A = the byte.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Kept"},
        "8556": {"comment":"D = the byte"},
        "8557": {"comment":"The status port"},
        "8560": {"synopsis":"Waits for RQM.","comment":"Main status"},
        "8562": {"comment":"RQM into the carry"},
        "8563": {"comment":"Wait"},
        "8565": {"comment":"DIO: the 765 sending?"},
        "8568": {"comment":"The data port"},
        "8570": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "8572": {"comment":"A short wait"},
        "8574": {"synopsis":"BC and DE back.","comment":"Back"},
        "8577": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0196) Turns the disk motor on: the time-out count at $E600 cleared, so\nMOTOR_TIMEOUT leaves the motor alone; when $5B67's bit 3 is clear, it is set (PORT_1FFD_SET)\nand the drive gets $E428 x about 0.1 s to come up to speed (13,640 rounds of 26 T-states\neach).\nKeeps AF and BC.","comment":"Kept"},
        "8579": {"comment":"No time-out running"},
        "8583": {"comment":"The copy of port $1FFD"},
        "8586": {"comment":"Motor on already?"},
        "8590": {"comment":"Bit 3: the motor"},
        "8592": {"comment":"On"},
        "8595": {"comment":"The start-up wait"},
        "8598": {"synopsis":"About 0.1 s, $E428 times.","comment":"Rounds left"},
        "8599": {"comment":"13,640 x 26 T-states"},
        "8602": {"synopsis":"One round of the 0.1 s.","comment":"Count down"},
        "8605": {"comment":"Until 0"},
        "8607": {"comment":"The next 0.1 s"},
        "8608": {"comment":"Rounds left?"},
        "8611": {"synopsis":"AF and BC back.","comment":"Back"},
        "8614": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0199) Starts the motor's time-out: the count at $E600 = $E429 when the motor is\non ($5B67 bit 3), 0 when not; MOTOR_TIMEOUT counts it down every second frame and turns the\nmotor off at 0.\nKeeps AF.","comment":"Kept"},
        "8615": {"comment":"No count"},
        "8616": {"comment":"...while it is set"},
        "8619": {"comment":"Motor on?"},
        "8624": {"comment":"No: no count"},
        "8626": {"comment":"The time-out"},
        "8629": {"comment":"For MOTOR_TIMEOUT"},
        "8632": {"synopsis":"AF back.","comment":"Back"},
        "8634": {"synopsis":"Writes A to port $1FFD and to its copy $5B67; interrupts are left as they are. Called from\n$2190 and $3EF0.\nEntry: A = the value.\nKeeps BC.","comment":"Kept"},
        "8635": {"comment":"The port"},
        "8638": {"comment":"The copy"},
        "8641": {"comment":"Out"},
        "8645": {"synopsis":"Sends the command's last byte (A), pages the bank in (port $7FFD = D) and reads the\nexecution phase while the 765 is executing (main status bit 5): the first E bytes go to the\nbuffer at HL (E = 0 keeps 256), the rest are read and dropped; then EXEC_END.\nEntry: as CMD_SEND_HEAD leaves it.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The last command byte"},
        "8648": {"comment":"The bank in"},
        "8650": {"comment":"The status port"},
        "8653": {"comment":"D = the execution bit"},
        "8655": {"comment":"Wait"},
        "8657": {"synopsis":"One byte to the buffer.","comment":"The data port"},
        "8659": {"comment":"To the buffer"},
        "8661": {"comment":"The status port"},
        "8663": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "8664": {"comment":"All kept: drop the rest"},
        "8667": {"synopsis":"Waits for the 765; one more byte while it is executing.","comment":"Main status"},
        "8669": {"comment":"Wait for RQM"},
        "8672": {"comment":"Still executing?"},
        "8673": {"comment":"A byte"},
        "8676": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8678": {"synopsis":"One byte read and dropped.","comment":"The data port"},
        "8680": {"comment":"Dropped"},
        "8682": {"comment":"The status port"},
        "8684": {"synopsis":"Waits for the 765; one more byte to drop while it is executing.","comment":"Main status"},
        "8686": {"comment":"Wait for RQM"},
        "8689": {"comment":"Still executing?"},
        "8690": {"comment":"Drop it"},
        "8693": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8695": {"synopsis":"Sends the command's last byte (A), pages the bank in (port $7FFD = D) and reads every byte\nof the execution phase into the buffer at HL, while main status bit 5 is set; then EXEC_END.\nEntry: as CMD_SEND_HEAD leaves it.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"The last command byte"},
        "8698": {"comment":"The bank in"},
        "8700": {"comment":"The status port"},
        "8703": {"comment":"D = the execution bit"},
        "8705": {"comment":"Wait"},
        "8707": {"synopsis":"One byte to the buffer.","comment":"The data port"},
        "8709": {"comment":"To the buffer"},
        "8711": {"comment":"The status port"},
        "8713": {"synopsis":"Waits for the 765; one more byte while it is executing.","comment":"Main status"},
        "8715": {"comment":"Wait for RQM"},
        "8718": {"comment":"Still executing?"},
        "8719": {"comment":"A byte"},
        "8722": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8724": {"synopsis":"Sends the command's last byte (A), pages the bank in (port $7FFD = D) and sends the buffer's\nbytes from HL while the 765 is executing (main status bit 5); then EXEC_END.\nEntry: as CMD_SEND_HEAD leaves it.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"The last command byte"},
        "8727": {"comment":"The bank in"},
        "8729": {"comment":"The status port"},
        "8732": {"comment":"D = the execution bit"},
        "8734": {"comment":"Wait"},
        "8736": {"synopsis":"One byte from the buffer.","comment":"OUTI lowers it to $3F: the data port"},
        "8738": {"comment":"From the buffer"},
        "8740": {"comment":"The status port"},
        "8742": {"synopsis":"Waits for the 765; one more byte while it is executing.","comment":"Main status"},
        "8744": {"comment":"Wait for RQM"},
        "8747": {"comment":"Still executing?"},
        "8748": {"comment":"A byte"},
        "8751": {"synopsis":"Pages back the bank in $5B5C and turns interrupts on.","comment":"The paging byte"},
        "8754": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "8757": {"comment":"The bank back"},
        "8759": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "8761": {"synopsis":"Key table, main: 39 bytes, the code of each key but CAPS SHIFT, by READ_KEYS's key number: B\nH Y 6 5 T G V, N J U 7 4 R F C, M K I 8 3 E D X, SYMBOL SHIFT ($0E) L O 9 2 W S Z, SPACE\nENTER ($0D) P 0 1 Q A. KEY_MAIN_CODE reads it at $2239 + key number.\nThe key tables after it run to $22C1; each is indexed from its start less its first code."},
        "8800": {"synopsis":"Key table, E mode letters: 26 tokens for A-Z, read from $221F + the letter: READ BIN LPRINT\nDATA TAN SGN ABS SQR CODE VAL LEN USR PI INKEY$ PEEK TAB SIN INT RESTORE RND CHR$ LLIST COS\nEXP STR$ LN (spelt as in the 48K ROM's KEYWORD_TABLE)."},
        "8826": {"synopsis":"Key table, E mode letters with a shift key: 26 bytes for A-Z, read from $2239 + the letter:\n~ BRIGHT PAPER \\ ATN { } CIRCLE IN VAL$ SCREEN$ ATTR INVERSE OVER OUT, $7F for P, ASN VERIFY\n| MERGE ] FLASH ACS INK [ BEEP."},
        "8852": {"synopsis":"Key table, CAPS SHIFT digits: 10 control codes for 0-9, read from $2264 + the digit: $0C $07\n$06 $04 $05 $08 $0A $0B $09 $0F, the manual's DELETE, EDIT, CAPS LOCK, TRUE VIDEO, INV.\nVIDEO, the four cursor keys (5 left, 6 down, 7 up, 8 right) and GRAPHICS. In G mode, 0 and 9\ngive these codes too."},
        "8862": {"synopsis":"Key table, SYMBOL SHIFT letters: 26 bytes for A-Z, read from $225D + the letter: STOP * ?\nSTEP >= TO THEN ^ AT - + = . , ; \" <= < NOT > OR / <> ` AND :."},
        "8888": {"synopsis":"Key table, E mode SYMBOL SHIFT digits: 10 tokens for 0-9, read from $2288 + the digit:\nFORMAT, DEF FN, FN, LINE, OPEN #, CLOSE #, MOVE, ERASE, POINT, CAT. SHOW_MESSAGE follows."},
        "8898": {"synopsis":"Has message B of COLOUR_MESSAGES shown by a routine of another ROM:\n1. A = B, with Z set by the XOR (SHOW_INSERT_DISK enters at $22C4 with A = 10 and NZ).\n2. The words at CURCHL ($5C51), FLAGS ($5C3B) and FLAGS2 ($5C6A) are kept on the stack.\n3. $DB22 = COLOUR_MESSAGES and the message is built at $DB29 (BUILD_MESSAGE).\n4. With HL = $DB29 and A and F as in step 1, the routine at $3FF7 is called in the ROM that\nclearing bit 2 of port $1FFD pages in, through L3E00 and the word after its CALL.\n5. The three words go back.\nReached from $0002.\nEntry: B = the message, C = the drive letter, D and E the numbers it prints.\nExit: A and F as the other ROM's routine leaves them.\nObserved: CAT with no disk in drive A showed \"Drive A: track 0 sector 0\", \"No data\" and\n\"Retry, Ignore or Cancel?\" on three lines; C gave the report \"No data, 0:1\".","comment":"Z for the other ROM"},
        "8899": {"comment":"A = the message"},
        "8900": {"synopsis":"Message A, the flags as they are (SHOW_MESSAGE).","comment":"HL kept"},
        "8901": {"comment":"CURCHL kept"},
        "8905": {"comment":"FLAGS and TV_FLAG kept"},
        "8910": {"comment":"FLAGS2 and DF_SZ kept"},
        "8915": {"comment":"The table: COLOUR_MESSAGES"},
        "8921": {"comment":"Message and flags kept"},
        "8922": {"comment":"Built at $DB29, HL on it"},
        "8925": {"comment":"The flags back"},
        "8926": {"comment":"The routine in the other ROM"},
        "8929": {"synopsis":"The word after CALL L3E00: $3FF7, the routine's address in the other ROM."},
        "8931": {"comment":"FLAGS2, DF_SZ back"},
        "8935": {"comment":"FLAGS, TV_FLAG back"},
        "8939": {"comment":"CURCHL back"},
        "8944": {"synopsis":"The disk-error messages SHOW_MESSAGE uses, fifteen of them, each ended by $FF and read by\nMESSAGE_TEXT through $DB22: the codes of DOS_MESSAGES, $0D for a new line, $FB for the\nwarning ink and $FA for the ink back (MESSAGE_PUT).\nMessages 0-9 are those of errors 0-9: Not ready, Write protected, Seek fail, Data error, No\ndata, Missing address mark, Bad format, Unknown error, Disk changed, please replace, Disk\nunsuitable; each starts with (11), (12) or (13), and those without (13) add a new line and\nthe warning ink; each ends with a new line and (14).\n10 asks for the disk for drive $FE to be put in and a key pressed. 11-14 are pieces:\n11 \"Drive X:\", 12 (11) \" track N\", 13 (12) \" sector N\", a new line and the warning ink,\n14 the ink back and \"Retry, Ignore or Cancel?\"."},
        "9379": {"synopsis":"Counts the hard disk units that answer (jump table at $00A0, entry $00A3).\n1. HD_UNIT_PROBE is tried on unit 0 and then unit 1, with the 512-byte buffer at $ED11 in\n   RAM bank 0.\n2. Each unit that gives A = $42 is counted.\nExit: A = the count (0-2), also stored at $DF9D.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"B = 2 units to try, C = 0 found"},
        "9382": {"synopsis":"Probes unit 2 - B.","comment":"Keep the count"},
        "9383": {"comment":"C = the unit: 0, then 1"},
        "9385": {"comment":"2 - B"},
        "9387": {"comment":"Buffer in RAM bank 0"},
        "9389": {"comment":"HL = the 512-byte buffer"},
        "9392": {"comment":"Probe the unit"},
        "9395": {"comment":"Count back"},
        "9396": {"comment":"Did it answer?"},
        "9400": {"comment":"Yes: one more unit"},
        "9401": {"synopsis":"Next unit.","comment":"Next unit"},
        "9403": {"comment":"A = the units found"},
        "9404": {"comment":"Kept at $DF9D"},
        "9408": {"synopsis":"Writes $A0, unit 0's select byte, to port $FEEF.\nChanges: A, BC.","comment":"Port $FEEF"},
        "9411": {"comment":"Unit 0's select byte"},
        "9413": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "9416": {"synopsis":"Finds out whether hard disk unit C answers and reads what it reports (DOS_JUMPS $01A2).\n1. $DF9E (HD_WAIT_STATUS's poll count) is set to 2000.\n2. $A0 (unit 0) or $B0 (unit 1) goes to port $FEEF (HD_SELECT_REG).\n3. Every value 0-255 written to port $DEEF must read back the same; otherwise A = 0.\n4. $EC goes to port $FFEF, and the 256 bytes that follow are read into the buffer\n   (HD_READ_DATA).\n5. For D = 1, 2, ...: sector 1 of cylinder D x 256 is asked for (0 to port $EEEF, D to\n   $EFEF, 1 to $DFEF and $DEEF, $20 to $FFEF). It stops at the first D for which port $FFEF,\n   once bit 7 clears, does not show bit 4 set and bit 1 clear, or whose 256 bytes (thrown\n   away) do not end with bits 7, 3 and 0 clear. D - 1 is stored at buffer + 256.\n6. $DF9E is set back to 0.\nEntry: C = the unit (0 or 1), B = the buffer's RAM bank, HL = the buffer.\nExit: carry clear in every case; A = $42 when the unit answered (HL = buffer + 512), else 0\n(no answer, time-out) or 7.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"Unit and bank kept"},
        "9418": {"comment":"Time limit: 2000 polls a round"},
        "9421": {"comment":"For HD_WAIT_STATUS"},
        "9425": {"comment":"Unit 1?"},
        "9426": {"comment":"Unit 0?"},
        "9427": {"comment":"Unit 0's select byte"},
        "9429": {"comment":"Yes: $A0"},
        "9431": {"comment":"Unit 1's select byte"},
        "9433": {"synopsis":"Unit select byte A to port $FEEF.","comment":"Select it, wait for it"},
        "9436": {"comment":"No answer?"},
        "9438": {"comment":"Try every value 0-255"},
        "9440": {"synopsis":"Writes E to port $DEEF and checks that it reads back.","comment":"Port $DEEF"},
        "9443": {"comment":"Write it"},
        "9445": {"comment":"Read it back"},
        "9447": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "9448": {"comment":"No: A = 0"},
        "9450": {"comment":"Next value"},
        "9451": {"comment":"All 256 tried?"},
        "9453": {"comment":"Command $EC"},
        "9455": {"comment":"to port $FFEF"},
        "9458": {"comment":"Command sent"},
        "9460": {"comment":"Carry: read its answer"},
        "9461": {"synopsis":"With carry: the 256 bytes after command $EC into the buffer.","comment":"Registers back"},
        "9462": {"comment":"B = the bank, C = the unit"},
        "9463": {"comment":"The 256 bytes into the buffer"},
        "9466": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9468": {"comment":"Keep the registers and the buffer"},
        "9470": {"comment":"HL = the buffer + 256"},
        "9471": {"comment":"D = the cylinder high byte tried"},
        "9473": {"synopsis":"Asks for sector 1 of cylinder (D + 1) x 256.","comment":"Cylinder low byte 0"},
        "9474": {"comment":"to port $EEEF"},
        "9477": {"comment":"Cylinder low byte written"},
        "9479": {"comment":"Sector 1 to port $DFEF"},
        "9482": {"comment":"A = 1"},
        "9483": {"comment":"Sector written"},
        "9485": {"comment":"Count 1 to port $DEEF"},
        "9488": {"comment":"Count written"},
        "9490": {"comment":"Next cylinder high byte"},
        "9491": {"comment":"to port $EFEF"},
        "9494": {"comment":"Cylinder high byte written"},
        "9496": {"comment":"All 255 tried?"},
        "9498": {"comment":"Port $FFEF"},
        "9501": {"comment":"Command $20"},
        "9503": {"comment":"Command sent"},
        "9505": {"comment":"A moment"},
        "9506": {"synopsis":"Waits for bit 7 of port $FFEF to clear.","comment":"Read port $FFEF"},
        "9508": {"comment":"Bit 7 into carry"},
        "9509": {"comment":"Still busy?"},
        "9511": {"comment":"Bits 4 and 1"},
        "9513": {"comment":"Bit 4 set, bit 1 clear?"},
        "9515": {"comment":"No: the probe ends"},
        "9517": {"comment":"Port $CEEF"},
        "9519": {"comment":"Keep the count tried"},
        "9520": {"comment":"256 bytes"},
        "9523": {"comment":"To $0000: thrown away"},
        "9525": {"comment":"Read them"},
        "9528": {"comment":"Wait: bits 7, 3, 0 all clear"},
        "9531": {"comment":"Wait for the end"},
        "9534": {"comment":"D back"},
        "9535": {"comment":"Worked: try the next one"},
        "9537": {"synopsis":"Stores the number of steps that worked at buffer + 256; A = $42.","comment":"D = the steps that worked"},
        "9538": {"comment":"HL = the buffer + 256"},
        "9539": {"comment":"B = the bank"},
        "9540": {"comment":"The buffer's bank in"},
        "9541": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9544": {"comment":"Stored after the 256 bytes"},
        "9545": {"comment":"HL = the buffer + 512"},
        "9546": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "9547": {"comment":"Bank 7 back"},
        "9552": {"comment":"A = $42: the unit answered"},
        "9554": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "9555": {"synopsis":"$DF9E back to 0.","comment":"Keep HL"},
        "9556": {"comment":"Time limit back to 65536"},
        "9559": {"comment":"For HD_WAIT_STATUS"},
        "9564": {"synopsis":"Port $DEEF did not keep a value: A = 0, carry clear.","comment":"A = 0: no answer"},
        "9566": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "9567": {"comment":"Out, carry clear"},
        "9569": {"synopsis":"Reads 512-byte block C:DE of a hard disk partition (jump table at $00A0, entry $00AC; also\nfrom $315E): the 256-byte sectors 2 x block and 2 x block + 1 (HD_SECTOR_READ).\nEntry: IX = the partition record, C:DE = the block, B = the buffer's RAM bank, HL = the\nbuffer.\nExit: carry, HL past the 512 bytes; or carry clear and A = 0 (time-out), 2 (outside the\npartition) or 7 (error bit). With bit 7 of C set: A = 2 and NZ, carry not changed.\nChanges: AF, HL; RAM bank 7 is paged in at the end.","comment":"Block over 23 bits?"},
        "9571": {"comment":"Then error 2"},
        "9573": {"comment":"Bit 7 set: error 2"},
        "9574": {"comment":"Keep the block"},
        "9576": {"comment":"C:DE = 2 x the block"},
        "9578": {"comment":"(2 x C:DE)"},
        "9582": {"comment":"Read its first sector"},
        "9585": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9587": {"comment":"Then the second"},
        "9588": {"comment":"Read the second"},
        "9591": {"synopsis":"Registers back.","comment":"Registers back"},
        "9592": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "9594": {"synopsis":"Reads 256-byte sector C:DE of partition IX into HL in RAM bank B: the registers set up\n(HD_SECTOR_SETUP), $20 to port $FFEF, then HD_READ_DATA.\nExit: carry, HL + 256; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"Registers for sector C:DE"},
        "9597": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9598": {"comment":"Command $20"},
        "9601": {"comment":"to port $FFEF"},
        "9604": {"comment":"Command sent"},
        "9607": {"synopsis":"Reads the 256 bytes a command has made ready.\n1. Waits until bits 7, 3 and 0 of port $FFEF read 0, 1, 0 (HD_WAIT_STATUS).\n2. Reads 256 bytes from port $CEEF into HL with RAM bank B paged in; bank 7 back.\n3. Waits until bits 7, 3 and 0 all read 0; error 7 if bit 0 is then set.\nEntry: B = the bank, HL = the buffer.\nExit: carry, HL + 256; or carry clear and A = 0 (time-out) or 7.","comment":"Keep the buffer"},
        "9608": {"comment":"Wait: bit 7 clear, bit 3 set, bit 0 clear"},
        "9611": {"comment":"Wait for the data"},
        "9614": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "9615": {"comment":"Not ready?"},
        "9618": {"comment":"The buffer's bank in"},
        "9619": {"comment":"Paged in"},
