        "9846": {"comment":"Read the status"},
        "9849": {"comment":"Bit 0 set?"},
        "9851": {"comment":"No: success"},
        "9853": {"comment":"Yes: error 7"},
        "9855": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "9857": {"synopsis":"Polls port $FFEF until its bits in mask H equal L.\nGives up with A = 7 when bit 7 is clear and bit 0 set, or with A = 0 after 9 rounds of the\ncount at $DF9E (0 counts as 65536).\nEntry: H = the mask, L = the bits wanted.\nExit: carry when they came; else carry clear and A = 0 or 7.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Registers kept"},
        "9859": {"comment":"9 rounds"},
        "9861": {"synopsis":"A round of polls.","comment":"Keep the round count"},
        "9862": {"comment":"DE = polls a round"},
        "9866": {"comment":"Port $FFEF"},
        "9869": {"synopsis":"One poll of port $FFEF.","comment":"Status"},
        "9871": {"comment":"The bits looked at"},
        "9872": {"comment":"As wanted?"},
        "9873": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "9874": {"comment":"Matched: out with carry"},
        "9876": {"comment":"Busy?"},
        "9878": {"comment":"Yes: keep waiting"},
        "9880": {"comment":"Error bit set?"},
        "9882": {"comment":"Yes: error 7"},
        "9884": {"synopsis":"Counts the poll.","comment":"Count the poll"},
        "9885": {"comment":"Round over?"},
        "9886": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "9887": {"comment":"No: poll again"},
        "9889": {"comment":"Round count back"},
        "9890": {"comment":"Next round"},
        "9891": {"comment":"All 9 rounds?"},
        "9893": {"comment":"(balance the stack)"},
        "9894": {"comment":"Time-out: A = 0"},
        "9896": {"synopsis":"Carry clear.","comment":"Carry clear"},
        "9897": {"synopsis":"Registers back.","comment":"Drop the round count"},
        "9898": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "9901": {"synopsis":"Error bit: A = 7.","comment":"Error 7"},
        "9903": {"comment":"Out, carry clear"},
        "9905": {"synopsis":"Sets the registers for 256-byte sector C:DE of partition IX (also from $310A, $3952).\n1. (IX+$10), the unit select byte, to port $FEEF (HD_SELECT_HEAD).\n2. The sector is divided by the unit's sectors per cylinder (bytes 4-5 of $E883, or of $E88D\n   when bit 4 of (IX+$10) is set) and the rest by its sectors per track (byte 3): cylinder,\n   head, sector.\n3. The partition's first head (IX+3) is added, wrapping at the unit's head count (byte 2)\n   into the next cylinder; then its first cylinder (IX+1, IX+2).\n4. Error 2 past its last cylinder (IX+4, IX+5), or on that cylinder past its last head\n   (IX+6).\n5. Head OR (IX+$10) to port $FEEF, sector + 1 to $DFEF, 1 to $DEEF, the cylinder to $EEEF\n   (low) and $EFEF (high).\nExit: carry; or carry clear and A = 0 (time-out), 2 or 7.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Registers kept"},
        "9908": {"comment":"Head 0 for now"},
        "9909": {"comment":"Select the unit, wait for it"},
        "9912": {"comment":"No answer?"},
        "9915": {"comment":"HL:DE = the sector"},
        "9916": {"comment":"HL = C, the top part"},
        "9918": {"comment":"Unit 0's record"},
        "9921": {"comment":"Unit 1?"},
        "9927": {"comment":"Unit 1's record"},
