        "10097": {"comment":"The low byte"},
        "10098": {"comment":"inverted"},
        "10099": {"comment":"C = the low byte"},
        "10100": {"comment":"DE = the remainder"},
        "10102": {"synopsis":"Gets the next sector of a multi-sector read ready (from $1A3E, $1A49, $3594, $3882).\n1. When bit 7 of (IX+0) is set: (IX+0) to port $FEEF (tried until it answers), (IX+1) to\n   $EFEF, (IX+2) to $EEEF, (IX+3) to $DFEF; bit 7 of (IX+5) cleared; then (IX+4) to $DEEF\n   and $20 to $FFEF.\n2. Either way (IX-1) is counted down (HSN_COUNT).\n3. HD_WAIT_DATA.\nExit: BC = $CEEF, DE = $0100, for HD_DATA_IN.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"New command needed?"},
        "10106": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10108": {"comment":"No: count the sector"},
        "10111": {"comment":"Wait for its data"},
        "10113": {"synopsis":"A new command from the bytes at IX.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "10115": {"comment":"Old HL stacked"},
        "10116": {"synopsis":"Byte 0 to port $FEEF until it answers.","comment":"Byte 0 to port $FEEF"},
