        "10254": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "10257": {"synopsis":"Gives the fixed number $0106 (jump table at $00A0, entry $00A0).\nExit: DE = $0106, carry set.","comment":"DE = $0106"},
        "10260": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "10262": {"synopsis":"Points IX at the record of hard disk unit A (jump table at $00A0, entry $00A9): $E883 for\nunit 0, $E88D for unit 1.\nEntry: A = the unit.\nExit: carry and IX = the record; carry clear and A = $16 when A is over 1 or the unit has no\ncylinders (bytes 0-1 zero).\nChanges: AF, IX.","comment":"Bit 0: the unit"},
        "10264": {"comment":"Unit 0's record"},
        "10268": {"comment":"Unit 0"},
        "10270": {"comment":"Unit 1's record"},
        "10274": {"synopsis":"A over 1, or no cylinders: error $16.","comment":"A over 1?"},
        "10275": {"comment":"Then error $16"},
        "10277": {"comment":"Over 1: error"},
        "10278": {"comment":"Any cylinders?"},
        "10281": {"comment":"(high byte)"},
        "10284": {"comment":"No: error $16"},
        "10286": {"comment":"None: error"},
        "10287": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "10289": {"synopsis":"Sets up the hard disk work area and applies the settings kept on unit 0 (jump table at\n$00A0, entry $00A6; the end of $01A8's set-up).\n1. The four partition records ($E897-$E8E2) and the two drive records ($E8E3-$EB42) are\n   cleared.\n2. With $DF9E = 2000, each unit's system partition is looked for (HD_UNIT_FIND_SYS); unit 0\n   is selected; $DF9E back to 0.\n3. With CAPS SHIFT held, nothing more is done.\n4. Byte $28 of unit 0's entry 0 (L3075) goes to $EC0F, $EC11, $5C8F and $5C48; its bits 3-5\n   to the border; and every attribute byte at $5800-$5AFF that is $38 becomes it. Byte $29\n   goes to $5C8D. Bit 6 of $5B66 is cleared.\n5. Bytes $2A-$2C of entry 0, where not zero, go to L3370 with L = \"A\", \"B\" and \"M\"; bytes\n   $2D-$2F, where not zero, to L3227 as L with A = 2, 3, 4.\n6. For each entry BC of each unit whose byte $3C is not zero, L3227 is called with A = the\n   unit and L = that byte; a unit ends at error $38 or $16.\n7. Byte $30 of entry 0, if not zero, goes to L012D; if that succeeds it is stored at $5B79\n   and $5B7A.\nExit: carry.","comment":"The four partition records"},
        "10292": {"comment":"(next byte)"},
        "10295": {"comment":"76 bytes"},
        "10298": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "10300": {"comment":"Spread the zero"},
