        "10560": {"synopsis":"Sets up a unit's records and looks for its system partition.\n1. The record at DE gets the 16 bytes at $29B0 (in use, everything else 0), select byte A at\n   $10, entry 0 at $11-$12.\n2. The unit record at HL gets the 8 bytes at $29BB (1 cylinder, 2 heads, 2 sectors per\n   track, 4 sectors per cylinder) and DE at bytes 8-9.\n3. The entry named at $29C3 is looked for (PART_FIND_NAME); if it is not found with type 1,\n   the search is repeated with the record moved to head 1.\n4. Found: bytes $10-$1F of the entry go to the record, bytes $20-$27 to the unit record. Not\n   found: the record's byte 0 and the unit's cylinders are cleared.\nEntry: HL = the unit record, DE = the record, A = $A0 (unit 0) or $B0 (unit 1).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; $EF11-$EF50.","comment":"Keep the records"},
