        "10762": {"synopsis":"Lays out a new partition table on unit A (jump table at $00A0, entry $00B2).\n1. Error $3B when partitions of the unit are mapped (HD_UNIT_MAPPED).\n2. If the unit has no cylinders yet, the unused record found becomes its system record\n   (error $3C when none).\n3. The unit record: DE cylinders, B heads, C sectors per track, (B AND $7F) x C per\n   cylinder, HL the last entry.\n4. The system record: type 1, from cylinder 0, head 0 (head 1 when bit 7 of B is set; the\n   flag then cleared), to the head that holds block HL / 8; its size (PART_SIZE_SET); select\n   byte $A0 + 16 x unit; entry 0.\n5. The system partition is filled with zeros (PART_REC_FILL).\n6. Entry 1: type $FF, from the next head to the disk's last head of its last cylinder.\n7. Entry 0: the name at $29C3, the record's bytes 0-$0A at $10-$1A, the unit record's 8\n   bytes at $20-$27, $38 at $28 and $29.\nEntry: A = the unit, DE = cylinders, B = heads (bit 7: start on head 1), C = sectors per\ntrack, HL = the last entry number.\nExit: carry; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX; $EF11-$EF50, $ED11-$EF10.","comment":"Registers kept"},
