        "11755": {"synopsis":"Makes a partition from the 64-byte entry at HL (jump table at $00A0, entry $00B8).\n1. Error $39 when an entry has its name (PART_FIND_NAME).\n2. The smallest free entry (type $FF) that holds its size (bytes $17-$19, the last block) is\n   found (PART_BEST_FIT); error $1A when none.\n3. The new end is worked out from the free entry's start (BLOCK_CYL_HEAD). If it is not the\n   free entry's end, an unused entry (type 0) becomes a free one for the rest (error $1A\n   when none).\n4. The free entry is cut to the new end and resized; its bytes $11-$1F go to the new entry,\n   which is written in its place.\nEntry: A = the unit, HL = the entry.\nExit: carry; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; $EF11-$EF90.","comment":"IX kept"},
