        "12298": {"comment":"... as the free entry's end"},
        "12301": {"comment":"Then its size"},
        "12303": {"synopsis":"The free entry starts just after the entry being freed: the free entry's start (bytes\n$11-$13, $EF62-$EF64) becomes the freed entry's start ($EF22-$EF24), joining the two.","comment":"The freed entry's start head"},
        "12306": {"comment":"... as the free entry's start"},
        "12309": {"comment":"The freed entry's start cylinder"},
        "12312": {"comment":"... as the free entry's start"},
        "12315": {"synopsis":"The joined free entry at $EF51: its size recounted ($2F05), then written back as entry BC;\nthe freed entry (its number on the stack) is cleared to all zeros on the disk, and the\njoined\nentry, copied to $EF11, takes its place in a new search from entry 0 (back to $2FB9), so\nthat\nfree space on both sides of it is joined too.","comment":"The joined free entry"},
        "12318": {"comment":"Its size from its start and end"},
        "12321": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "12323": {"comment":"Written back as entry BC"},
        "12326": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "12328": {"comment":"DE = the freed entry's number"},
        "12330": {"comment":"The joined entry's number kept instead"},
        "12333": {"comment":"64 bytes"},
        "12335": {"comment":"The freed entry cleared"},
        "12338": {"synopsis":"Clears B bytes at HL.","comment":"A zero"},
        "12341": {"comment":"For all 64"},
        "12343": {"comment":"BC = the freed entry's number"},
        "12345": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "12346": {"comment":"... cleared on the disk"},
        "12352": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "12354": {"comment":"The joined entry"},
        "12357": {"comment":"... becomes the entry to free"},
        "12363": {"comment":"64 bytes"},
        "12365": {"comment":"A new search with it"},
        "12368": {"synopsis":"Leaves with the error in A (carry clear): the unit and the entry number dropped, IX back.","comment":"The unit dropped"},
        "12369": {"comment":"The entry number dropped"},
        "12370": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "12373": {"synopsis":"The next entry of the table to look at, until the entry number wraps round to 0.","comment":"The next entry"},
        "12374": {"comment":"Wrapped round to 0?"},
        "12376": {"comment":"No: look at it"},
        "12379": {"synopsis":"No more free space next to it: the entry at $EF11 is marked free (type $FF, $EF21), its name\ncleared, and written back as the entry on the stack; IX back.\nExit: carry as the write leaves it.","comment":"Type $FF: free space"},
        "12384": {"comment":"Its name"},
        "12387": {"comment":"16 bytes"},
        "12389": {"synopsis":"Clears B bytes at HL.","comment":"A zero"},
        "12392": {"comment":"For all 16"},
        "12394": {"comment":"The entry"},
        "12397": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "12398": {"comment":"Its number"},
        "12399": {"comment":"Written to the disk"},
        "12402": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "12405": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00D3) Reads one byte of the 32 kept for the partition's own use in entry BC\nof unit A's partition table (bytes $20-$3F of the entry).\nEntry: A = the unit (0 or 1), BC = the entry, L = the byte (0-$1F; higher numbers wrap).\nExit: carry set and A = the byte, Z when it is 0; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; the entry buffer at $EF11.","comment":"HL at the byte"},
        "12408": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "12409": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "12410": {"comment":"Z when 0"},
        "12411": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "12413": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00D6) Writes byte H into the 32 kept for the partition's own use in entry BC of\nunit A's partition table (bytes $20-$3F of the entry): the entry is read, changed and\nwritten\nback.\nEntry: A = the unit (0 or 1), BC = the entry, L = the byte (0-$1F; higher numbers wrap), H =\nthe value.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; the entry buffer at $EF11.","comment":"The unit kept"},
        "12414": {"comment":"HL at the byte, A = H"},
        "12417": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "12419": {"comment":"The new value in"},
        "12420": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "12421": {"comment":"The entry"},
        "12424": {"comment":"... written back"},
        "12428": {"synopsis":"The read failed: the unit dropped, the error in A.","comment":"The unit dropped"},
        "12430": {"synopsis":"Reads entry BC of unit A's partition table into $EF11 ($2B72) and points at one of its 32\nbytes for the partition's own use.\nEntry: A = the unit, BC = the entry, L = the byte, H = a value.\nExit: carry set, HL = $EF31 + (L AND $1F), A = H; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"The byte number kept"},
        "12431": {"comment":"The entry buffer"},
        "12434": {"comment":"Entry BC of unit A read"},
        "12437": {"comment":"The byte number back"},
        "12438": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "12439": {"comment":"The byte, 0-$1F"},
        "12443": {"comment":"A = the value given in H"},
        "12446": {"comment":"From the entry's byte $20"},
        "12450": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "12452": {"synopsis":"Checks that the partition open at IX (a slot of the table at $E897) is of type 2, the kind\nread and written a record at a time.\nEntry: IX = the open partition.\nExit: carry set if so; carry clear and A = $3D if not.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"The partition's type"},
        "12455": {"comment":"Type 2?"},
        "12457": {"comment":"Carry: yes"},
        "12459": {"comment":"Error $3D"},
        "12461": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "12463": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00E8) Returns the number of the next record of the type-2 partition open at IX\n(its slot's bytes $0C-$0D).\nEntry: IX = the open partition.\nExit: carry set and BC = the record number; carry clear and A = $3D for another type.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Type 2?"},
        "12467": {"comment":"BC = the next record"},
        "12473": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "12475": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00EB) Sets the next record of the type-2 partition open at IX (its slot's bytes\n$0C-$0D) to BC, which may not be above the record count in bytes $0E-$0F.\nEntry: IX = the open partition, BC = the record number.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = $3D for another type, $15 for a number\ntoo high.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Type 2?"},
        "12479": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "12480": {"comment":"HL = the number of records"},
        "12486": {"comment":"BC above it?"},
        "12490": {"comment":"Carry when not"},
        "12491": {"comment":"Error $15 if so"},
        "12494": {"comment":"The next record = BC"},
        "12500": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "12502": {"synopsis":"Works out the first sector of the next record of the type-2 partition open at IX and moves\nits record pointer on: the pointer (bytes $0C-$0D) starts again at 0 when it is above the\nrecord count (bytes $0E-$0F); the sector is the pointer times the sectors to a record (byte\n$0B, $2F80).\nEntry: IX = the open partition.\nExit: carry set and C:DE = the record's first sector in the partition, the pointer one up;\ncarry clear and A = $3D for another type. B and HL kept.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.","comment":"Type 2?"},
        "12506": {"comment":"B kept"},
        "12508": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "12509": {"comment":"DE = the next record"},
        "12515": {"comment":"HL = the number of records"},
        "12521": {"comment":"Above it?"},
        "12524": {"comment":"No: keep it"},
        "12526": {"comment":"Yes: from record 0"},
        "12529": {"synopsis":"DE = the record to use: its first sector (DE times byte $0B into A:DE, then C), and the\npointer stored one past it.","comment":"The record kept"},
        "12530": {"comment":"B = the sectors to a record"},
        "12533": {"comment":"A:DE = the record's first sector"},
        "12536": {"comment":"C = its high byte"},
        "12537": {"comment":"The record"},
        "12538": {"comment":"... plus one"},
        "12539": {"comment":"... is the next record"},
        "12545": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "12546": {"comment":"B back"},
        "12548": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "12550": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00E2) Reads the next record of the type-2 partition open at IX into memory at HL\nin bank B, and moves the record pointer on:\n1. RP_NEXT_SECTOR gives the record's first sector; $26B1 loads the drive's registers for it.\n2. Bank B is paged in at $C000 (SWAP_BANK), and $27A4 asks the drive for twice the record's\nsector count (byte $0B) of 256-byte reads at once.\n3. $25B9 takes each 256 bytes from port $CEEF; $27B0 waits for the next.\n4. Bank 7 back.\nEntry: IX = the open partition, HL = the memory, B = its bank.\nExit: carry set; carry clear and A = the error. BC kept.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"C:DE = the record's first sector"},
        "12554": {"comment":"The drive's registers set for it"},
        "12558": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "12559": {"comment":"E = the sectors to a record"},
        "12562": {"comment":"Bank B in"},
        "12566": {"comment":"Twice as many 256-byte reads"},
        "12568": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "12569": {"comment":"The read asked for"},
        "12572": {"synopsis":"Takes 256 bytes from port $CEEF to HL, then waits for the next 256 until the count in E runs\nout.","comment":"256 bytes in"},
        "12575": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "12576": {"comment":"All read?"},
        "12579": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "12580": {"comment":"Waits for the next 256"},
        "12583": {"comment":"And reads them"},
        "12585": {"synopsis":"Bank 7 back, BC back, carry set.","comment":"Bank 7 back"},
        "12590": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "12591": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "12593": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00DF) Writes memory at HL in bank B as the next record of the type-2 partition\nopen at IX, a sector at a time ($2604, 512 bytes each), and moves the record pointer on.\nEntry: IX = the open partition, HL = the memory, B = its bank.\nExit: carry set; carry clear and A = the error. HL past the record.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"C:DE = the record's first sector"},
        "12597": {"comment":"A = the sectors to a record"},
        "12600": {"synopsis":"Writes one sector C:DE from HL ($2604), then the next sector, until the count on the stack\nruns out.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "12602": {"comment":"Sector C:DE written from HL"},
        "12605": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "12608": {"comment":"The next sector"},
        "12609": {"comment":"Its low word wrapped round?"},
        "12613": {"comment":"Yes: C one up too"},
        "12614": {"synopsis":"One sector fewer to write; carry set when all are done.","comment":"The count"},
        "12615": {"comment":"All written?"},
        "12618": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "12620": {"synopsis":"A write failed: the count dropped, the error in A.","comment":"The count dropped"},
        "12622": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00E5) Exchanges the next record of the type-2 partition open at IX with the\nmemory at HL in bank B, a sector at a time: each sector is read into $ED11 (bank 7, $2561),\nthe memory written in its place ($2604), and the sector read copied over the memory; then\nthe record pointer moves on.\nEntry: IX = the open partition, HL = the memory, B = its bank.\nExit: carry set; carry clear and A = the error. HL past the record.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"C:DE = the record's first sector"},
        "12626": {"comment":"A = the sectors to a record"},
        "12629": {"synopsis":"One sector of the exchange: read into $ED11, the memory at HL written to it, then the 512\nbytes read copied to HL and HL past them.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "12633": {"comment":"Bank 7's sector buffer"},
        "12636": {"comment":"... in bank 7"},
        "12638": {"comment":"Sector C:DE read into it"},
        "12644": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "12648": {"comment":"The memory written as sector C:DE"},
        "12653": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "12657": {"comment":"From the buffer"},
        "12660": {"comment":"512 bytes"},
        "12663": {"comment":"... to the memory"},
        "12666": {"comment":"HL past them"},
        "12669": {"comment":"The next sector"},
        "12670": {"comment":"Its low word wrapped round?"},
        "12674": {"comment":"Yes: C one up too"},
        "12675": {"synopsis":"One sector fewer to exchange; carry set when all are done.","comment":"The count"},
        "12676": {"comment":"All done?"},
        "12679": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "12681": {"synopsis":"A read or a write failed: the count dropped, the error in A.","comment":"The count dropped"},
        "12683": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00D9) Opens a type-2 partition for BC records of A sectors each: the smallest\ntype-2 partition not already open that holds them is looked for ($2D71) on unit 0, then on\nunit 1, and opened in a slot of $E897 ($2C9D); the slot's byte $0B gets A, bytes $0E-$0F BC,\nand the record pointer (bytes $0C-$0D) 0.\nEntry: A = the sectors to a record (1-$20), BC = the number of records.\nExit: carry set and IX = the open partition; carry clear and A = $15 for a bad A, $40 for\nno type-2 partition big enough, or another error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"The sectors to a record kept"},
        "12684": {"comment":"The number of records kept"},
        "12685": {"comment":"L:DE = the size needed"},
        "12688": {"comment":"Type 2"},
        "12692": {"comment":"Unit 0"},
        "12694": {"comment":"A big enough partition there?"},
        "12699": {"comment":"Unit 0"},
        "12701": {"comment":"Yes: open it"},
        "12703": {"comment":"Unit 1"},
        "12704": {"comment":"A big enough partition there?"},
        "12707": {"comment":"Error $40"},
        "12709": {"comment":"None on either"},
        "12711": {"comment":"Unit 1"},
        "12713": {"synopsis":"Opens partition BC of unit A in a slot ($2C9D), then sets it up (RP_SET_SIZE).","comment":"Open partition BC of unit A"},
        "12716": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "12718": {"synopsis":"Sets up the open partition at IX for records: byte $0B = the sectors to a record, bytes\n$0E-$0F = the number of records (both from the stack), and the record pointer (bytes\n$0C-$0D) = 0.\nExit: carry set.","comment":"The number of records"},
        "12725": {"comment":"The sectors to a record"},
        "12729": {"comment":"The record pointer = 0"},
        "12737": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "12739": {"synopsis":"Drops three words from the stack and returns, the error in A: also the way out of\nRP_LAST_SECTOR (its return address the first word) for a bad record size.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "12740": {"synopsis":"Drops two words from the stack and returns, the error in A.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "12743": {"synopsis":"Works out the last sector of BC + 1 records of A sectors: L:DE = A x BC + A - 1, the size a\ntype-2 partition needs for records 0 to BC. A must be 1 to $20: else the routine drops its\nreturn address and the two words the caller pushed and returns from the caller with A = $15\n(RP_POP3).\nEntry: A = the sectors to a record, BC = the number of records.\nExit: L:DE = the last sector; H = 0.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = 0 for the sum"},
        "12746": {"comment":"E = A - 1"},
        "12748": {"comment":"D = A for the count"},
        "12749": {"comment":"1 to $20 sectors?"},
        "12752": {"comment":"Error $15"},
        "12754": {"comment":"No: out of the caller too"},
        "12756": {"comment":"A = 0 for the high byte"},
        "12757": {"synopsis":"Adds BC into A:HL D times.","comment":"BC once more"},
        "12760": {"comment":"A times"},
        "12763": {"comment":"Plus A - 1"},
        "12766": {"comment":"DE = the low word"},
        "12767": {"comment":"L = the high byte"},
        "12769": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00EE) Sets the type-2 partition open at IX to hold BC records of A sectors each,\nwhen they fit in it: L:DE from RP_LAST_SECTOR is compared with the partition's last sector\n(bytes $07-$09); when not above it, RP_SET_SIZE takes A and BC, and the record pointer goes\nback to 0.\nEntry: IX = the open partition, A = the sectors to a record (1-$20), BC = the number of\nrecords.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = $3D for another type, $15 for records that\ndo not fit or a bad A.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"D = the sectors to a record"},
        "12770": {"comment":"Type 2?"},
        "12774": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "12776": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "12777": {"comment":"L:DE = the last sector needed"},
        "12780": {"comment":"The partition's last sector, high"},
        "12783": {"comment":"Below the one needed?"},
        "12786": {"comment":"Above: it fits"},
        "12788": {"comment":"The middle byte"},
        "12791": {"comment":"Below?"},
        "12794": {"comment":"Above: it fits"},
        "12796": {"comment":"The low byte"},
        "12799": {"comment":"Not below: it fits"},
        "12802": {"synopsis":"The records do not fit: the two words dropped, error $15.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "12804": {"comment":"Error $15"},
        "12806": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "12808": {"synopsis":"Finds drive letter L's word in the drive table at $E2A0 (16 words, A to P, each the address\nof the drive's parameter block or 0), noting the letter at $EF91.\nEntry: L = the letter (a capital).\nExit: carry set, HL = the word's address, DE = the word, Z when the letter has no drive;\ncarry clear and A = $15 for a letter outside A-P.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"The letter kept"},
        "12812": {"comment":"Below A?"},
        "12816": {"comment":"Above P?"},
        "12820": {"comment":"HL = its number"},
        "12823": {"comment":"Two bytes each"},
        "12824": {"comment":"The table's high bytes"},
        "12828": {"comment":"D = the word's high byte"},
        "12829": {"comment":"HL at its low byte"},
        "12830": {"comment":"E = the low byte"},
        "12831": {"comment":"Z when no drive"},
        "12833": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "12835": {"synopsis":"The letter is outside A-P: error $15.","comment":"Carry clear"},
        "12836": {"comment":"Error $15"},
        "12839": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00F1) Gives drive letter L to a partition or a device:\n1. A = 2, 3 or 4: a device (LMAP_DEVICE).\n2. A = 0 or 1: partition BC of unit A, which must be of type 3. One of the two drive blocks\n   of\n$130 bytes at $E8E3 must be free (first word 0; error $3F); the letter must be in A-P\n(error $15) and unused (error $3E).\n3. The entry is read into $EF11 (type other than 3: error $38) and the drive block filled:\n+$00-$1B the entry's bytes $20-$3B (the drive's parameters), +$1C the letter, +$1D $A0\nwith the unit in bit 4, +$1E-$27 zero, +$28 the address of the block's buffer (+$30), +$2A\n$27DF, +$2C $27E1 and +$2E $27F9 (the routines the file system calls for the drive).\n4. The partition is opened in a slot of $E897 ($2C9D; on failure the block is freed again),\nthe slot's address goes to the block's +$17-$18 and the block's address into the drive\ntable.\n5. With bit 6 of $5B66 set the letter is also kept on the disk: taken from every other\nrecord (LETTER_FORGET) and written as byte $1C of the entry's own bytes (PART_BYTE_SET).\nEntry: A = the unit or device, BC = the entry, L = the letter.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"A device?"},
        "12844": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "12848": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "12849": {"comment":"The first drive block"},
        "12852": {"comment":"Two of them"},
        "12854": {"comment":"$130 bytes each"},
        "12857": {"synopsis":"Looks at each drive block at $E8E3 for one whose first word is 0 (free); error $3F when both\nare in use.","comment":"A free block?"},
        "12861": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "12863": {"comment":"The next block"},
        "12866": {"comment":"Error $3F"},
        "12868": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "12869": {"synopsis":"Leaves with the error in A: three words dropped, IX back.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "12872": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "12875": {"synopsis":"A free drive block: its address on the stack, the letter's word in the drive table found;\nthe entry read and checked to be of type 3, a partition with a file system.","comment":"The block kept, HL = the letter"},
        "12876": {"comment":"Its word in the drive table"},
        "12879": {"comment":"Outside A-P?"},
        "12881": {"comment":"Error $3E"},
        "12883": {"comment":"Carry clear for the error"},
        "12884": {"comment":"Already in use?"},
        "12886": {"comment":"DE = the block"},
        "12887": {"comment":"BC = the entry"},
        "12888": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "12889": {"comment":"The table word's address kept"},
        "12892": {"comment":"The entry buffer"},
        "12895": {"comment":"Entry BC of unit A read"},
        "12900": {"comment":"Its type"},
        "12903": {"comment":"Type 3?"},
        "12907": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "12908": {"comment":"Error $38"},
        "12912": {"synopsis":"A type-3 partition: the drive block filled from the entry, then the partition opened.","comment":"The entry's bytes $20-$3B"},
        "12915": {"comment":"DE = the block"},
        "12920": {"comment":"28 bytes"},
        "12923": {"comment":"... to the block's +$00-$1B"},
        "12925": {"comment":"HL = the block's +$1C"},
        "12926": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "12929": {"comment":"... to +$1C"},
        "12931": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "12933": {"comment":"... into bit 4"},
        "12937": {"comment":"With $A0 as +$1D"},
        "12939": {"comment":"... to +$1D"},
        "12941": {"comment":"+$1E-$27 cleared"},
        "12943": {"synopsis":"Clears B bytes at HL.","comment":"A zero"},
        "12946": {"comment":"For all ten"},
        "12948": {"comment":"HL = the block's +$28"},
        "12954": {"comment":"+$28: the buffer at +$30"},
        "12958": {"comment":"+$2A: $27DF"},
        "12964": {"comment":"+$2C: $27E1"},
        "12970": {"comment":"+$2E: $27F9"},
        "12975": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "12976": {"comment":"The entry"},
        "12979": {"comment":"Partition BC of unit A opened"},
        "12982": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "12986": {"comment":"HL = the block"},
        "12988": {"comment":"The block's +$17"},
        "12992": {"comment":"DE = the open partition"},
        "12995": {"comment":"... to +$17-$18"},
        "12998": {"comment":"The block's address"},
        "12999": {"comment":"HL = the table word"},
        "13000": {"comment":"... into the drive table"},
        "13003": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "13005": {"comment":"Kept on the disk too?"},
        "13010": {"comment":"No: carry, done"},
        "13012": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "13013": {"comment":"The entry kept"},
        "13014": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "13018": {"comment":"... taken from the other records"},
        "13021": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "13024": {"comment":"... as the value"},
        "13025": {"comment":"Byte $1C of the entry's own bytes"},
        "13029": {"comment":"Written to the disk"},
        "13033": {"synopsis":"The partition did not open: the drive block's first word cleared (free again), the error in\nA, IX back.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "13035": {"comment":"HL = the block"},
        "13036": {"comment":"Its first word cleared: free"},
        "13042": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "13045": {"synopsis":"Gives drive letter L to device A: 2 the first floppy unit, 3 the second, 4 the RAM disk:\n1. The device's parameter block comes from DEVICE_TABLE; for a floppy unit the disk\ncontroller must answer (DOS_JUMPS $0157), else error $41; A above 4 is error $41 too.\n2. A block already in the drive table is error $3B; the letter must be in A-P (error $15)\n   and\nunused (error $3E).\n3. The block's address goes into the drive table and the letter to its +$1C; the first\nfloppy unit's letter is noted at $E3EA when none is.\n4. With bit 6 of $5B66 set the letter is also kept on the disk: taken from every other\n   record\n(LETTER_FORGET) and written as byte $0D, $0E or $0F (one per device) of entry 0's own bytes\non unit 0 (PART_BYTE_SET).\nEntry: A = the device (2-4), L = the letter.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The letter kept"},
        "13046": {"comment":"E = the device less 2"},
        "13051": {"comment":"The RAM disk?"},
        "13055": {"comment":"Above it?"},
        "13057": {"comment":"A disk controller?"},
        "13060": {"comment":"No: error $41"},
        "13062": {"synopsis":"The device is there: its parameter block from DEVICE_TABLE (6 bytes an entry), then the\ndrive\ntable searched for it.","comment":"HL = the device's number"},
        "13064": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13065": {"comment":"Times 6"},
        "13068": {"comment":"DEVICE_TABLE"},
        "13072": {"comment":"BC = the parameter block"},
        "13075": {"comment":"The drive table"},
        "13078": {"comment":"16 words"},
        "13080": {"synopsis":"Compares one word of the drive table with BC: the block given a letter already is error $3B.","comment":"The word's low byte"},
        "13082": {"comment":"The block's?"},
        "13085": {"comment":"The high byte"},
        "13087": {"comment":"Error $3B"},
        "13089": {"comment":"The same: in use already"},
        "13091": {"synopsis":"The next word of the drive table.","comment":"The next word"},
        "13092": {"comment":"All 16?"},
        "13095": {"comment":"DE = the device's number"},
        "13096": {"comment":"HL = the letter"},
        "13098": {"comment":"Its word in the drive table"},
        "13102": {"comment":"Outside A-P?"},
        "13103": {"comment":"Error $3E"},
        "13105": {"comment":"Carry clear for the error"},
        "13106": {"comment":"Already in use?"},
        "13107": {"comment":"The block into the drive table"},
        "13110": {"comment":"The block's +$1C"},
        "13114": {"comment":"A letter noted for the first floppy?"},
        "13120": {"comment":"No: this the first floppy unit?"},
        "13124": {"comment":"Yes: its letter noted"},
        "13130": {"synopsis":"The letter goes to the block's +$1C; with bit 6 of $5B66 set it is also written on the disk\n(entry 0's own byte $0D plus the device's number).","comment":"The letter"},
        "13133": {"comment":"... to the block's +$1C"},
        "13134": {"comment":"Kept on the disk too?"},
        "13139": {"comment":"No: carry, done"},
        "13141": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "13142": {"comment":"The device's number kept"},
        "13143": {"comment":"L = the letter"},
        "13144": {"comment":"... taken from the other records"},
        "13149": {"comment":"Entry 0's own byte $0D"},
        "13152": {"comment":"... plus the device's number"},
        "13153": {"comment":"H = the letter"},
        "13154": {"comment":"Unit 0"},
        "13155": {"comment":"Entry 0"},
        "13157": {"comment":"Written to the disk"},
        "13161": {"synopsis":"The device has a letter already: error $3B (already in A), two words dropped.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "13164": {"synopsis":"No such device, or no disk controller: error $41.","comment":"Error $41"},
        "13166": {"comment":"Dropped"},
        "13168": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00F4) Takes drive letter L away from its partition or device:\n1. The letter's word in the drive table must be in A-P (error $15); a letter with no drive\ngoes on to step 4.\n2. The drive is logged out (DRIVE_LOG_OUT; error $24 when it has open files) and its word in\nthe drive table cleared. A drive block of a partition (its +$1B with bits 2-3 clear) is\nfreed by clearing its first word.\n3. The letter noted at $E3EA is cleared if it is this one, and so is the block's +$1C; for a\npartition (+$2A = $27DF) its slot in $E897 is closed ($2CE4).\n4. With bit 6 of $5B66 set the letter is also taken from the records on the disk\n(LETTER_FORGET).\nEntry: L = the letter.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The letter's drive"},
        "13171": {"comment":"Outside A-P?"},
        "13172": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "13174": {"comment":"No drive: only the disk's records"},
        "13176": {"comment":"IX = the drive's block"},
        "13179": {"comment":"Logged out"},
        "13182": {"comment":"Open files?"},
        "13184": {"comment":"The drive table's word cleared"},
        "13188": {"comment":"HL = the block"},
        "13189": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "13192": {"comment":"A floppy unit or the RAM disk?"},
        "13194": {"comment":"No: the block's first word cleared"},
        "13199": {"synopsis":"Clears the letter noted at $E3EA when it is this drive's, and the block's letter (+$1C).","comment":"The letter noted"},
        "13202": {"comment":"This drive's?"},
        "13205": {"comment":"No"},
        "13207": {"comment":"Yes: cleared"},
        "13211": {"synopsis":"The block's letter cleared; for a partition's drive (+$2A = $27DF) its slot in $E897 is\nclosed.","comment":"No letter"},
        "13215": {"comment":"The block's +$2A routine"},
        "13221": {"comment":"A partition's?"},
        "13227": {"comment":"No"},
        "13229": {"comment":"The open partition"},
        "13238": {"comment":"Closed"},
        "13241": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "13243": {"synopsis":"With bit 6 of $5B66 set, the letter is taken from the records on the disk (LETTER_FORGET).","comment":"Kept on the disk too?"},
        "13248": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "13249": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "13251": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "13255": {"comment":"... taken from the records"},
        "13258": {"synopsis":"IX back.","comment":"IX back"},
        "13261": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00F7) Tells what drive letter L stands for, writing its name into 18 bytes at\nBC (filled with spaces first):\n1. A letter with no drive: carry set and Z.\n2. A partition's drive (block +$2A = $27DF): the partition's entry is read ($2B72) and the\nname is the unit (\"0\" or \"1\"), \">\" and the entry's 16-byte name; A = the unit, BC = the\nentry.\n3. A device: its text from DEVICE_TABLE (for example \"2>Floppy device 0\"); A = 2, 3 or 4,\nthe device (LDESC_DEVICE).\nEntry: L = the letter, BC = the 18 bytes.\nExit: carry set, NZ and A, BC as above; carry clear and A = the error ($15 for a letter\noutside A-P).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The buffer kept"},
        "13262": {"comment":"A space"},
        "13264": {"comment":"18 of them"},
        "13266": {"synopsis":"Fills E bytes at BC with A.","comment":"A space"},
        "13269": {"comment":"For all 18"},
        "13271": {"comment":"The letter's drive"},
        "13274": {"comment":"DE = its word's address"},
        "13275": {"comment":"BC = the buffer"},
        "13276": {"comment":"Outside A-P?"},
        "13277": {"comment":"No drive: carry and Z"},
        "13278": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "13280": {"comment":"The buffer kept"},
        "13281": {"comment":"IX = the drive's block"},
        "13284": {"comment":"Its +$2A routine"},
        "13290": {"comment":"A partition's?"},
        "13296": {"comment":"No: a device"},
        "13298": {"comment":"The open partition"},
        "13307": {"comment":"Its unit"},
        "13310": {"comment":"... from bit 4 of +$10"},
        "13316": {"comment":"BC = its entry"},
        "13322": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13323": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "13324": {"comment":"The entry buffer"},
        "13327": {"comment":"Entry BC of unit A read"},
        "13330": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "13334": {"comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "13335": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "13337": {"comment":"The unit as a digit"},
        "13340": {"comment":"Then \">\""},
        "13345": {"comment":"The entry's name"},
        "13348": {"comment":"16 bytes"},
        "13353": {"comment":"Carry and NZ"},
        "13356": {"comment":"B = the unit"},
        "13357": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "13358": {"comment":"BC = the entry"},
        "13359": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "13362": {"synopsis":"The entry could not be read: three words dropped, the error in A, IX back.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "13364": {"synopsis":"Two words dropped, IX back.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "13365": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "13368": {"synopsis":"A device's drive: its block's address looked for in the three entries of DEVICE_TABLE; the\nentry's text (its length at +4) copied to the buffer, A = the device (+5). Error $41 for a\nblock not in the table.","comment":"DE = the block"},
        "13371": {"comment":"DEVICE_TABLE"},
        "13375": {"comment":"Three devices"},
        "13377": {"synopsis":"Compares one entry's block address with DE.","comment":"The entry's block"},
        "13383": {"comment":"This one?"},
        "13386": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "13388": {"comment":"Six bytes an entry"},
        "13393": {"comment":"All three?"},
        "13396": {"comment":"Error $41"},
        "13400": {"synopsis":"Copies the entry's text to the buffer; A = the device, carry set and NZ.","comment":"HL = the text"},
        "13406": {"comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "13407": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "13412": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "13414": {"comment":"Carry and NZ"},
        "13417": {"comment":"A = the device"},
        "13420": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "13423": {"synopsis":"The three devices a drive letter can be given to, 6 bytes each: the address of the device's\nparameter block, the address of its text, the text's length and the device's number: $E2C0\n\"2>Floppy device 0\" (2), $E32D \"3>Floppy device 1\" (3), $E39A \"4>RAMdisk\" (4)."},
        "13441": {"synopsis":"The devices' texts, without an end marker (DEVICE_TABLE gives their lengths): 17, 17 and 9\nbytes."},
        "13484": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00FA) Takes drive letter L out of the records of drive letters kept on the\ndisk:\n1. Entry 0 of unit 0 is read: for A, B or M its flag among the entry's own bytes $0A-$0C\n($EF3B-$EF3D) is set to 1, and any of bytes $0D-$0F ($EF3E-$EF40, the devices' letters)\nholding it is cleared; the entry is written back. When it cannot be read, step 2 follows\nat once.\n2. Every entry of units 0 and 1 is read in turn: a type-3 entry whose byte $1C ($EF4D, the\npartition's letter) is L gets 0 there and is written back. A unit ends at error $38 (no\nmore entries) or $16 (no such unit).\nEntry: L = the letter.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The letter kept"},
        "13485": {"comment":"Unit 0"},
        "13486": {"comment":"Entry 0"},
        "13488": {"comment":"The entry buffer"},
        "13491": {"comment":"Entry 0 of unit 0 read"},
        "13494": {"comment":"E = the letter"},
        "13495": {"comment":"Failed: only the partitions"},
        "13497": {"comment":"The flag for A"},
        "13500": {"comment":"The letter A?"},
        "13503": {"comment":"No"},
        "13505": {"comment":"Yes: flag set"},
        "13507": {"synopsis":"The flag for B ($EF3C) set when the letter is B.","comment":"The flag for B"},
        "13508": {"comment":"The letter B?"},
        "13510": {"comment":"No"},
        "13512": {"comment":"Yes: flag set"},
        "13514": {"synopsis":"The flag for M ($EF3D) set when the letter is M.","comment":"The flag for M"},
        "13515": {"comment":"The letter M?"},
        "13517": {"comment":"No"},
        "13519": {"comment":"Yes: flag set"},
        "13521": {"synopsis":"The devices' letters ($EF3E-$EF40): any that is L is cleared.","comment":"The devices' letters"},
        "13524": {"comment":"Three of them"},
        "13526": {"synopsis":"One device's letter: cleared when it is L.","comment":"This one?"},
        "13528": {"comment":"No"},
        "13530": {"comment":"Yes: cleared"},
        "13532": {"synopsis":"The next device's letter.","comment":"The next"},
        "13533": {"comment":"All three?"},
        "13535": {"comment":"Unit 0"},
        "13536": {"comment":"Entry 0"},
        "13538": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "13539": {"comment":"The entry"},
        "13542": {"comment":"... written back"},
        "13545": {"comment":"The letter back"},
        "13546": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "13547": {"synopsis":"Starts on the partitions of unit 0.","comment":"Unit 0"},
        "13548": {"synopsis":"Starts on unit A's partition table at entry 0.","comment":"From entry 0"},
        "13551": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "13552": {"synopsis":"Reads entry BC of the unit on the stack; a type-3 entry holding the letter in its byte $1C\nloses it.","comment":"A = the unit"},
        "13554": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "13555": {"comment":"The entry buffer"},
        "13558": {"comment":"Entry BC read"},
        "13561": {"comment":"The letter back"},
        "13562": {"comment":"Failed: the end of the table?"},
        "13564": {"comment":"Its type"},
        "13567": {"comment":"Type 3?"},
        "13569": {"comment":"No"},
        "13571": {"comment":"Its letter"},
        "13574": {"comment":"This one?"},
        "13575": {"comment":"No"},
        "13577": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "13581": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "13583": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "13584": {"comment":"The entry"},
        "13587": {"comment":"... written back"},
        "13590": {"comment":"The letter back"},
        "13591": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "13593": {"synopsis":"The next entry, until the number wraps round.","comment":"The next entry"},
        "13594": {"comment":"Wrapped round?"},
        "13596": {"comment":"No: read it"},
        "13598": {"synopsis":"The next unit, until both are done: carry set.","comment":"The unit"},
        "13599": {"comment":"The next one"},
        "13600": {"comment":"Both done?"},
        "13602": {"comment":"No"},
        "13604": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "13606": {"synopsis":"A read or a write failed: error $38 (past the last entry) or $16 (no unit) ends the unit;\nany other error is returned.","comment":"Past the last entry?"},
        "13608": {"comment":"Yes: the next unit"},
        "13610": {"comment":"No such unit?"},
        "13612": {"comment":"Yes: the next unit"},
        "13614": {"comment":"The unit dropped"},
        "13615": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "13617": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $00FD) Loads and runs a snapshot file from a partition's drive, reading the\npartition straight from the hard disk. The name's last character tells the kind: one with\nbit 6 set (as in \"A\") takes the first layout, one without (as in \"0\") the second:\n1. The file is opened as number 0 for reading (OPEN_BY_NAME) and its first 30 bytes read to\n$5000; A:DE = the bytes left plus 1 (FILE_LEN_GET less FILE_POS_GET), A also to $4015.\n2. FILE_RUN_LIST turns the rest of the file into a list of disk runs at $506B; the file is\nclosed (CLOSE_FILE). From here interrupts are off, SP = $5067, and the bytes come one at a\ntime from the disk (SNAP_BYTE, the list at IX): the bytes before the file pointer in the\nfirst sector are skipped ($27CB).\n3. First layout: the border from $501A (port $FE), $5013 kept to its bit 2; with A = 0 (a\n   file\nof 48K) the RAM from $4003 (SNAP_48K_LOAD); otherwise $4003-$FFFF with bank 0 at $C000,\nthen 2 bytes for the stub's JP address, the byte for port $7FFD, the RAM at $C000 copied to\nthe bank it names, one byte skipped and the other banks in order (not 2, 5 or that bank).\n4. Second layout: SNAP_Z80.\n5. SNAP_START sets the registers and runs the program.\nEntry: HL = the file's name, ended by $FF.\nExit: only when the file cannot be opened, read or listed: carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: everything.","comment":"DE at the name"},
        "13619": {"synopsis":"Finds the $FF at the end of the name; the last character before it goes to $401D.","comment":"A character"},
        "13621": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "13625": {"comment":"Back to the last character"},
        "13627": {"comment":"A = the last character"},
        "13628": {"comment":"... to $401D: the layout"},
        "13631": {"comment":"File 0, read access"},
        "13634": {"comment":"D = 0"},
        "13635": {"comment":"E = 1"},
        "13637": {"comment":"Opened"},
        "13640": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "13641": {"comment":"The 30 bytes to $5000"},
        "13644": {"comment":"30 bytes"},
        "13647": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "13648": {"comment":"C = 7"},
        "13650": {"comment":"Read"},
        "13653": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "13654": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "13656": {"comment":"E:HL = the file pointer"},
        "13659": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13661": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "13663": {"comment":"E:HL = the file's length"},
        "13666": {"comment":"BC = the pointer's low word"},
        "13668": {"comment":"HL = the low word left"},
        "13670": {"comment":"C = the pointer's high byte"},
        "13671": {"comment":"A = the high byte left"},
        "13673": {"comment":"Plus 1"},
        "13678": {"comment":"DE = the low word"},
        "13679": {"comment":"A to $4015"},
        "13682": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13683": {"comment":"BC = file 0's record"},
        "13686": {"comment":"A:DE = the bytes to read"},
        "13687": {"comment":"The list at $506B"},
        "13690": {"comment":"The disk runs of the rest"},
        "13693": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "13694": {"comment":"The list's end noted"},
        "13697": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "13699": {"comment":"Closed"},
        "13702": {"comment":"Interrupts off from here"},
        "13703": {"comment":"The stack below the list"},
        "13706": {"comment":"IX = the list's first run"},
        "13710": {"comment":"HL = the bytes to skip"},
        "13716": {"comment":"The first run asked for"},
        "13719": {"comment":"The bytes before the file pointer"},
        "13722": {"comment":"The disk's registers aside"},
        "13723": {"comment":"The first layout?"},
        "13728": {"comment":"No: the second"},
        "13731": {"comment":"The border"},
        "13736": {"comment":"Bit 2 of $5013 kept"},
        "13744": {"comment":"A file of 48K?"},
        "13748": {"comment":"The first layout's map: $0010"},
        "13751": {"comment":"The disk's registers back"},
        "13752": {"comment":"Not packed"},
        "13755": {"comment":"From $4003"},
        "13757": {"comment":"48K: load it"},
        "13760": {"comment":"$4003-$47FF, bank 0 in"},
        "13763": {"comment":"The stack under the moved list"},
        "13766": {"comment":"The rest to $FFFF"},
        "13769": {"comment":"The stub's JP address, low"},
        "13773": {"comment":"... high"},
        "13777": {"comment":"... into the stub"},
        "13780": {"comment":"The JP"},
        "13785": {"comment":"The byte for port $7FFD"},
        "13788": {"comment":"... into the stub"},
        "13791": {"comment":"The bank it pages in"},
        "13793": {"comment":"Bank 0?"},
        "13795": {"comment":"HL aside"},
        "13796": {"comment":"From $C000"},
        "13799": {"comment":"E = the bank"},
        "13800": {"synopsis":"Copies bank 0's $C000-$FFFF to bank E a byte at a time, since the RAM loaded at $C000\nbelongs to the bank the snapshot pages in.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "13804": {"comment":"Its byte"},
        "13805": {"comment":"Bank E"},
        "13809": {"comment":"... gets it"},
        "13811": {"comment":"To $FFFF"},
        "13815": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "13816": {"synopsis":"Skips one byte of the file, then loads the other banks at $C000 in order from bank 0, all\nbut\nbanks 2 and 5 and the one paged in.","comment":"One byte skipped"},
        "13819": {"comment":"From bank 0"},
        "13820": {"synopsis":"Bank A: skipped when it is 2, 5 or the bank paged in, otherwise paged in at $C000 and\nloaded.","comment":"Bank 2?"},
        "13824": {"comment":"Bank 5?"},
        "13828": {"comment":"L = the byte for port $7FFD"},
        "13831": {"comment":"H = this bank"},
        "13832": {"comment":"The bank it pages in?"},
        "13836": {"comment":"A = this bank"},
        "13839": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "13842": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13843": {"comment":"From $C000"},
        "13846": {"comment":"Loaded to $FFFF"},
        "13849": {"comment":"The bank back"},
        "13850": {"synopsis":"The next bank, up to 7, then SNAP_START.","comment":"The next bank"},
        "13851": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "13855": {"comment":"Then run it"},
        "13857": {"synopsis":"The second layout: the header byte at $500C ($FF taken as 1) gives the border (bits 1-3, to\nport $FE), bit 7 of the byte at $500B (bit 0) and whether the RAM is packed (bit 5, to IYL);\nthe table at SNAP_Z80_MAP is put aside in the other HL. A word at $5006 other than 0 starts\nthe RAM at once, from $4000 (SNAP_48K_LOAD); 0 means a further header (SNAP_Z80_EXT).","comment":"The flags byte"},
        "13861": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "13865": {"comment":"Taken as 1"},
        "13868": {"synopsis":"The flags byte in A: its bit 0 to the carry and bit 7 of $500B, its bits 1-3 to the border,\nits bit 5 to IYL.","comment":"Bit 0 to the carry"},
        "13869": {"comment":"The border"},
        "13871": {"comment":"The byte at $500B"},
        "13873": {"comment":"Bit 7 cleared"},
        "13875": {"comment":"... unless bit 0 was set"},
        "13879": {"synopsis":"Stores the byte at $500B, then takes the flags byte's bit 5 (packed RAM) to IYL.","comment":"Back"},
        "13880": {"comment":"The flags byte again"},
        "13881": {"comment":"Packed?"},
        "13884": {"comment":"IYL: 0 for not"},
        "13886": {"comment":"The second layout's map"},
        "13889": {"comment":"Put aside"},
        "13890": {"comment":"The word at $5006"},
        "13893": {"comment":"0?"},
        "13895": {"comment":"Yes: a further header"},
        "13898": {"comment":"From $4000"},
        "13900": {"synopsis":"Loads 48K of RAM from $4000 + L: $4000-$47FF with bank 0 paged in (SNAP_BANK0_LOW, which\nalso\nmoves the run list and builds the registers block), then the rest to $FFFF.","comment":"Up to $47FF; bank 0 in"},
        "13903": {"comment":"The stack under the moved list"},
        "13906": {"comment":"The rest to $FFFF"},
        "13909": {"synopsis":"Runs the program loaded:\n1. The rest of the disk sector is read away ($27D7).\n2. The interrupt mode from $4010 (0, 1 or 2).\n3. The registers block at $4000 popped: HL', DE', BC', AF', HL, DE, IY, IX, then $4010-$4011\n   (R\nfrom $4011 less 9, its bit 7 kept) and $4012-$4013 (F and I).\n4. SP from $4016, BC = $1FFD, A = $4015, and on to the stub at $4018 (port $1FFD = A, port\n$7FFD = $401D, BC and A from the stub, EI unless cleared, then RET or JP).","comment":"The rest of the sector read away"},
        "13912": {"comment":"IM 0"},
        "13914": {"comment":"... unless $4010 says 1 or 2"},
        "13921": {"comment":"IM 1"},
        "13924": {"comment":"1?"},
        "13926": {"comment":"IM 2"},
        "13928": {"synopsis":"Pops the registers block at $4000 and goes to the stub at $4018.","comment":"The registers block"},
        "13931": {"comment":"HL', DE', BC'"},
        "13935": {"comment":"AF'"},
        "13937": {"comment":"HL, DE, IY, IX"},
        "13943": {"comment":"B = R, C = the mode"},
        "13944": {"comment":"R less 9"},
        "13947": {"comment":"... with its own bit 7"},
        "13951": {"comment":"R set"},
        "13953": {"comment":"F, and A = I"},
        "13954": {"comment":"I set"},
        "13956": {"comment":"The program's SP"},
        "13960": {"comment":"For the stub's OUT"},
        "13963": {"comment":"Port $1FFD's byte"},
        "13966": {"comment":"The stub"},
        "13969": {"synopsis":"The further header of the second layout:\n1. Its length (one byte; a second byte other than 0 restarts the machine, RST $00); the word\nfor $5006 (the program's address); H = the next byte (the machine kind); the next to $5069\n(the byte for port $7FFD); two skipped; the next (a sound chip register number) kept.\n2. The sixteen sound chip registers written through ports $FFFD and $BFFD, then the register\nkept selected.\n3. A length of $17 (23): H one up when it is 3 or more, and 4 as the byte for port $1FFD.\nOtherwise the remaining bytes are read away, the last of them (length 55 or more) being\nthe byte for port $1FFD, 4 for a shorter header; it goes to $506A.\n4. H below 4: three blocks for a 48K machine (SNAP_48_BLOCK); 4 and above: eight for a 128K\none (SNAP_128).","comment":"Its length, low"},
        "13973": {"comment":"High"},
        "13976": {"comment":"Above 255?"},
        "13980": {"comment":"The program's address, low"},
        "13986": {"comment":"... high"},
        "13992": {"comment":"H = the machine kind"},
        "13996": {"comment":"The byte for port $7FFD"},
        "14002": {"comment":"Skipped"},
        "14005": {"comment":"Skipped"},
        "14008": {"comment":"A sound chip register number"},
        "14011": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14012": {"comment":"The other registers"},
        "14013": {"comment":"Register 0 on, 16 of them"},
        "14016": {"synopsis":"Writes one sound chip register: D (in the other set) to port $FFFD, the byte read to port\n$BFFD; D one up, E one down until 16 are done.","comment":"The register's value"},
        "14020": {"comment":"The registers' set"},
        "14021": {"comment":"Port $FFFD"},
        "14024": {"comment":"The register selected"},
        "14026": {"comment":"Port $BFFD"},
        "14028": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "14030": {"comment":"The next register"},
        "14031": {"comment":"All 16?"},
        "14034": {"comment":"Port $FFFD"},
        "14036": {"comment":"The number kept"},
        "14037": {"comment":"... selected again"},
        "14039": {"comment":"Back"},
        "14040": {"comment":"The header's length"},
        "14041": {"comment":"23?"},
        "14043": {"comment":"No"},
        "14045": {"comment":"The machine kind"},
        "14046": {"comment":"3 or more?"},
        "14050": {"comment":"Yes: one up"},
        "14051": {"comment":"Port $1FFD's byte 4"},
        "14053": {"synopsis":"A longer header: carry when fewer than 32 bytes remain past the first 23; all of them are\nread\naway, the last in L.","comment":"32 or more left?"},
        "14055": {"synopsis":"Reads one of the remaining header bytes into L; the carry from the length test kept.","comment":"The count and the carry kept"},
        "14056": {"comment":"A byte"},
        "14059": {"comment":"... in L"},
        "14060": {"comment":"Back"},
        "14061": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "14064": {"comment":"The last byte read"},
        "14065": {"comment":"Long enough: port $1FFD's byte"},
        "14067": {"synopsis":"Port $1FFD's byte 4.","comment":"4"},
        "14069": {"synopsis":"Stores the byte for port $1FFD at $506A, then picks the loading by the machine kind in H.","comment":"The byte for port $1FFD"},
        "14072": {"comment":"The machine kind"},
        "14073": {"comment":"A 128K machine?"},
        "14078": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "14082": {"comment":"Three blocks"},
        "14084": {"comment":"Carry clear for SNAP_BLOCK_HEAD"},
        "14085": {"synopsis":"One block of a 48K machine: its header (SNAP_BLOCK_HEAD) gives the page: 4 loads\n$8000-$BFFF, 5 $C000-$FFFF, 8 $4000-$7FFF (its first 2K by SNAP_LOW_FROM0, which also builds\nthe registers block); any other page restarts the machine.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "14086": {"comment":"A = the block's page"},
        "14089": {"comment":"Page 4: $8000"},
        "14092": {"comment":"... to $BFFF"},
        "14095": {"comment":"Page 4?"},
        "14099": {"comment":"Page 5: $C000"},
        "14101": {"comment":"... to $FFFF"},
        "14104": {"comment":"Page 5?"},
        "14108": {"comment":"Page 8?"},
        "14110": {"comment":"No: restart"},
        "14112": {"comment":"$4000-$47FF first"},
        "14115": {"comment":"The count"},
        "14116": {"comment":"The stack under the moved list"},
        "14119": {"comment":"The count again"},
        "14120": {"comment":"... the rest to $7FFF"},
        "14123": {"synopsis":"Loads the block to the end set in IYH, then the next block until three are done.","comment":"Loaded"},
        "14126": {"comment":"The count"},
        "14127": {"comment":"All three?"},
        "14130": {"comment":"Then run it"},
        "14133": {"synopsis":"A layout this loader cannot take: the machine starts again from address 0.","comment":"Restart"},
        "14134": {"synopsis":"Eight blocks of a 128K machine.","comment":"Eight blocks"},
        "14136": {"comment":"Carry clear for SNAP_BLOCK_HEAD"},
        "14137": {"synopsis":"One block of a 128K machine: its page less 3 is the bank (0-7, else a restart), paged in at\n$C000 and loaded there; bank 5 goes to $4000-$47FF first (SNAP_LOW_FROM0, building the\nregisters block), then the bytes for ports $7FFD and $1FFD from the header to the stub\n($401D, $4015), and the rest from $C800.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "14138": {"comment":"A = the block's page"},
        "14141": {"comment":"Below 3?"},
        "14145": {"comment":"Above 10?"},
        "14149": {"comment":"At $C000"},
        "14152": {"comment":"The bank paged in"},
        "14155": {"comment":"Bank 5?"},
        "14159": {"comment":"$4000-$47FF first"},
        "14162": {"comment":"The count"},
        "14163": {"comment":"The stack under the moved list"},
        "14166": {"comment":"The count again"},
        "14167": {"comment":"Port $7FFD's byte"},
        "14170": {"comment":"... to the stub"},
        "14173": {"comment":"Port $1FFD's byte"},
        "14176": {"comment":"... to the stub"},
        "14179": {"comment":"The rest from $C800"},
        "14181": {"synopsis":"Loads the block to $FFFF, then the next block until eight are done.","comment":"To $FFFF"},
        "14184": {"comment":"Loaded"},
        "14187": {"comment":"The count"},
        "14188": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "14191": {"comment":"Then run it"},
        "14194": {"synopsis":"Bank 0 paged in, then SNAP_LOW from $4000 + L; IYH = 0 for the next load to go on to $FFFF.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "14198": {"comment":"$4000-$47FF"},
        "14201": {"comment":"The next load to $FFFF"},
        "14205": {"synopsis":"SNAP_LOW from $4000.","comment":"From $4000"},
        "14207": {"synopsis":"Loads the snapshot's RAM from $4000 + L to $47FF, then uses the bytes at $4000 on as the\nregisters block and the run list:\n1. The rest of the run list (from the current run's count) is moved to $4047, IX following.\n2. The map at the other HL (SNAP_MAP_COPY) copies first the stub's bytes from this ROM (D =\n   0)\nto $4018-$4026, then the header's values from $5000 (D = $50) to the registers block.\n3. $401D = $10 and $4015 = 4: the paging for a 48K machine.\n4. With the header's interrupt byte ($4014) 0, the stub's EI ($4025) becomes a NOP.\nEntry: L = the low byte to start from; the other HL = the map.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX; the other set's HL.","comment":"From $40xx"},
        "14209": {"comment":"... to $47FF"},
        "14212": {"comment":"Loaded"},
        "14215": {"comment":"The map in HL"},
        "14216": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14217": {"comment":"The run list's end"},
        "14220": {"comment":"IX at the current run's count"},
        "14224": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "14226": {"comment":"BC = the bytes left in the list"},
        "14230": {"comment":"The new place"},
        "14233": {"comment":"IX follows it"},
        "14238": {"comment":"HL = the old place"},
        "14239": {"comment":"Moved"},
        "14241": {"comment":"The map"},
        "14242": {"comment":"The stub's bytes from this ROM"},
        "14247": {"comment":"The values from the header"},
        "14252": {"comment":"Port $7FFD's byte for 48K"},
        "14257": {"comment":"Port $1FFD's byte for 48K"},
        "14261": {"comment":"The disk's registers back"},
        "14262": {"comment":"Interrupts on in the program?"},
        "14266": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "14267": {"comment":"No: the stub's EI a NOP"},
        "14271": {"synopsis":"Copies bytes into $4000-$403F as a map at HL says, until an entry with bit 7 set: each entry\nis a source low byte (the high byte is D), then a byte whose bits 0-5 are the low byte of\nthe\nplace at $40xx and whose bits 6-7 are the count less 1.\nEntry: HL = the map, D = the source's high byte.\nExit: HL past the end byte.\nChanges: AF, BC, E, HL.","comment":"Places at $40xx"},
        "14273": {"synopsis":"One entry of the map.","comment":"E = the source's low byte"},
        "14275": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "14278": {"comment":"The place"},
        "14279": {"comment":"... in bits 0-5"},
        "14282": {"comment":"The count less 1"},
        "14283": {"comment":"... from bits 6-7"},
        "14287": {"comment":"Past the entry"},
        "14288": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14289": {"comment":"L = the count"},
        "14291": {"synopsis":"Copies L bytes from DE to BC.","comment":"A byte"},
        "14293": {"comment":"... to its place"},
        "14295": {"comment":"All of them?"},
        "14298": {"comment":"The map back"},
        "14301": {"synopsis":"Writes A to port $7FFD (only: $5B5C is left as it is), keeping BC.","comment":"Kept"},
        "14302": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "14307": {"comment":"Back"},
        "14309": {"synopsis":"The map for the second layout (SNAP_MAP_COPY), two lists each ended by $80: the stub's bytes\nfrom this ROM's $002F-$0035 to $4018-$4026, then the header's values at $5000 to their\nplaces\nin the registers block and the stub (the first layout's map is at $0010)."},
        "14355": {"synopsis":"Loads bytes as they are from HL until H AND $F8 reaches IYH.","comment":"The run used up?"},
        "14357": {"comment":"Yes: the next run"},
        "14360": {"comment":"One byte fewer"},
        "14361": {"comment":"A byte from the disk"},
        "14363": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "14364": {"comment":"Within the page?"},
        "14368": {"comment":"The next page"},
        "14369": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "14377": {"synopsis":"Loads the snapshot's RAM from HL until H AND $F8 reaches IYH (IYH = 0: to $FFFF): as it is\nwhen IYL is 0 (SNAP_COPY_LOOP), otherwise unpacked: ED ED n b stands for n bytes b (n = 0\nfor\n256), and any other byte stands for itself.\nEntry: HL = the address, IYL, IYH; the disk's registers in BC, DE and IX.\nChanges: AF, HL; BC = $CEEF, DE.","comment":"Packed?"},
        "14380": {"comment":"No"},
        "14382": {"synopsis":"One byte of the packed RAM: $ED goes to SNAP_UNP_ED.","comment":"The run used up?"},
        "14384": {"comment":"Yes: the next run"},
        "14387": {"comment":"One byte fewer"},
        "14388": {"comment":"A byte from the disk"},
        "14390": {"comment":"$ED?"},
        "14394": {"synopsis":"Stores a byte and moves on.","comment":"Stored"},
        "14395": {"comment":"Within the page?"},
        "14400": {"synopsis":"The end when H AND $F8 reaches IYH.","comment":"The end?"},
        "14408": {"synopsis":"An $ED: a second $ED makes a run (count, then the byte); anything else stands for itself\nafter the $ED (SNAP_UNP_ONE_ED).","comment":"The next byte"},
        "14411": {"comment":"$ED too?"},
        "14415": {"comment":"The count"},
        "14418": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14419": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "14422": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "14423": {"synopsis":"Stores the byte B times.","comment":"The byte"},
        "14425": {"comment":"... B times"},
        "14427": {"comment":"BC back for the disk"},
        "14432": {"synopsis":"A lone $ED: stored, then the byte after it (SNAP_UNP_STORE); past $FFFF carry, the end.","comment":"The $ED stored"},
        "14435": {"comment":"Then the byte after it"},
        "14437": {"comment":"The next page"},
        "14438": {"comment":"... and the byte after it"},
        "14440": {"comment":"Past $FFFF: done"},
        "14442": {"synopsis":"Reads a memory block's header of the second layout's further kind: its length (2 bytes;\n$FFFF\nmeans stored as it is, IYL = 0, else packed) and its page.\nEntry: carry clear.\nExit: A = the page; IYL set.","comment":"The length, low"},
        "14445": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14446": {"comment":"High"},
        "14449": {"comment":"$FFFF"},
        "14450": {"comment":"... gives 0"},
        "14451": {"comment":"IYL: 0 for as it is"},
        "14453": {"synopsis":"Reads the next byte of the file from the disk: when the current run is used up (DE = 0) the\nnext one is started (SNAP_NEXT_RUN), then a byte from port $CEEF.\nEntry: BC = $CEEF, DE = the bytes left of the run, IX = the run list.\nExit: A = the byte.\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"The run used up?"},
        "14455": {"comment":"Yes: the next run"},
        "14458": {"comment":"One byte fewer"},
        "14459": {"comment":"A byte from the disk"},
        "14462": {"synopsis":"Starts the next run of the list at IX ($2776), unless the list has ended ($FF).","comment":"The list's end?"},
        "14466": {"comment":"No: the next run asked for"},
        "14470": {"synopsis":"Lists where the next A:DE bytes of an open file lie on the hard disk, so that they can be\nread straight from the drive (SNAP_LOAD, and the routine at $1A10). The file must be open\nfor\nreading only (mode byte 1 at its record's +$20; else error $1D) on a partition's drive (+$06\nnot 0 and the read routine at +$2C $27E1; else error $1D, or DRIVE_FIND's):\n1. The list starts with a word: the file pointer's low byte, the bytes to skip in the first\n256-byte sector. ($F511) = the number of 256-byte sectors to read; ($F513) = the sector\nwithin the first block.\n2. For each extent (EXTENT_HOLDS, EXTENT_FIND) and each of its blocks, the block's first\nsector in the partition is turned into the drive's register values ($26B1, which sets\nthem) and these are read back from ports $FEEF, $EFEF, $EEEF and $DFEF into the list,\nfollowed by the number of sectors to read there (the rest of the block, or fewer at the\nend).\n3. $FF ends the list.\nEntry: BC = the file's record, A:DE = the bytes to read, HL = the list.\nExit: carry set and HL past the $FF; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; $F511-$F515.","comment":"The byte count kept"},
        "14472": {"comment":"The list's next place"},
        "14475": {"comment":"The record's mode byte"},
        "14480": {"comment":"Bits 0-1"},
        "14482": {"comment":"Read only?"},
        "14483": {"comment":"Error $1D"},
        "14487": {"comment":"The record's drive letter"},
        "14489": {"comment":"IX = its parameter block"},
        "14492": {"comment":"No such drive?"},
        "14494": {"comment":"+$06 0?"},
        "14500": {"comment":"Its read routine"},
        "14506": {"comment":"A partition's?"},
        "14513": {"synopsis":"Not a hard disk file: error $1D.","comment":"Error $1D"},
        "14515": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "14516": {"synopsis":"Leaves with the error: the byte count dropped.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "14519": {"synopsis":"A file on a partition: the list's first word, then the number of sectors to read.","comment":"E:HL = the file pointer"},
        "14522": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "14524": {"comment":"At the list"},
        "14528": {"comment":"The pointer's low byte"},
        "14531": {"comment":"... as the first word"},
        "14535": {"comment":"HL = the pointer's 256-byte sector"},
        "14537": {"comment":"DE = the bytes to skip"},
        "14543": {"comment":"The list past the word"},
        "14551": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "14553": {"comment":"A = the count's high byte"},
        "14554": {"comment":"HL = its low word"},
        "14556": {"comment":"The first sector's bytes"},
        "14562": {"comment":"... in DE"},
        "14565": {"comment":"Less them"},
        "14567": {"comment":"A:HL = the bytes past it"},
        "14569": {"comment":"E = the high byte"},
        "14570": {"comment":"Any in a part sector?"},
        "14572": {"comment":"HL = the whole sectors past it"},
        "14574": {"comment":"The first sector"},
        "14577": {"comment":"No part sector"},
        "14579": {"comment":"And the part sector"},
        "14580": {"synopsis":"Stores the number of 256-byte sectors to read at $F511, then the sector within the first\nblock at $F513, and the file's first block number in DE.","comment":"The sectors to read"},
        "14584": {"comment":"DE = the file's 256-byte sector"},
        "14585": {"comment":"The block mask"},
        "14588": {"comment":"... in 256-byte sectors"},
        "14590": {"comment":"The sector in its block"},
        "14594": {"comment":"The block shift"},
        "14597": {"comment":"Less 1 for 256-byte sectors"},
        "14598": {"comment":"DE = the block in the file"},
        "14601": {"synopsis":"Finds the extent holding block DE of the file and reads its directory entry into the\nrecord (EXTENT_HOLDS, EXTENT_FIND).","comment":"The block kept"},
        "14602": {"comment":"The block shift"},
        "14605": {"comment":"DE = the block's 128-byte record"},
        "14608": {"comment":"H, L = its extent bytes"},
        "14612": {"comment":"The record's +$0C"},
        "14616": {"comment":"Keeping the masked bits"},
        "14618": {"comment":"... with the extent's"},
        "14622": {"comment":"+$0E too"},
        "14623": {"comment":"Its directory entry"},
        "14626": {"comment":"The block back"},
        "14627": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "14628": {"comment":"The block in the extent"},
        "14631": {"comment":"Two bytes each"},
        "14632": {"comment":"From the record's +$10"},
        "14638": {"synopsis":"One block of the extent: its first 256-byte sector in the partition (plus the sector within\nit at $F513), the drive's register values for it into the list, then the number of sectors\nto read there.","comment":"The block kept"},
        "14639": {"comment":"DE = the block's number"},
        "14643": {"comment":"The next one's place kept"},
        "14644": {"comment":"The record kept"},
        "14645": {"comment":"The block shift"},
        "14648": {"comment":"Less 1 for 256-byte sectors"},
        "14649": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14650": {"comment":"DE = the block's first sector"},
        "14653": {"comment":"C = 0"},
        "14655": {"comment":"Plus the sector within it"},
        "14663": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "14665": {"comment":"The open partition"},
        "14674": {"comment":"The drive's registers set for it"},
        "14677": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "14679": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "14681": {"comment":"The list's next place"},
        "14684": {"comment":"The head register"},
        "14690": {"comment":"The cylinder high register"},
        "14696": {"comment":"The cylinder low register"},
        "14702": {"comment":"The sector register"},
        "14708": {"comment":"B = the block shift less 1"},
        "14709": {"comment":"The sector within the block"},
        "14712": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "14713": {"comment":"1"},
        "14715": {"synopsis":"Doubles A B times: the sectors in a block.","comment":"Doubled"},
        "14718": {"comment":"Less those before the start"},
        "14719": {"comment":"BC = the sectors to read here"},
        "14722": {"comment":"The list's place kept"},
        "14723": {"comment":"The sectors still to read"},
        "14726": {"comment":"L kept"},
        "14727": {"comment":"Fewer than these?"},
        "14730": {"comment":"No"},
        "14732": {"comment":"Yes: only them"},
        "14733": {"comment":"And none left (Z)"},
        "14734": {"synopsis":"Stores the sectors left, then the count of this run in the list; at Z (none left) the list\nis\nended, otherwise the next block from its first sector: in the same extent while the next\nplace is within the record's +$10-$1F, else in the next extent.","comment":"The sectors left"},
        "14737": {"comment":"The list's place"},
        "14738": {"comment":"The run's count"},
        "14740": {"comment":"The list's next place"},
        "14743": {"comment":"The record"},
        "14744": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "14745": {"comment":"None left: the end"},
        "14747": {"comment":"The next block's place"},
        "14748": {"comment":"The block's number"},
        "14749": {"comment":"From the block's start"},
        "14753": {"comment":"The next block"},
        "14754": {"comment":"The next block's place kept"},
        "14755": {"comment":"Past the record's +$1F?"},
        "14760": {"comment":"Within the extent?"},
        "14765": {"comment":"No: the next extent"},
        "14768": {"synopsis":"The drive's registers could not be set: two words dropped, then FRL_END; HL then holds the\nopen partition's address, which gets the $FF.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "14770": {"synopsis":"Ends the list with $FF; two words dropped.","comment":"The list's end"},
        "14773": {"comment":"Dropped"},
        "14776": {"synopsis":"Reads port BC into the list at HL and moves HL on.","comment":"The register"},
        "14778": {"comment":"... into the list"},
        "14781": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $019F) Does nothing but return error $3A.\nExit: carry clear, A = $3A.","comment":"Error $3A"},
        "14783": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "14785": {"synopsis":"Finds stream A's word in STRMS ($5C10, streams -3 to 15).\nEntry: A = the stream.\nExit: carry set, HL = the word's address, BC = the word (its channel's offset from CHANS\nplus 1, or 0 when closed); carry clear and A = $17 for a stream outside -3 to 15.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"Streams from -3 on"},
        "14787": {"comment":"Above 15?"},
        "14791": {"comment":"Two bytes each"},
        "14792": {"comment":"STRMS"},
        "14799": {"comment":"BC = the word"},
        "14802": {"comment":"HL at it"},
        "14803": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "14805": {"synopsis":"A word dropped, then error $17.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "14806": {"synopsis":"Error $17, carry clear.","comment":"Error $17"},
        "14808": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "14810": {"synopsis":"Steps past an entry's word, then on to the next entry (TBL_FIND).","comment":"Past the word"},
        "14812": {"synopsis":"Looks for character C in a table of 3-byte entries (a character, then a routine's address)\nended by 0.\nEntry: HL = the table, C = the character.\nExit: carry set and HL at the entry's word; carry clear when not found.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The entry's character"},
        "14814": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "14816": {"comment":"This one?"},
        "14819": {"comment":"Carry: found"},
        "14821": {"synopsis":"Reads \",n\" from the text (NUM_AFTER_COMMA) and checks that n is not above the limit in HL.\nEntry: HL = the limit, DE = the text, BC = its length.\nExit: carry set and HL = n when there is one within the limit; carry clear otherwise.\nDE and BC past it.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The limit kept"},
        "14822": {"comment":"\",n\"?"},
        "14825": {"comment":"None"},
        "14827": {"comment":"DE = n"},
        "14828": {"comment":"HL = the limit"},
        "14829": {"comment":"Above it?"},
        "14832": {"comment":"Carry when not"},
        "14833": {"comment":"HL = the text"},
        "14834": {"comment":"HL = n, DE = the text"},
        "14836": {"synopsis":"No number: the limit dropped.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "14838": {"synopsis":"Reads a comma and a number after it (NUM_PARSE) from the text.\nEntry: DE = the text, BC = its length.\nExit: carry set and HL = the number; carry clear when the text has ended (Z) or goes on with\nsomething other than a comma (NZ).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Any text left?"},
        "14840": {"comment":"No: Z and no carry"},
        "14841": {"comment":"A comma?"},
        "14844": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "14846": {"comment":"... when not"},
        "14847": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14849": {"synopsis":"Reads a decimal number from the text, skipping spaces, up to the first other character or\nthe end of the text.\nEntry: DE = the text, BC = its length.\nExit: carry set, HL = the number (0 for none); DE at the first other character, BC the\nlength left.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The number so far"},
        "14852": {"synopsis":"One character: a space is skipped, a digit taken in, anything else ends the number.","comment":"Text left?"},
        "14854": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "14855": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "14856": {"comment":"The character"},
        "14857": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "14861": {"comment":"Below '0': done"},
        "14864": {"comment":"Above '9'?"},
        "14866": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "14869": {"comment":"HL times 2"},
        "14872": {"comment":"Times 8"},
        "14874": {"comment":"Times 10"},
        "14878": {"comment":"Plus the digit"},
        "14880": {"synopsis":"The next character.","comment":"The next character"},
        "14884": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $0056) Attaches stream A to the channel the text at DE (length BC) names:\n1. The stream must be closed or attached to K, S or P (error $17).\n2. One character: K, S or P (STD_CHAN_TABLE), the standard channels, words 1, 6 and $10.\n3. More: \"x>\" first names the kind, I, O, U, M, V or W (CHAN_TYPE_TABLE, small letters too);\nwith no \">\" the kind is I and all the text is the name. Its routine makes the channel.\n4. The channel's offset goes into the stream's word in STRMS.\nEntry: A = the stream, DE = the text, BC = its length.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = $17 for a bad stream, $0E for any other\nfailure.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The length kept"},
        "14885": {"comment":"The stream's word"},
        "14888": {"comment":"Bad stream?"},
        "14890": {"comment":"Closed?"},
        "14894": {"comment":"Its channel's letter"},
        "14904": {"comment":"K?"},
        "14908": {"comment":"S?"},
        "14912": {"comment":"P?"},
        "14914": {"comment":"No: error $17"},
        "14916": {"synopsis":"The text: one character names a standard channel, more a channel to make.","comment":"The length"},
        "14917": {"comment":"The stream's word kept"},
        "14918": {"comment":"K, S or P"},
        "14921": {"comment":"Any text?"},
        "14925": {"comment":"One character?"},
        "14929": {"comment":"A = the first character"},
        "14930": {"comment":"Yes: a standard channel"},
        "14932": {"comment":"The kinds to make"},
        "14936": {"comment":"The second character"},
        "14938": {"comment":"A \">\"?"},
        "14940": {"comment":"I for none"},
        "14944": {"comment":"The kind"},
        "14945": {"comment":"Past \"x>\""},
        "14949": {"synopsis":"Finds the kind's routine in the table at HL and calls it; DE (the channel's offset) goes\ninto the stream's word.","comment":"A capital"},
        "14952": {"comment":"C = the kind"},
        "14953": {"comment":"Its routine"},
        "14957": {"comment":"Unknown?"},
        "14959": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "14963": {"comment":"The channel made"},
        "14966": {"comment":"The stream's word"},
        "14967": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "14969": {"comment":"The offset into it"},
        "14972": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "14974": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL: called, it calls the routine at HL.","comment":"To the routine"},
        "14975": {"synopsis":"A word dropped, then error $0E.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "14976": {"synopsis":"Error $0E, carry clear.","comment":"Error $0E"},
        "14978": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "14980": {"synopsis":"The standard channels a stream can be attached to (TBL_FIND): K SOPEN_K, S SOPEN_S, P\nSOPEN_P, then 0."},
        "14990": {"synopsis":"K: DE = 1, the channel at CHANS.","comment":"Offset 1"},
        "14994": {"synopsis":"S: DE = 6.","comment":"Offset 6"},
        "14998": {"synopsis":"P: DE = $10.","comment":"Offset $10"},
        "15000": {"synopsis":"D = 0 and carry set: DE is the offset.","comment":"DE = the offset"},
        "15002": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "15004": {"synopsis":"The kinds of channel to make (TBL_FIND): I SOPEN_I, O SOPEN_O, U SOPEN_U, M SOPEN_M, V\nSOPEN_V, W SOPEN_W, then 0."},
        "15023": {"synopsis":"U: a file opened for reading and writing, D = 2, E = 2 for OPEN_BY_NAME.","comment":"D = 2, E = 2"},
        "15026": {"comment":"Read and write"},
        "15030": {"synopsis":"O: a file opened for writing, D = 2, E = 4.","comment":"D = 2, E = 4"},
        "15033": {"comment":"Write"},
        "15037": {"synopsis":"I: a file opened for reading, D = 0, E = 2.","comment":"D = 0, E = 2"},
        "15040": {"comment":"Read"},
        "15042": {"synopsis":"Makes a channel F for a file:\n1. The name (up to 17 characters) is copied to $C022 in bank 7, ended by $FF.\n2. The first file number from 2 to 15 that is not open (FILE_FREE_REC) is taken; none: the\nerror FILE_FREE_REC gives.\n3. The file is opened by OPEN_BY_NAME with C = the access (1 read, 2 write, 3 both) and D, E\nfrom the kind. Each DOS call runs with bank 7 in and the stack moved (BANK7_STACK,\nSYSVARS_SAVE, then SYSVARS_RESTORE, BANK0_STACK).\n4. A 14-byte channel is made from F_CHAN_TEMPL (CHAN_NEW) with the file number at +$0D.\nEntry: A = the access, HL = D and E, DE = the name, BC = its length.\nExit: carry set and DE = the channel's offset; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The access kept"},
        "15043": {"comment":"D and E kept"},
        "15044": {"comment":"The name's place in bank 7"},
        "15047": {"comment":"Longer than 255?"},
        "15051": {"comment":"B = the length"},
        "15053": {"comment":"Up to 17?"},
        "15057": {"synopsis":"17 characters at most.","comment":"17 at most"},
        "15059": {"synopsis":"Copies the name to bank 7 a character at a time.","comment":"HL = the name"},
        "15060": {"synopsis":"One character: read with the caller's paging, written with bank 7 in.","comment":"A character"},
        "15062": {"comment":"Bank 7 in"},
        "15065": {"comment":"... to $C022 on"},
        "15067": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "15070": {"comment":"For all of it"},
        "15072": {"comment":"Bank 7 in"},
        "15075": {"comment":"The end marker"},
        "15078": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "15081": {"comment":"From file number 2"},
        "15083": {"synopsis":"Tries file number B: free (FILE_FREE_REC) goes on to SOPEN_FILE_NO.","comment":"Kept"},
        "15084": {"comment":"Bank 7 in"},
        "15087": {"comment":"The system variables aside"},
        "15090": {"comment":"File B free?"},
        "15093": {"comment":"Them back"},
        "15096": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "15100": {"comment":"Free?"},
        "15102": {"comment":"The next number"},
        "15104": {"comment":"Up to 15?"},
        "15108": {"comment":"Dropped"},
        "15111": {"synopsis":"A free file number: the file opened as it, then the channel made.","comment":"The name"},
        "15114": {"comment":"D and E"},
        "15115": {"comment":"The access"},
        "15116": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "15117": {"comment":"B and C kept"},
        "15118": {"comment":"Bank 7 in"},
        "15121": {"comment":"The system variables aside"},
        "15124": {"comment":"The file opened"},
        "15127": {"comment":"Them back"},
        "15130": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "15133": {"comment":"Failed?"},
