        "15236": {"comment":"Only one?"},
        "15238": {"comment":"A capital"},
        "15240": {"comment":"Below A?"},
        "15244": {"comment":"Above Z?"},
        "15247": {"comment":"L = the letter"},
        "15248": {"comment":"Then \"$\"?"},
        "15254": {"comment":"The last character?"},
        "15256": {"comment":"Bit 7 set"},
        "15258": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "15259": {"comment":"The template"},
        "15262": {"comment":"A channel of 16 bytes"},
        "15265": {"comment":"13 from the template"},
        "15268": {"comment":"The channel made"},
        "15271": {"comment":"HL at its +$0D"},
        "15275": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "15276": {"comment":"... to +$0D"},
        "15277": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "15279": {"synopsis":"The first 13 bytes of a channel V (a string variable): output and input $5B00, the letter V,\nthe words $39EF, $39D7 and $39FB, and the length $0010."},
        "15292": {"synopsis":"W: a channel W, a window of the screen, from \"W>row,column,height,width[,character\nwidth[,address]]\":\n1. Row 0-23, column 0-31, height up to 24 less the row, width up to 32 less the column.\n2. The character width, 3 to 8 (8 when not given), chooses a character set from\nW_FONT_TABLE; a sixth number gives one's address instead (256 is taken off it; below\n$4000 makes nothing).\n3. A 77-byte channel from W_CHAN_TEMPL: +$0D the column, +$0E the row, +$0F the right\ncolumn, +$10 the bottom row, +$11 the column, +$12 the row times 8, +$13 the character\nwidth, +$14-$15 the character set, +$18 the characters a line, +$19 ATTR_P.\nAny number out of range: nothing made, carry clear. The width alone is not refused: without\nit 32 less the column is taken, and one too large is kept as it is.\nExit: carry set and DE = the channel's offset.","comment":"The row"},
        "15295": {"comment":"Above 255?"},
        "15298": {"comment":"Above 23?"},
        "15302": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "15303": {"comment":"Up to 31"},
        "15306": {"comment":"The column"},
        "15309": {"comment":"Bad?"},
        "15312": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "15313": {"comment":"L = the row"},
        "15314": {"comment":"H = the column"},
        "15315": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "15316": {"comment":"Up to 24 less the row"},
        "15322": {"comment":"The height"},
        "15325": {"comment":"Bad?"},
        "15328": {"comment":"The height kept"},
        "15329": {"comment":"H, L kept"},
        "15330": {"comment":"Up to 32 less the column"},
        "15336": {"comment":"The width"},
        "15339": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "15340": {"comment":"H, L back"},
        "15341": {"comment":"The height again"},
        "15342": {"comment":"H = the width"},
        "15343": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "15344": {"comment":"A character width?"},
        "15347": {"comment":"8 when not"},
        "15351": {"comment":"Above 255?"},
        "15356": {"comment":"3 or more?"},
        "15359": {"comment":"Carry when not"},
        "15362": {"comment":"Up to 8?"},
        "15366": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "15367": {"comment":"Its own character set?"},
        "15370": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "15372": {"comment":"The width given"},
        "15373": {"synopsis":"Takes the character set for width A from W_FONT_TABLE.","comment":"Kept"},
        "15374": {"comment":"The character sets"},
        "15377": {"comment":"Width 3?"},
        "15381": {"synopsis":"Moves on one word of W_FONT_TABLE per width above 3.","comment":"The next word"},
        "15383": {"comment":"Its width?"},
        "15386": {"synopsis":"HL = the character set from the table.","comment":"HL = the character set"},
        "15390": {"comment":"Then the channel"},
        "15392": {"synopsis":"A character set's address given: below $4000 makes nothing; 256 is taken off it.","comment":"Below $4000?"},
        "15395": {"comment":"Yes: nothing"},
        "15397": {"comment":"Less 256"},
        "15398": {"synopsis":"Makes the channel when all the text was used, and fills it in.","comment":"Text left?"},
        "15400": {"comment":"Yes: nothing"},
        "15402": {"comment":"The character set kept"},
        "15403": {"comment":"The template"},
        "15406": {"comment":"A channel of 77 bytes"},
        "15409": {"comment":"13 from the template"},
        "15412": {"comment":"The channel made"},
        "15415": {"comment":"HL at its +$15"},
        "15419": {"comment":"The character set"},
        "15420": {"comment":"... to +$14-$15"},
        "15424": {"comment":"The character width"},
        "15425": {"comment":"... to +$13"},
        "15427": {"comment":"B = the width, C = the height"},
        "15428": {"comment":"DE = the column, row"},
        "15429": {"comment":"... the offset kept instead"},
        "15431": {"comment":"The width kept"},
        "15432": {"comment":"The row times 8"},
        "15436": {"comment":"... to +$12"},
        "15438": {"comment":"The column to +$11"},
        "15440": {"comment":"The height"},
        "15441": {"comment":"... plus the row"},
        "15442": {"comment":"... less 1"},
        "15443": {"comment":"... to +$10: the bottom row"},
        "15445": {"comment":"The width"},
        "15446": {"comment":"... plus the column"},
        "15447": {"comment":"... less 1"},
        "15448": {"comment":"... to +$0F: the right column"},
        "15450": {"comment":"The row to +$0E"},
        "15452": {"comment":"The column to +$0D"},
        "15453": {"comment":"E = the width"},
        "15456": {"comment":"HL = the width, DE = +$0D"},
        "15457": {"comment":"Times 8: in pixels"},
        "15460": {"comment":"The character width"},
        "15461": {"comment":"... in BC"},
        "15464": {"comment":"A counts the characters"},
        "15465": {"synopsis":"Counts how many characters of width BC go into HL.","comment":"One character fewer"},
        "15467": {"comment":"One more character"},
        "15468": {"comment":"Room for it?"},
        "15470": {"comment":"A = the characters a line"},
        "15471": {"comment":"The channel's +$18"},
        "15475": {"comment":"The characters a line"},
        "15477": {"comment":"ATTR_P"},
        "15480": {"comment":"... to +$19"},
        "15481": {"comment":"DE = the offset"},
        "15482": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "15484": {"synopsis":"Three words dropped: nothing made.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "15485": {"synopsis":"Two words dropped: nothing made.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "15486": {"synopsis":"One word dropped: nothing made.","comment":"Dropped"},
        "15488": {"synopsis":"The character sets for character widths 3 to 8 (SOPEN_W_FONT): $2B62, $2B62, $2B7B, $2B7B,\n$2B3E and $2B1F (used as they are; an address given in the text has 256 taken off)."},
        "15500": {"synopsis":"The first 13 bytes of a channel W (a window): output and input $5B00, the letter W, the\nwords\n$27D0, $399C and $399C, and the length $004D."},
        "15513": {"synopsis":"Makes a channel of BC bytes at the end of CHANS, just before its end marker (at PROG - 1):\nthe room is made by ROM 0's routine at $3FAF (which calls ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM), the first DE\nbytes are copied from the template at HL and the rest cleared.\nEntry: HL = the template, DE = the bytes in it, BC = the channel's length.\nExit: HL = the channel, DE = its offset from CHANS plus 1 (the word for STRMS).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; the other register set.","comment":"The template kept"},
        "15514": {"comment":"Its length kept"},
        "15515": {"comment":"The channel's length kept"},
        "15516": {"comment":"CHANS' end marker"},
        "15519": {"comment":"... at PROG - 1"},
        "15520": {"comment":"Kept: the new channel's place"},
        "15521": {"comment":"HL and BC in the other set"},
        "15522": {"comment":"ROM 0: room at HL"},
        "15527": {"comment":"DE = the channel"},
        "15528": {"comment":"HL = its length"},
        "15529": {"comment":"BC = the template's length"},
        "15531": {"comment":"The bytes to clear"},
        "15533": {"comment":"The template"},
        "15534": {"comment":"The channel kept"},
        "15535": {"comment":"The template copied"},
        "15537": {"comment":"HL = the channel"},
        "15538": {"comment":"BC = the bytes to clear"},
        "15539": {"synopsis":"Clears the rest of the channel, BC bytes at DE.","comment":"Any left?"},
        "15543": {"comment":"A zero"},
        "15546": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "15549": {"synopsis":"DE = the channel's offset from CHANS plus 1.","comment":"The channel kept"},
        "15550": {"comment":"CHANS"},
        "15555": {"comment":"The offset"},
        "15557": {"comment":"Plus 1"},
        "15558": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "15559": {"comment":"HL = the channel"},
        "15561": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $0059) Closes stream A:\n1. A closed stream: carry set at once.\n2. The channel's letter chooses its routine from CLOSE_TABLE (an unknown one: error $17),\ncalled with DE = the channel + 4; its failure gives error $12.\n3. The stream's word gets its first value back: the word from STRMS_DEFAULTS for streams -3\n   to\n3, 0 for the others.\nEntry: A = the stream.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The stream's word"},
        "15564": {"comment":"Bad stream?"},
        "15565": {"comment":"Closed?"},
        "15567": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "15568": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "15569": {"comment":"The word's address kept"},
        "15570": {"comment":"The channel"},
        "15573": {"comment":"... its letter"},
        "15577": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "15578": {"comment":"DE = the channel + 4"},
        "15579": {"comment":"The close routines"},
        "15582": {"comment":"C's routine"},
        "15585": {"comment":"Unknown?"},
        "15588": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "15592": {"comment":"The channel closed"},
        "15595": {"comment":"The stream's word"},
        "15596": {"comment":"Error $12"},
        "15598": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "15599": {"comment":"0 for streams 4 on"},
        "15602": {"comment":"Less $5C1E"},
        "15606": {"comment":"Streams 4 on?"},
        "15609": {"comment":"STRMS_DEFAULTS"},
        "15612": {"comment":"... at the stream's word"},
        "15613": {"comment":"BC = its first value"},
        "15616": {"synopsis":"Stores BC as the stream's word.","comment":"HL = the stream's word"},
        "15617": {"comment":"BC into it"},
        "15620": {"synopsis":"K, S or P: nothing to close, carry set.","comment":"Carry: done"},
        "15622": {"synopsis":"The close routines by channel letter (TBL_FIND): K, S and P SCLOSE_STD, F SCLOSE_F, M, V and\nW\nSCLOSE_RECLAIM, then 0."},
        "15644": {"synopsis":"The first words of STRMS for streams -3 to 3 ($5C10-$5C1D), put back when one is closed: 1,\n6, $0B, 1, 1, 6 and $10."},
        "15658": {"synopsis":"F: the channel's file (number at the channel's +$0D) closed by CLOSE_FILE, with bank 7 in\nand the stack moved; then the channel removed (SCLOSE_RECLAIM).","comment":"The channel's +$0D"},
        "15662": {"comment":"B = the file number"},
        "15663": {"comment":"The channel + 4 kept"},
        "15664": {"comment":"Bank 7 in"},
        "15667": {"comment":"The system variables aside"},
        "15670": {"comment":"The file closed"},
        "15673": {"comment":"Them back"},
        "15676": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "15679": {"comment":"The channel + 4"},
        "15680": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "15681": {"synopsis":"Removes the channel from CHANS: its length (word at +$0B) and its address go to ROM 0's\nroutine at $3F77 (which calls ROM 3's RECLAIM).\nEntry: DE = the channel + 4.\nExit: carry set.","comment":"The channel's +$0B"},
        "15685": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "15688": {"comment":"DE = the channel"},
        "15692": {"comment":"HL = the channel"},
        "15693": {"comment":"HL and BC in the other set"},
        "15694": {"comment":"ROM 0: the channel removed"},
        "15699": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "15701": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $005F) Calls ROM 0's routine at $392D with DE = 0, the register sets exchanged\nfirst.","comment":"The other set"},
        "15702": {"comment":"DE = 0"},
        "15705": {"synopsis":"Calls ROM 0's routine at $392D with the DE given.","comment":"ROM 0's $392D"},
        "15711": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $005C) Calls ROM 0's routine at $392D with DE = 2; unlike the others the\nregister sets are not exchanged.","comment":"DE = 2"},
        "15716": {"synopsis":"(The JP at $0062) Calls ROM 0's routine at $392D with DE = 4, the register sets exchanged\nfirst.","comment":"The other set"},
        "15717": {"comment":"DE = 4"},
        "15722": {"synopsis":"The way back from BANK7_STACK: port $7FFD = 0 (bank 0 at $C000, bit 4 clear; $5B5C\ntoo), and SP exchanged with the word at $5B6A; AF and HL kept.\nChanges: SP; port $7FFD and $5B5C.","comment":"AF kept"},
        "15723": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "15724": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "15725": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = 0"},
        "15728": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "15729": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "15732": {"comment":"The other stack"},
        "15735": {"comment":"This one noted"},
        "15739": {"comment":"... in use"},
        "15740": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "15741": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "15744": {"comment":"The return address on it"},
        "15745": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "15747": {"synopsis":"Writes A to port $7FFD and to its copy $5B5C, keeping BC.","comment":"Kept"},
        "15748": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "15753": {"comment":"Its copy"},
        "15756": {"comment":"Back"},
        "15758": {"synopsis":"Changes to the stack noted at $5B6A (exchanging SP with it) and pages bank 7 in (port $7FFD\n= 7, $5B5C too); AF and HL kept. BANK0_STACK is the way back.\nChanges: SP; port $7FFD and $5B5C.","comment":"AF kept"},
        "15759": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "15760": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "15761": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "15764": {"comment":"The other stack"},
        "15767": {"comment":"This one noted"},
        "15771": {"comment":"... in use"},
        "15772": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "15775": {"comment":"The return address on it"},
        "15776": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "15781": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "15782": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "15784": {"synopsis":"Before a DOS call from BASIC: $5B7C-$5BFF (132 bytes) go to $E77C-$E7FF in bank 7, SP is\nnoted\nat $E602 and the stack set to $5BFF; all the main registers kept. SYSVARS_RESTORE is the way\nback.\nChanges: SP.","comment":"The registers noted"},
        "15787": {"comment":"$5B7C-$5BFF"},
        "15790": {"comment":"... to $E77C-$E7FF"},
        "15793": {"comment":"132 bytes"},
        "15798": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "15799": {"comment":"SP noted"},
        "15803": {"comment":"The stack at $5BFF"},
        "15807": {"comment":"The return address on it"},
        "15808": {"synopsis":"Takes BC, DE, AF and HL back from $E606-$E60D and returns with interrupts on.","comment":"BC back"},
        "15812": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "15816": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "15821": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "15824": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "15826": {"synopsis":"Interrupts off, then HL, AF, DE and BC noted at $E608, $E606, $E60A and $E60C.","comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "15827": {"comment":"HL noted"},
        "15830": {"comment":"AF noted"},
        "15835": {"comment":"DE noted"},
        "15839": {"comment":"BC noted"},
        "15844": {"synopsis":"After a DOS call: $E77C-$E7FF back to $5B7C-$5BFF and SP back from $E602; all the main\nregisters kept.\nChanges: SP.","comment":"The registers noted"},
        "15847": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "15848": {"comment":"... noted"},
        "15851": {"comment":"$E77C-$E7FF"},
        "15854": {"comment":"... back to $5B7C-$5BFF"},
        "15857": {"comment":"132 bytes"},
        "15862": {"comment":"SP back"},
        "15866": {"comment":"The return address on it"},
        "15870": {"comment":"The registers back"},
        "15872": {"synopsis":"Calls the address in the word after the CALL in ROM 0, keeping AF and HL: they are parked at\n$5B56 and $5B52; the word is read (and stepped over on the stack) into HL; bit 2 of port\n$1FFD (and its copy $5B67) is cleared with interrupts off, which pages ROM 0 in in place of\nthis one (bit 4 of port $7FFD being clear), and the code goes on there with CALL_ROM0_BACK\npushed as the way back.\nChanges: BC.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "15875": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "15880": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "15885": {"comment":"The return address stepped past it"},
        "15888": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "15903": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "15907": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "15908": {"comment":"AF and HL back"},
        "15916": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "15917": {"synopsis":"The way back from ROM 0: bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67) set again, which pages this ROM\nback in, keeping AF and BC.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "15919": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD set: this ROM"},
        "15934": {"comment":"Back"},
        "15937": {"synopsis":"Scans the keyboard: reads the eight half-rows (port $FE with B = $FE, $FD, ... $7F) and\ncollects up to two keys down as key numbers, E the last found and D the one before ($FF for\nnone).\nA key number is $2F less the half-row number less 8 x (bit + 1): CAPS SHIFT is $27, SYMBOL\nSHIFT $18 (Klive's key matrix: row 0 bit 0, row 7 bit 1).\nReturns NZ at once on a third key. At the end Z means the keys are usable: fewer than two,\nor two with CAPS SHIFT or SYMBOL SHIFT as one of them (then in D).\nExit: DE = the key numbers.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nThe 48K ROM's $0205-$03B4 are here in three pieces, the same but for the addresses in them:\nits key tables at $2239-$22C1, its code from $028E at $3E41-$3EE5 and from $0333 at\n$3F77-$3FF8.","comment":"L = $2F: the first half-row's key number"},
        "15939": {"comment":"No keys yet"},
        "15942": {"comment":"B = $FE: the first half-row"},
        "15945": {"synopsis":"Reads one half-row: A = its five key bits, 1 for a key down.","comment":"The half-row's bits"},
        "15947": {"comment":"1 for a key down"},
        "15948": {"comment":"Five keys"},
        "15950": {"comment":"A key down in this half-row?"},
        "15952": {"comment":"H = the keys down"},
        "15953": {"comment":"A = the half-row's number"},
        "15954": {"synopsis":"One more key found: NZ out at once when D already held one (three keys)."},
        "15955": {"comment":"A third key: not usable"},
        "15956": {"synopsis":"Finds the key's column: 8 off the number per bit shifted out of H."},
        "15958": {"comment":"The next key into the carry"},
        "15960": {"comment":"Until the key down"},
        "15962": {"comment":"D = the key before"},
        "15963": {"comment":"E = this key"},
        "15964": {"comment":"More keys in the half-row"},
        "15966": {"synopsis":"The next half-row, L one lower, until B's 0 bit has gone round.","comment":"The next half-row's number"},
        "15967": {"comment":"The next half-row"},
        "15969": {"comment":"Until all eight"},
        "15971": {"comment":"A second key in D?"},
        "15973": {"comment":"No: Z, done"},
        "15974": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT?"},
        "15976": {"comment":"Z: usable"},
        "15977": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT?"},
        "15979": {"comment":"Z: usable"},
        "15980": {"comment":"D and E swapped: the shift key into D"},
        "15983": {"comment":"Z when it is SYMBOL SHIFT; NZ: two keys, no shift"},
        "15986": {"synopsis":"Reads the keyboard, from INT_FRAME every frame while this ROM is paged in, and keeps the two\nkey sets of KSTATE (4 bytes each: the main code or $FF when unused, a release counter, the\nrepeat counter, the decoded code):\n1. READ_KEYS; nothing when it reports NZ (three keys, or two without a shift key).\n2. Each set in use counts its release counter down; at 0 the set is freed (KBD_SET_LOOP).\n3. KEY_MAIN_CODE turns the scan into a main code; none for no key or a shift key alone.\n4. A code a set already holds is a key still held: KBD_REPEAT. A new one goes into a free\n   set, the second one first, and is decoded (KBD_NEW_KEY); with both sets in use it is\n   ignored. A new or repeated key goes into LAST_K, with FLAGS bit 5 set.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; KSTATE, LAST_K, FLAGS.","comment":"The keys down"},
        "15989": {"comment":"Not usable"},
        "15990": {"comment":"HL = KSTATE's first set"},
        "15993": {"synopsis":"One key set: in use (bit 7 of its first byte clear)? Then its release counter one down, and\nthe set freed ($FF) when it reaches 0."},
        "15998": {"comment":"Its release counter down"},
        "16002": {"comment":"Freed"},
        "16004": {"synopsis":"After the set at $5C00, the one at $5C04.","comment":"A = L: which set?"},
        "16005": {"comment":"The second set next"},
        "16011": {"comment":"No usable key?"},
        "16018": {"comment":"Held in the first set?"},
        "16021": {"comment":"DE = the first set"},
        "16025": {"comment":"Held in the second set?"},
        "16028": {"comment":"The second set free?"},
        "16032": {"comment":"HL = the first set"},
        "16033": {"comment":"The first set free? Neither: the key is ignored"},
        "16036": {"synopsis":"A new key into the free set at HL: its main code, release counter 5, repeat counter REPDEL,\nthen the code KEY_DECODE gives for MODE (C), FLAGS (D) and the shift key (B).","comment":"E = the main code"},
        "16037": {"comment":"Into the set"},
        "16039": {"comment":"Release counter 5"},
        "16042": {"comment":"Repeat counter REPDEL"},
        "16047": {"comment":"C = MODE"},
        "16050": {"comment":"D = FLAGS"},
        "16054": {"comment":"A = the decoded code"},
        "16058": {"comment":"Into the set"},
        "16059": {"synopsis":"LAST_K = A, and FLAGS bit 5 set: a key is waiting."},
        "16067": {"synopsis":"A key still held: its release counter back to 5, and the repeat counter one down; at 0 it is\nset to REPPER and the set's decoded code goes into LAST_K again (KBD_STORE_KEY)."},
        "16068": {"comment":"Release counter 5 again"},
        "16071": {"comment":"Repeat counter down"},
        "16072": {"comment":"Not yet"},
        "16073": {"comment":"REPPER from now on"},
        "16078": {"comment":"A = the set's decoded code"},
        "16081": {"synopsis":"Turns READ_KEYS's key numbers into a main code: E is the key, D the shift key ($FF for\nnone).\nExit: carry and A = the key's code from KEYS_MAIN; no carry for no key, CAPS SHIFT alone\n($27) or SYMBOL SHIFT alone; B = the shift key, D = 0.\nChanges: AF, B, D, HL.","comment":"B = the shift key"},
        "16082": {"comment":"D = 0 for the index"},
        "16084": {"comment":"A = the key"},
        "16085": {"comment":"No key, or CAPS SHIFT alone?"},
        "16088": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT as the key"},
        "16092": {"comment":"... with no other: none"},
        "16095": {"synopsis":"A = KEYS_MAIN's code for key number E; carry set.","comment":"HL = KEYS_MAIN"},
        "16098": {"comment":"+ the key number"},
        "16100": {"comment":"Carry: a key"},
        "16102": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $019C) Turns the disk motor off at once: the time-out count at $E600 cleared,\nthen\nbit 3 of $5B67 cleared and written to port $1FFD ($21BA). Keeps AF.\nAlso from $1AA2 and $1FA0.","comment":"Kept"},
        "16103": {"comment":"No time-out count"},
        "16107": {"comment":"Bit 3 (the motor) cleared"},
        "16112": {"comment":"... to port $1FFD"},
        "16115": {"comment":"Back"},
        "16117": {"synopsis":"(DOS_JUMPS $0190) Runs a command block with a read execution phase: all its command bytes\nbut the last sent (CMD_SEND_HEAD), the last one and every byte the 765 gives into the buffer\n(EXEC_READ), then the results to $E430 (RESULTS_READ). Also from $1C80.\nEntry: HL = the command block.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"All but the last command byte"},
        "16120": {"comment":"The last, then the data in"},
        "16123": {"comment":"The results"},
        "16126": {"synopsis":"Unused: two bytes $00."},
        "16128": {"synopsis":"Entered in ROM 1's copy of these bytes, to call the address in the word after the CALL in\nthis ROM, keeping AF, BC and HL (parked at $5B56, $5B54 and $5B52): bit 4 of the paging byte\n$5B5C (port $7FFD) is cleared and bit 2 of $5B67 (port $1FFD) set, with interrupts off,\nwhich\npages this ROM in, and the code goes on at the address with CALL_ROM2_BACK pushed as the way\nback.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "16131": {"comment":"BC parked"},
        "16135": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "16140": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "16145": {"comment":"The return address stepped past it"},
        "16146": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "16150": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "16152": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD cleared"},
        "16166": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD set: this ROM"},
        "16180": {"comment":"The address on the stack"},
        "16181": {"comment":"AF, BC and HL back"},
        "16193": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16194": {"synopsis":"The way back to ROM 1: bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared and bit 4 of port $7FFD set again (and\ntheir copies), keeping AF and BC.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "16196": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared"},
        "16210": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD set: ROM 1"},
        "16224": {"comment":"Back"},
        "16227": {"synopsis":"The way back to ROM 0 from a call made through ROM 0's own routine at $3EC9 (which pushes\nthis address as the way back): bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67) cleared, keeping AF and BC;\nbit 4 of port $7FFD stays clear, so ROM 0 comes back in. Nothing in this ROM refers to it.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "16229": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16244": {"comment":"Back"},
        "16247": {"synopsis":"Turns a main code into the code the key gives: E = the main code, B = the shift key ($FF\nnone, $27 CAPS SHIFT, $18 SYMBOL SHIFT), C = MODE (0 K/L/C, 1 E, 2 G), D = FLAGS (bit 3 set:\nL mode). Letters ($41-$5A):\n1. MODE 0, no shift or CAPS SHIFT: a keyword token in K mode (KD_K_TOKEN); in L mode the\n   capital, or the small letter when neither CAPS SHIFT nor CAPS LOCK (FLAGS2 bit 3) is on.\n   SYMBOL SHIFT: KEYS_SYM_LETTERS.\n2. MODE 1: KEYS_E_LETTERS, or KEYS_E_SHIFTED with either shift key (KD_E_LETTER).\n3. MODE 2: the letter + $4F, A to U giving $90-$A4.\nDigits go to $3FAB; the other codes come back as they are.\nExit: A = the code.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"A = the main code"},
        "16248": {"comment":"Below \":\": a digit, space, ENTER or SYMBOL SHIFT"},
        "16252": {"comment":"MODE - 1"},
        "16253": {"comment":"MODE 0?"},
        "16256": {"comment":"MODE 1?"},
        "16258": {"comment":"MODE 2: A-U to $90-$A4"},
        "16261": {"synopsis":"A letter in E mode: KEYS_E_LETTERS with no shift key, KEYS_E_SHIFTED with either."},
        "16264": {"comment":"No shift key ($FF + 1 = 0)?"},
        "16267": {"comment":"Either: KEYS_E_SHIFTED"},
        "16270": {"synopsis":"A = the byte at HL + E: the key's entry in the table chosen (HL is the table's start less\nthe first code).","comment":"DE = the code"},
        "16275": {"synopsis":"A letter in K, L or C mode: with SYMBOL SHIFT (B bit 0 clear) from KEYS_SYM_LETTERS;\notherwise a token in K mode, a letter in L mode.","comment":"HL for KEYS_SYM_LETTERS"},
        "16278": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT ($18, bit 0 clear)?"},
        "16282": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 3 clear: K mode?"},
        "16286": {"comment":"CAPS LOCK: the capital"},
        "16291": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT: the capital"},
        "16293": {"comment":"Otherwise the small letter"},
        "16296": {"synopsis":"K mode: the letter + $A5, a keyword token (A gives $E6, NEW)."},
        "16299": {"synopsis":"Turns a key's character below ':' (reached from $3F7A) into the code it gives in the current\nmode. Characters below '0' stand as they are. For a digit: MODE 0 (K, L or C) keeps it with\nno shift, takes the table at $2264 (indexed by the digit at $3F8E) with caps shift, and\ngives the symbol on the key with symbol shift; MODE 1 (E) takes the table at $2288 with\nsymbol shift, and otherwise gives $10-$17 for '0'-'7' and $02/$03 for '8'/'9', with caps\nshift $18-$1F and $00/$01; MODE 2 (G) takes the table at $2264 for '9' and '0', gives\n$80-$87 for '8' and '1'-'7', and the inverse graphic (XOR $0F) when shifted.\nEntry: A = E = the character, C = MODE, B = the shift key's code ($FF for none; bit 5 set\nfor caps shift, clear for symbol shift).\nExit: A = the code.","comment":"Below '0': the code stands as it is"},
        "16302": {"comment":"MODE 0 (K, L or C)?"},
        "16306": {"comment":"MODE 2 or more (G)?"},
        "16308": {"comment":"E mode: HL = $2288, indexed by the digit at $3F8E"},
        "16311": {"comment":"Symbol shift (bit 5 clear) takes the table"},
        "16315": {"comment":"'8' or '9'?"},
        "16319": {"comment":"'0' to '7' give $10 to $17"},
        "16321": {"comment":"No shift: done"},
        "16323": {"comment":"Caps shift: $18 to $1F"},
        "16326": {"synopsis":"E mode, '8' or '9': $02/$03, or $00/$01 with caps shift.","comment":"'8' and '9' give $02 and $03"},
        "16328": {"comment":"No shift: done"},
        "16330": {"comment":"Caps shift: $00 and $01"},
        "16333": {"synopsis":"G mode digits: the table for '9' and '0', block graphics $80-$87 for the others, inverted\nwhen shifted.","comment":"G mode: HL = $2264, indexed by the digit at $3F8E"},
        "16336": {"comment":"'9' comes from the table"},
        "16340": {"comment":"So does '0'"},
        "16344": {"comment":"'1' to '7' give $81 to $87, '8' gives $80"},
        "16348": {"comment":"No shift: done"},
        "16350": {"comment":"Shifted: the inverse block graphic"},
        "16353": {"synopsis":"K, L or C mode digits: the digit itself, the table at $2264 with caps shift, or the symbol\nwith symbol shift.","comment":"K, L or C mode: no shift keeps the digit"},
        "16355": {"comment":"Caps shift (bit 5 set)?"},
        "16357": {"comment":"HL = $2264 for the caps-shifted digits"},
        "16362": {"comment":"Symbol shift: '1' gives '!', '3' '#' and so on"},
        "16364": {"comment":"'2'?"},
        "16368": {"comment":"'0'?"},
        "16371": {"comment":"'0' gives '_'"},
        "16374": {"synopsis":"Symbol shift and '2': '@'.","comment":"'2' gives '@'"},
        "16377": {"synopsis":"Unused: $FF up to the last byte."}
      }
    }
  },
